ooperate.\nCells crudley combine when they communicate.\n\nCounterfeit co-sign. My credit's catastrophic.\nI'd counter with a check but I'm too cozy with a cartridge\n\nWe crave the cosmic - space screensavers in cubicles.\nCited collateral can chew down to your cuticles.\n\nCaught, cornered, caged, and casually confined.\nA concept for cartoons where cans and calves combine.\n\nIn closing, cable's dead so why channel companions\nwhen the crucifix canon is consistently candid?\n\n[drinking outta cups]\nEverybody sucks. I'm my own favorite rapper.\nBump my own rhymes while I'm sitting on the crapper.\n\nThe cracker, the slacker, the div-slinging hacker.\nRhyming in circles like a rap protractor.\n\nAbstractor. Hiding what he's after.\nGot the Midas touch but there's no X-Factor.\n\nRhyme extracter. Finds, refactors.\nAlways reads ahead to the next 2 chapters.\n\nI'm in a sea-hell drinking outta cups.\nWriting down punchlines, thinking up puns.\n\nThe kid isn't evil. I think that he's nuts.\nHe's writing so emo and crying too much.\n\nAlways revealing his feelings and healing by dealing this villainous venom he's spitting.\nKilling his demons and serving his beats like croissants that you drop when you see the precision.\n\nThe sentence enhancers he throws in his rhymes are the reason you listen so fuck your opinion.\nThe kitchen is closed and the genie Is hoping 3 wishes will fix it but it's your decision.\n\nSpongeBob is screaming at night and we're meme-ing and being a typical atypical.\nLooking for meaning. Believe me, there's meaning. Not just trying to fit these rhyme syllables\n\n...but admittedly, that's most of it.\n\n[you call this mercy?]\nDoes he do it for the lulz, the antics, and the anecdotes?\nAnesthesia served with an anti-antidote.\n\nEuthanize, murder, self-defense, or a white lie?\nSuffocating softly in a glass room; no light.\n\nTemperatures boil and temperaments soiled.\nMauled jowls and howls. To the victims go spoils.\n\nPrincess bed, a stretcher, and fear in the cat's eyes\nbut do the consequences even fit the crime?\n\nBloodstained remnants, ripped garments, and stitches.\nIncisive delusions, injections, incisions.\n\nThe matrix is glitching, he played God with decisions.\nLast words, the predicate of the death sentence.\n\nVicious vermin or precious Persians,\nShepherds, rats. A cathode burn-in.\n\nTrue atrocities or just another Tuesday?\nWhy don't we ask and see what the wounds say?\n\nInstincts kicked in, it's just the hex of the species\nbut those puppy dog eyes don't make this so easy.\n\nHe wrote her a note, it read \"Best wishes.\nGood night, sweetie.\", sealed with bunny kisses.\n\n\n\n[florence]\nBlue candle wax drips onto bolded yellow letters.\nA fiber inbound from a cashmere sweater.\n\nBut the focus of the moths are on the butane flames.\nYou can really see their beauty between each keyframe.\n\nA wrinkled map of veins much thinner than my college thesis.\nI didn't go to school but I'm barely facetious.\n\nNow picture frames are smashed as well as all the glassware.\nSpaghetti code-words for confetti-covered nightmares.\n\nDancing in the sprinkler of a manicured lawn.\nIce-cream water and the yodeling of songs.\n\nTea-leaves excrete love inside of stainless steel.\nIt might have lost its shine but it still feels real.\n\nImmobile meals for mailmen to bring to all the locals.\nPecan pie on both sides of bifocals.\n\nShe spoke her mind even if it was ugly\nbut she'd rather die than let anyone go hungry.\n\n\n\n[let's take it apart and put it back together]\nCobwebs behind your eyes, reverb between your ears.\nAn empty space for thinking and for facing all your fears.\n\nA little dusty but there's a broom and a rug.\nThe glass on the floor explains all the blood.\n\nObfuscated reminiscing, scared of what's to come.\nBarely coughed the words out with smoke in his lungs.\n\nThere's a swing set in the corner behind the rollercoaster.\nTo get a better view, just move the serotonin over.\n\nAnti-this, anti-that. He's psychotic as it is.\nFeel-good and do-little are his only friends.\n\nResting in isolation while coveting peace.\nSpiders on the ceiling that crawl into your dreams.\n\nIt's dim but you can still read all the files in the cabinets.\nPick a drawer, any drawer. They're all filled with accidents.\n\nTime capsules capturing classical hopes.\nAre you disappointed yet? There's a flash sale on rope.\n\nDeja vu's moving in so get used to his habits.\nHe'll always remind you not to rest on the Sabbath.\n\nLet's hope you re-adjust so you'll stop laughing with a frown.\nGet out of bed and pick it up. I promise that you're better now.\n\n\n\n\"\"\";\n",
  "lib/pages/music/music_page.dart": "import 'package:archbtw_sh/pages/music/album_grid_item.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/pages/music/album_item_list.dart';\nimport 'package:flutter/material.dart';\n\nclass MusicPage extends StatelessWidget {\n  const MusicPage({super.key});\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    return Scaffold(\n      body: GridView.builder(\n        padding: const EdgeInsets.all(16.0),\n        gridDelegate: const SliverGridDelegateWithMaxCrossAxisExtent(\n          maxCrossAxisExtent: 250.0,\n          crossAxisSpacing: 16.0,\n          mainAxisSpacing: 16.0,\n          childAspectRatio: 0.80,\n        ),\n        itemCount: albumItems.length,\n        itemBuilder: (context, index) {\n          return AlbumGridItem(item: albumItems[index]);\n        },\n      ),\n    );\n  }\n}\n",
  "lib/pages/music/music_player.dart": "import 'dart:async';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/global/colors.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/global/site_music_controller.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/widgets/marquee_text.dart';\nimport 'package:flutter/material.dart';\n\nclass MusicPlayer extends StatefulWidget {\n  final String albumTitle;\n  final List<String> tracks;\n  final String audioPath;\n  final bool isDesktop;\n\n  const MusicPlayer({\n    super.key,\n    this.albumTitle = '',\n    required this.tracks,\n    required this.audioPath,\n    this.isDesktop = true,\n  });\n\n  @override\n  State<MusicPlayer> createState() => _MusicPlayerState();\n}\n\nclass _MusicPlayerState extends State<MusicPlayer> {\n  final SiteMusicController _controller = SiteMusicController.instance;\n  int _localTrackIndex = 0;\n  double? _dragValueMs;\n\n  bool get _isThisAlbumActive => _controller.isAlbumLoaded(widget.audioPath);\n\n  int get _currentTrackIndex => _isThisAlbumActive\n      ? _controller.currentTrackIndex.clamp(0, widget.tracks.length - 1)\n      : _localTrackIndex.clamp(0, widget.tracks.length - 1);\n\n  bool get _isPlaying => _isThisAlbumActive && _controller.isPlaying;\n\n  Duration get _position =>\n      _isThisAlbumActive ? _controller.position : Duration.zero;\n\n  Duration get _duration =>\n      _isThisAlbumActive ? _controller.duration : Duration.zero;\n\n  @override\n  void initState() {\n    super.initState();\n    _controller.registerVisibleAlbum(widget.audioPath);\n    _controller.addListener(_onControllerChanged);\n  }\n\n  @override\n  void didUpdateWidget(covariant MusicPlayer oldWidget) {\n    super.didUpdateWidget(oldWidget);\n    if (oldWidget.audioPath != widget.audioPath) {\n      _controller.unregisterVisibleAlbum(oldWidget.audioPath);\n      _controller.registerVisibleAlbum(widget.audioPath);\n    }\n  }\n\n  @override\n  void dispose() {\n    _controller.removeListener(_onControllerChanged);\n    _controller.unregisterVisibleAlbum(widget.audioPath);\n    super.dispose();\n  }\n\n  void _onControllerChanged() {\n    if (mounted) {\n      setState(() {});\n    }\n  }\n\n  Future<void> _playPause() async {\n    await _controller.togglePlayPause(\n      albumTitle: widget.albumTitle,\n      audioPath: widget.audioPath,\n      tracks: widget.tracks,\n      selectedIndex: _localTrackIndex,\n    );\n  }\n\n  Future<void> _playTrackAt(int index) async {\n    setState(() {\n      _localTrackIndex = index;\n    });\n    await _controller.playAlbumTrack(\n      albumTitle: widget.albumTitle,\n      audioPath: widget.audioPath,\n      tracks: widget.tracks,\n      trackIndex: index,\n    );\n  }\n\n  Future<void> _next() async {\n    final nextIdx = (_currentTrackIndex + 1) % widget.tracks.length;\n    await _playTrackAt(nextIdx);\n  }\n\n  Future<void> _previous() async {\n    final prevIdx =\n        (_currentTrackIndex - 1 + widget.tracks.length) % widget.tracks.length;\n    await _playTrackAt(prevIdx);\n  }\n\n  String _formatDuration(Duration duration) {\n    String twoDigits(int n) => n.toString().padLeft(2, \"0\");\n    String twoDigitMinutes = twoDigits(duration.inMinutes.remainder(60));\n    String twoDigitSeconds = twoDigits(duration.inSeconds.remainder(60));\n    return \"\$twoDigitMinutes:\$twoDigitSeconds\";\n  }\n\n  String _cleanTrackName(String name) {\n    return name.replaceAll('.wav', '').replaceAll('.m4a', '');\n  }\n\n  Widget _buildTextButton(\n    String label,\n    VoidCallback onTap, {\n    bool isPrimary = false,\n  }) {\n    return InkWell(\n      onTap: onTap,\n      borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(4),\n      child: Padding(\n        padding: const EdgeInsets.symmetric(horizontal: 8.0, vertical: 4.0),\n        child: Text(\n          label,\n          style: TextStyle(\n            color: Colors.white70,\n            fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n            fontSize: 13,\n            fontWeight: isPrimary ? FontWeight.bold : FontWeight.normal,\n          ),\n        ),\n      ),\n    );\n  }\n\n  Widget _buildTerminalHeader(Color accentColor) {\n    return Row(\n      children: [\n        Text(\n          '~ > ',\n          style: TextStyle(\n            color: accentColor,\n            fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n            fontSize: 14,\n            fontWeight: FontWeight.bold,\n          ),\n        ),\n        Expanded(\n          child: MarqueeText(\n            text:\n                './\${_cleanTrackName(widget.tracks[_currentTrackIndex]).replaceAll(' ', '_')}.sh',\n            style: const TextStyle(\n              color: Colors.white,\n              fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n              fontSize: 14,\n            ),\n          ),\n        ),\n      ],\n    );\n  }\n\n  Widget _buildControlsRow(Color accentColor) {\n    final double maxMs = _duration.inMilliseconds.toDouble() > 0\n        ? _duration.inMilliseconds.toDouble()\n        : 1.0;\n    final double effectivePosMs =\n        (_dragValueMs ?? _position.inMilliseconds.toDouble()).clamp(0.0, maxMs);\n    final Duration displayedPosition = _dragValueMs != null\n        ? Duration(milliseconds: _dragValueMs!.toInt())\n        : _position;\n\n    return Column(\n      crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.stretch,\n      children: [\n        Wrap(\n          alignment: WrapAlignment.spaceBetween,\n          crossAxisAlignment: WrapCrossAlignment.center,\n          spacing: 8,\n          runSpacing: 8,\n          children: [\n            Row(\n              mainAxisSize: MainAxisSize.min,\n              children: [\n                _buildTextButton(\n                  _isPlaying ? '[ PAUSE ]' : '[ PLAY ]',\n                  _playPause,\n                  isPrimary: true,\n                ),\n                const SizedBox(width: 4),\n                _buildTextButton('[ BACK ]', _previous),\n                const SizedBox(width: 4),\n                _buildTextButton('[ NEXT ]', _next),\n              ],\n            ),\n            Padding(\n              padding: const EdgeInsets.symmetric(horizontal: 4.0),\n              child: Text(\n                '\${_formatDuration(displayedPosition)} / \${_formatDuration(_duration)}',\n                style: TextStyle(\n                  color: Colors.white.withValues(alpha: 0.7),\n                  fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                  fontSize: 12,\n                ),\n              ),\n            ),\n          ],\n        ),\n        const SizedBox(height: 10),\n        SliderTheme(\n          data: SliderThemeData(\n            trackHeight: 2,\n            activeTrackColor: accentColor,\n            inactiveTrackColor: Colors.white.withValues(alpha: 0.16),\n            thumbColor: accentColor,\n            thumbShape: const RoundSliderThumbShape(enabledThumbRadius: 5),\n            overlayShape: const RoundSliderOverlayShape(overlayRadius: 12),\n            trackShape: const RectangularSliderTrackShape(),\n          ),\n          child: Slider(\n            key: const Key('audio_scrubber'),\n            value: effectivePosMs,\n            max: maxMs,\n            onChangeStart: (value) {\n              if (_isThisAlbumActive) {\n                setState(() {\n                  _dragValueMs = value;\n                });\n              }\n            },\n            onChanged: (value) {\n              if (_isThisAlbumActive) {\n                setState(() {\n                  _dragValueMs = value;\n                });\n                _controller.seek(Duration(milliseconds: value.toInt()));\n              }\n            },\n            onChangeEnd: (value) {\n              if (_isThisAlbumActive) {\n                setState(() {\n                  _dragValueMs = null;\n                });\n                _controller.seek(Duration(milliseconds: value.toInt()));\n              }\n            },\n          ),\n        ),\n      ],\n    );\n  }\n\n  Widget _buildTracklist(Color accentColor) {\n    return Column(\n      crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.start,\n      children: [\n        Text(\n          '// AVAILABLE_TRACKS',\n          style: TextStyle(\n            color: Colors.white.withValues(alpha: 0.3),\n            fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n            fontSize: 11,\n            fontWeight: FontWeight.bold,\n            letterSpacing: 1.1,\n          ),\n        ),\n        const SizedBox(height: 12),\n        ...widget.tracks.asMap().entries.map((entry) {\n          final int index = entry.key;\n          final String track = entry.value;\n          final bool isCurrent = index == _currentTrackIndex;\n\n          return InkWell(\n            onTap: () => _playTrackAt(index),\n            hoverColor: accentColor.withValues(alpha: 0.05),\n            child: Padding(\n              padding: const EdgeInsets.symmetric(\n                vertical: 6.0,\n                horizontal: 4.0,\n              ),\n              child: Row(\n                children: [\n                  SizedBox(\n                    width: 24,\n                    child: Text(\n                      isCurrent ? '->' : '  ',\n                      style: TextStyle(\n                        color: accentColor,\n                        fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                        fontWeight: FontWeight.bold,\n                      ),\n                    ),\n                  ),\n                  Flexible(\n                    child: isCurrent\n                        ? MarqueeText(\n                            text: _cleanTrackName(track).toLowerCase(),\n                            style: TextStyle(\n                              color: accentColor,\n                              fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                              fontSize: 13,\n                            ),\n                          )\n                        : Text(\n                            _cleanTrackName(track).toLowerCase(),\n                            style: TextStyle(\n                              color: Colors.white.withValues(alpha: 0.7),\n                              fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                              fontSize: 13,\n                            ),\n                            overflow: TextOverflow.ellipsis,\n                          ),\n                  ),\n                  if (isCurrent && _isPlaying) ...[\n                    const SizedBox(width: 12),\n                    _buildPlayingIndicator(accentColor),\n                  ],\n                ],\n              ),\n            ),\n          );\n        }),\n      ],\n    );\n  }\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    final Color accentColor = kAccentColor;\n\n    return Container(\n      margin: const EdgeInsets.symmetric(vertical: 24),\n      child: Column(\n        crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.start,\n        children: [\n          _buildTerminalHeader(accentColor),\n          const SizedBox(height: 16),\n          _buildControlsRow(accentColor),\n          const SizedBox(height: 32),\n          _buildTracklist(accentColor),\n        ],\n      ),\n    );\n  }\n\n  Widget _buildPlayingIndicator(Color color) {\n    return SizedBox(\n      height: 10,\n      width: 12,\n      child: Row(\n        mainAxisAlignment: MainAxisAlignment.spaceBetween,\n        children: List.generate(\n          3,\n          (i) => _PlayingBar(color: color, delay: i * 200),\n        ),\n      ),\n    );\n  }\n}\n\nclass _PlayingBar extends StatefulWidget {\n  final Color color;\n  final int delay;\n  const _PlayingBar({required this.color, required this.delay});\n\n  @override\n  State<_PlayingBar> createState() => _PlayingBarState();\n}\n\nclass _PlayingBarState extends State<_PlayingBar>\n    with SingleTickerProviderStateMixin {\n  late AnimationController _controller;\n\n  @override\n  void initState() {\n    super.initState();\n    _controller = AnimationController(\n      vsync: this,\n      duration: const Duration(milliseconds: 600),\n    );\n    Future.delayed(Duration(milliseconds: widget.delay), () {\n      if (mounted) _controller.repeat(reverse: true);\n    });\n  }\n\n  @override\n  void dispose() {\n    _controller.dispose();\n    super.dispose();\n  }\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    return AnimatedBuilder(\n      animation: _controller,\n      builder: (context, child) {\n        return Container(\n          width: 2,\n          height: 3 + (7 * _controller.value),\n          color: widget.color,\n        );\n      },\n    );\n  }\n}\n",
  "lib/pages/music/album_art.dart": "import 'package:archbtw_sh/pages/music/album_item.dart';\nimport 'package:flutter/material.dart';\n\nclass AlbumArt extends StatelessWidget {\n  final AlbumItem item;\n  const AlbumArt({super.key, required this.item});\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    return Padding(\n      padding: const EdgeInsets.all(16.0),\n      child: Center(\n        child: ConstrainedBox(\n          constraints: const BoxConstraints(maxWidth: 480.0, maxHeight: 480.0),\n          child: AspectRatio(\n            aspectRatio: 1.0,\n            child: Hero(\n              tag: item.coverUrl,\n              createRectTween: (begin, end) =>\n                  MaterialRectArcTween(begin: begin, end: end),\n              child: ClipRRect(\n                borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(12.0),\n                child: Stack(\n                  fit: StackFit.expand,\n                  alignment: Alignment.center,\n                  children: [\n                    Image.asset(item.coverUrl, fit: BoxFit.cover),\n                    if (item.isLocked) ...[\n                      Positioned.fill(\n                        child: Container(\n                          color: Colors.black.withValues(alpha: 0.35),\n                        ),\n                      ),\n                      Center(\n                        child: Container(\n                          padding: const EdgeInsets.all(16),\n                          decoration: BoxDecoration(\n                            color: Colors.black.withValues(alpha: 0.7),\n                            shape: BoxShape.circle,\n                            border: Border.all(\n                              color: Colors.white24,\n                              width: 1.5,\n                            ),\n                          ),\n                          child: const Icon(\n                            Icons.lock_outline,\n                            color: Colors.white,\n                            size: 36,\n                          ),\n                        ),\n                      ),\n                    ],\n                  ],\n                ),\n              ),\n            ),\n          ),\n        ),\n      ),\n    );\n  }\n}\n",
  "lib/pages/music/album_detail_page.dart": "import 'package:archbtw_sh/global/colors.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/pages/music/album_art.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/pages/music/album_details.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/pages/music/album_item.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/pages/music/annotated_lyrics_section.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/widgets/holiday_snow_overlay.dart';\nimport 'package:flutter/material.dart';\n\nclass AlbumDetailPage extends StatefulWidget {\n  final AlbumItem item;\n  const AlbumDetailPage({super.key, required this.item});\n\n  @override\n  State<AlbumDetailPage> createState() => _AlbumDetailPageState();\n}\n\nclass _AlbumDetailPageState extends State<AlbumDetailPage> {\n  bool _isLyricsExpanded = false;\n\n  void _toggleLyrics() {\n    setState(() {\n      _isLyricsExpanded = !_isLyricsExpanded;\n    });\n  }\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    return Scaffold(\n      backgroundColor: kBackgroundColor,\n      appBar: AppBar(\n        backgroundColor: Colors.transparent,\n        elevation: 0,\n        leading: const BackButton(color: kTextColor),\n      ),\n      body: Stack(\n        children: [\n          Positioned.fill(\n            child: RepaintBoundary(\n              child: SingleChildScrollView(\n                child: Center(\n                  child: ConstrainedBox(\n                    constraints: const BoxConstraints(maxWidth: 1200.0),\n                    child: LayoutBuilder(\n                      builder: (context, constraints) {\n                        final bool isDesktop = constraints.maxWidth > 800.0;\n\n                        final albumArt = AlbumArt(item: widget.item);\n\n                        if (isDesktop) {\n                          return Padding(\n                            padding: const EdgeInsets.all(32.0),\n                            child: Column(\n                              children: [\n                                Row(\n                                  crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.start,\n                                  children: [\n                                    Expanded(\n                                      flex: 2,\n                                      child: Column(\n                                        children: [\n                                          albumArt,\n                                          AlbumDetails(\n                                            item: widget.item,\n                                            isDesktop: isDesktop,\n                                            showTitle: true,\n                                            showPlayer: false,\n                                            showLyricsButton: false,\n                                            showLyricsContent: false,\n                                          ),\n                                        ],\n                                      ),\n                                    ),\n                                    const SizedBox(width: 32.0),\n                                    Expanded(\n                                      flex: 3,\n                                      child: AlbumDetails(\n                                        item: widget.item,\n                                        isDesktop: isDesktop,\n                                        showTitle: false,\n                                        showPlayer: true,\n                                        showLyricsButton: true,\n                                        showLyricsContent: false,\n                                        isLyricsExpanded: _isLyricsExpanded,\n                                        onToggleLyrics: _toggleLyrics,\n                                      ),\n                                    ),\n                                  ],\n                                ),\n                                if (_isLyricsExpanded &&\n                                    !widget.item.isLocked &&\n                                    widget.item.lyrics.isNotEmpty) ...[\n                                  const SizedBox(height: 24),\n                                  Divider(\n                                    color: kAccentColor.withValues(alpha: 0.2),\n                                    height: 1,\n                                  ),\n                                  const SizedBox(height: 24),\n                                  AnnotatedLyricsSection(\n                                    item: widget.item,\n                                    isDesktop: true,\n                                  ),\n                                ],\n                              ],\n                            ),\n                          );\n                        } else {\n                          return Column(\n                            crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.stretch,\n                            children: [\n                              albumArt,\n                              AlbumDetails(\n                                item: widget.item,\n                                isDesktop: isDesktop,\n                                showTitle: true,\n                                showPlayer: true,\n                                showLyricsButton: true,\n                                showLyricsContent: true,\n                                isLyricsExpanded: _isLyricsExpanded,\n                                onToggleLyrics: _toggleLyrics,\n                              ),\n                            ],\n                          );\n                        }\n                      },\n                    ),\n                  ),\n                ),\n              ),\n            ),\n          ),\n          const Positioned.fill(child: HolidaySnowOverlay()),\n        ],\n      ),\n    );\n  }\n}\n",
  "lib/pages/music/album_details.dart": "import 'package:archbtw_sh/games/blubber_game.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/pages/music/annotated_lyrics_section.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/pages/music/music_player.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/games/lemon_game.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/games/santa_game.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/global/colors.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/pages/music/album_item.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/pages/overheat/overheat_page.dart';\nimport 'package:flutter/material.dart';\nimport 'package:font_awesome_flutter/font_awesome_flutter.dart';\n\nclass AlbumDetails extends StatefulWidget {\n  final AlbumItem item;\n  final bool isDesktop;\n  final bool showTitle;\n  final bool showPlayer;\n  final bool showLyricsButton;\n  final bool showLyricsContent;\n  final bool? isLyricsExpanded;\n  final VoidCallback? onToggleLyrics;\n\n  const AlbumDetails({\n    super.key,\n    required this.item,\n    required this.isDesktop,\n    this.showTitle = true,\n    this.showPlayer = true,\n    this.showLyricsButton = false,\n    this.showLyricsContent = true,\n    this.isLyricsExpanded,\n    this.onToggleLyrics,\n  });\n\n  @override\n  State<AlbumDetails> createState() => _AlbumDetailsState();\n}\n\nclass _AlbumDetailsState extends State<AlbumDetails> {\n  bool _internalExpanded = false;\n\n  bool get _isExpanded => widget.isLyricsExpanded ?? _internalExpanded;\n\n  void _handleToggle() {\n    if (widget.onToggleLyrics != null) {\n      widget.onToggleLyrics!();\n    } else {\n      setState(() {\n        _internalExpanded = !_internalExpanded;\n      });\n    }\n  }\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    final double iconSize = widget.isDesktop ? 22 : 18;\n\n    return Column(\n      crossAxisAlignment: widget.isDesktop && widget.showTitle\n          ? CrossAxisAlignment.center\n          : CrossAxisAlignment.start,\n      children: [\n        if (widget.showTitle)\n          Padding(\n            padding: const EdgeInsets.symmetric(horizontal: 16.0, vertical: 12),\n            child: Wrap(\n              alignment: widget.isDesktop\n                  ? WrapAlignment.center\n                  : WrapAlignment.spaceBetween,\n              crossAxisAlignment: WrapCrossAlignment.center,\n              spacing: 14,\n              runSpacing: 10,\n              children: [\n                Text(\n                  widget.item.title,\n                  style: TextStyle(\n                    color: kTextColor,\n                    fontWeight: FontWeight.bold,\n                    fontSize: 24,\n                    fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                  ),\n                ),\n                if (widget.item.isLocked) ...[\n                  IconButton(\n                    tooltip: \"launch_protocol: overheat\",\n                    icon: FaIcon(\n                      FontAwesomeIcons.fire,\n                      color: const Color(0xFFFF6F00),\n                      size: iconSize,\n                    ),\n                    onPressed: () {\n                      Navigator.of(context).push(\n                        PageRouteBuilder(\n                          opaque: false,\n                          pageBuilder: (context, anim, secAnim) =>\n                              const OverheatPage(),\n                          transitionsBuilder: (context, anim, secAnim, child) {\n                            return FadeTransition(opacity: anim, child: child);\n                          },\n                        ),\n                      );\n                    },\n                  ),\n                ] else if (widget.item.title.toLowerCase() == 'blubber' ||\n                    widget.item.title.toLowerCase() == 'santa\\'s cookies' ||\n                    widget.item.title.toLowerCase() == 'life\\'s lemons') ...[\n                  Tooltip(\n                    message: _getTooltipForAlbum(widget.item.title),\n                    child: ElevatedButton.icon(\n                      key: const Key('launch_game_button'),\n                      style: ElevatedButton.styleFrom(\n                        backgroundColor: kAccentColor.withValues(alpha: 0.16),\n                        foregroundColor: kAccentColor,\n                        elevation: 0,\n                        padding: const EdgeInsets.symmetric(\n                          horizontal: 14,\n                          vertical: 10,\n                        ),\n                        side: const BorderSide(color: kAccentColor, width: 1.6),\n                        shape: RoundedRectangleBorder(\n                          borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(8),\n                        ),\n                      ),\n                      icon: const Icon(\n                        Icons.sports_esports,\n                        color: kAccentColor,\n                        size: 18,\n                      ),\n                      label: Text(\n                        _getGameLabelForAlbum(widget.item.title),\n                        style: const TextStyle(\n                          color: Colors.white,\n                          fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                          fontWeight: FontWeight.bold,\n                          fontSize: 12,\n                          letterSpacing: 0.8,\n                        ),\n                      ),\n                      onPressed: () {\n                        Widget gamePage;\n                        final title = widget.item.title.toLowerCase();\n\n                        if (title == 'blubber') {\n                          gamePage = const WhaleGame();\n                        } else if (title == 'santa\\'s cookies') {\n                          gamePage = const SantasInvadersGame();\n                        } else {\n                          gamePage = const LemonsGame();\n                        }\n\n                        Navigator.of(context).push(\n                          PageRouteBuilder(\n                            pageBuilder: (context, anim, secAnim) => gamePage,\n                            transitionsBuilder:\n                                (context, anim, secAnim, child) {\n                                  return FadeTransition(\n                                    opacity: anim,\n                                    child: child,\n                                  );\n                                },\n                          ),\n                        );\n                      },\n                    ),\n                  ),\n                ],\n              ],\n            ),\n          ),\n        if (widget.item.isLocked && (widget.showPlayer || !widget.isDesktop))\n          Padding(\n            padding: const EdgeInsets.symmetric(horizontal: 16.0, vertical: 8),\n            child: Container(\n              padding: const EdgeInsets.all(20),\n              decoration: BoxDecoration(\n                border: Border.all(color: Colors.white24),\n                color: Colors.white.withValues(alpha: 0.04),\n                borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(8),\n              ),\n              child: const Column(\n                crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.start,\n                children: [\n                  Text(\n                    \"your order is in the oven.\",\n                    style: TextStyle(\n                      color: kTextColor,\n                      fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                      fontSize: 14,\n                      height: 1.5,\n                    ),\n                  ),\n                  SizedBox(height: 4),\n                  Text(\n                    \"estimated delivery time: march 2027\",\n                    style: TextStyle(\n                      color: Colors.white70,\n                      fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                      fontSize: 13,\n                      letterSpacing: 1.1,\n                    ),\n                  ),\n                ],\n              ),\n            ),\n          ),\n        if (widget.showPlayer && widget.item.tracks.isNotEmpty)\n          Padding(\n            padding: const EdgeInsets.symmetric(horizontal: 16.0),\n            child: MusicPlayer(\n              albumTitle: widget.item.title,\n              tracks: widget.item.tracks,\n              audioPath: widget.item.audioPath,\n              isDesktop: widget.isDesktop,\n            ),\n          ),\n        if (widget.showLyricsButton &&\n            !widget.item.isLocked &&\n            widget.item.lyrics.isNotEmpty)\n          Padding(\n            padding: const EdgeInsets.symmetric(horizontal: 16.0),\n            child: Row(\n              mainAxisAlignment: MainAxisAlignment.start,\n              children: [\n                TextButton.icon(\n                  onPressed: _handleToggle,\n                  icon: Icon(\n                    _isExpanded ? Icons.expand_less : Icons.expand_more,\n                    color: kAccentColor,\n                  ),\n                  label: Text(\n                    _isExpanded ? \"lyrics.collapse();\" : \"lyrics.expand();\",\n                    style: TextStyle(\n                      color: kAccentColor,\n                      fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                      fontWeight: FontWeight.bold,\n                      letterSpacing: 1.2,\n                    ),\n                  ),\n                ),\n              ],\n            ),\n          ),\n        if (widget.showLyricsContent &&\n            _isExpanded &&\n            !widget.item.isLocked &&\n            widget.item.lyrics.isNotEmpty)\n          Padding(\n            padding: const EdgeInsets.all(16.0),\n            child: AnnotatedLyricsSection(\n              item: widget.item,\n              isDesktop: widget.isDesktop,\n            ),\n          ),\n      ],\n    );\n  }\n}\n\nString _getTooltipForAlbum(String title) {\n  final t = title.toLowerCase();\n  if (t == 'blubber') return \"launch_protocol: gravity\";\n  if (t == 'santa\\'s cookies') return \"launch_protocol: chimney\";\n  return \"launch_protocol: gnu/linux\";\n}\n\nString _getGameLabelForAlbum(String title) {\n  final t = title.toLowerCase();\n  if (t == 'blubber') return \"PLAY: floppy_whale.sh\";\n  if (t == 'santa\\'s cookies') return \"PLAY: rudolph_spoke.sh\";\n  return \"PLAY: lifes_lemons.sh\";\n}\n",
  "lib/pages/music/album_grid_item.dart": "import 'package:archbtw_sh/global/colors.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/pages/music/album_detail_page.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/pages/music/album_item.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/widgets/loading_waveform.dart';\nimport 'package:flutter/material.dart';\n\nclass AlbumGridItem extends StatelessWidget {\n  final AlbumItem item;\n  const AlbumGridItem({super.key, required this.item});\n\n  Widget _flightShuttleBuilder(\n    BuildContext flightContext,\n    Animation<double> animation,\n    HeroFlightDirection flightDirection,\n    BuildContext fromHeroContext,\n    BuildContext toHeroContext,\n  ) {\n    final curvedAnimation = CurvedAnimation(\n      parent: animation,\n      curve: Curves.easeOutCubic,\n      reverseCurve: Curves.easeInCubic,\n    );\n\n    return AnimatedBuilder(\n      animation: curvedAnimation,\n      builder: (context, child) {\n        return Material(\n          type: MaterialType.transparency,\n          child: ClipRRect(\n            borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(12.0),\n            child: Stack(\n              fit: StackFit.expand,\n              alignment: Alignment.center,\n              children: [\n                Image.asset(item.coverUrl, fit: BoxFit.cover),\n                if (item.isLocked) ...[\n                  Container(color: Colors.black.withValues(alpha: 0.45)),\n                  Center(\n                    child: Container(\n                      padding: const EdgeInsets.all(14),\n                      decoration: BoxDecoration(\n                        color: Colors.black.withValues(alpha: 0.65),\n                        shape: BoxShape.circle,\n                        border: Border.all(color: Colors.white24, width: 1.5),\n                      ),\n                      child: const Icon(\n                        Icons.lock_outline,\n                        color: Colors.white,\n                        size: 30,\n                      ),\n                    ),\n                  ),\n                ],\n              ],\n            ),\n          ),\n        );\n      },\n    );\n  }\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    return InkWell(\n      onTap: () {\n        Navigator.push(\n          context,\n          PageRouteBuilder(\n            transitionDuration: const Duration(milliseconds: 380),\n            reverseTransitionDuration: const Duration(milliseconds: 300),\n            pageBuilder: (context, animation, secondaryAnimation) {\n              return AlbumDetailPage(item: item);\n            },\n            transitionsBuilder:\n                (context, animation, secondaryAnimation, child) {\n                  final curved = CurvedAnimation(\n                    parent: animation,\n                    curve: Curves.easeOutCubic,\n                    reverseCurve: Curves.easeInCubic,\n                  );\n                  return FadeTransition(opacity: curved, child: child);\n                },\n          ),\n        );\n      },\n      borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(12.0),\n      child: Card(\n        color: Colors.white.withValues(alpha: 0.05),\n        elevation: 0,\n        clipBehavior: Clip.antiAlias,\n        shape: RoundedRectangleBorder(\n          side: BorderSide(\n            color: Colors.white.withValues(alpha: 0.1),\n            width: 1,\n          ),\n          borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(12.0),\n        ),\n        child: Column(\n          crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.stretch,\n          children: [\n            Expanded(\n              child: Hero(\n                tag: item.coverUrl,\n                createRectTween: (begin, end) =>\n                    MaterialRectArcTween(begin: begin, end: end),\n                flightShuttleBuilder: _flightShuttleBuilder,\n                child: ClipRRect(\n                  borderRadius: const BorderRadius.vertical(\n                    top: Radius.circular(12.0),\n                  ),\n                  child: Stack(\n                    fit: StackFit.expand,\n                    children: [\n                      Image.asset(\n                        item.coverUrl,\n                        fit: BoxFit.cover,\n                        frameBuilder:\n                            (context, child, frame, wasSynchronouslyLoaded) {\n                              if (wasSynchronouslyLoaded || frame != null) {\n                                return child;\n                              }\n                              return Container(\n                                color: Colors.white.withValues(alpha: 0.02),\n                                child: const Center(\n                                  child: WaveformLoader(\n                                    height: 25,\n                                    barWidth: 3,\n                                  ),\n                                ),\n                              );\n                            },\n                        errorBuilder: (context, error, stackTrace) {\n                          return Container(\n                            color: Colors.grey[800],\n                            child: const Center(\n                              child: Icon(\n                                Icons.album_outlined,\n                                color: kTextColor,\n                                size: 50,\n                              ),\n                            ),\n                          );\n                        },\n                      ),\n                      if (item.isLocked) ...[\n                        Container(color: Colors.black.withValues(alpha: 0.45)),\n                        Center(\n                          child: Container(\n                            padding: const EdgeInsets.all(12),\n                            decoration: BoxDecoration(\n                              color: Colors.black.withValues(alpha: 0.65),\n                              shape: BoxShape.circle,\n                              border: Border.all(\n                                color: Colors.white24,\n                                width: 1.5,\n                              ),\n                            ),\n                            child: const Icon(\n                              Icons.lock_outline,\n                              color: Colors.white,\n                              size: 26,\n                            ),\n                          ),\n                        ),\n                      ],\n                    ],\n                  ),\n                ),\n              ),\n            ),\n            SizedBox(\n              height: 75.0,\n              child: Padding(\n                padding: const EdgeInsets.all(12.0),\n                child: Column(\n                  crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.start,\n                  mainAxisAlignment: MainAxisAlignment.center,\n                  children: [\n                    Row(\n                      children: [\n                        Expanded(\n                          child: Text(\n                            item.title,\n                            style: const TextStyle(\n                              color: kTextColor,\n                              fontWeight: FontWeight.bold,\n                              fontSize: 14,\n                              fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                            ),\n                            maxLines: 1,\n                            overflow: TextOverflow.ellipsis,\n                          ),\n                        ),\n                        if (item.isLocked)\n                          const Padding(\n                            padding: EdgeInsets.only(left: 4.0),\n                            child: Icon(\n                              Icons.lock_outline,\n                              size: 14,\n                              color: Colors.white54,\n                            ),\n                          ),\n                      ],\n                    ),\n                    if (item.isLocked) ...[\n                      const SizedBox(height: 4),\n                      const Text(\n                        'coming march 2027',\n                        style: TextStyle(\n                          color: Colors.white54,\n                          fontSize: 11,\n                          fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                        ),\n                      ),\n                    ],\n                  ],\n                ),\n              ),\n            ),\n          ],\n        ),\n      ),\n    );\n  }\n}\n",
  "lib/pages/music/album_item.dart": "class AlbumItem {\n  final String title;\n  final String coverUrl;\n  final String spotifyUrl;\n  final String appleMusicUrl;\n  final String soundCloudUrl;\n  final String youtubeUrl;\n  final bool soundCloudOnly;\n  final String lyrics;\n  final List<String> tracks;\n  final String audioPath;\n  final bool isLocked;\n\n  const AlbumItem({\n    required this.title,\n    required this.coverUrl,\n    required this.spotifyUrl,\n    required this.appleMusicUrl,\n    required this.soundCloudUrl,\n    required this.youtubeUrl,\n    required this.lyrics,\n    required this.soundCloudOnly,\n    required this.tracks,\n    required this.audioPath,\n    this.isLocked = false,\n  });\n}\n",
  "lib/pages/music/album_social_icon.dart": "import 'package:archbtw_sh/global/colors.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/global/helpers.dart';\nimport 'package:flutter/material.dart';\n\nclass AlbumSocialIcon extends StatelessWidget {\n  final IconData icon;\n  final String url;\n  final double size;\n\n  const AlbumSocialIcon({\n    super.key,\n    required this.icon,\n    required this.url,\n    this.size = 18.0,\n  });\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    return IconButton(\n      icon: Icon(icon, color: Colors.grey, size: size),\n      onPressed: () => openUrl(url),\n      splashColor: kAccentColor.withValues(alpha: 0.3),\n      hoverColor: kAccentColor.withValues(alpha: 0.1),\n    );\n  }\n}\n",
  "lib/pages/music/annotated_lyrics_section.dart": "import 'dart:math' as math;\n\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/global/colors.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/global/site_music_controller.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/pages/music/album_item.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/pages/music/lyric_annotations.dart';\nimport 'package:flutter/material.dart';\n\n/// Interactive Rap Genius-style lyrics viewer with per-track and per-line\n/// breakdowns tailored to the archBTW.sh terminal aesthetic.\nclass AnnotatedLyricsSection extends StatefulWidget {\n  final AlbumItem item;\n  final bool isDesktop;\n\n  const AnnotatedLyricsSection({\n    super.key,\n    required this.item,\n    required this.isDesktop,\n  });\n\n  @override\n  State<AnnotatedLyricsSection> createState() => _AnnotatedLyricsSectionState();\n}\n\nclass _AnnotatedLyricsSectionState extends State<AnnotatedLyricsSection> {\n  final SiteMusicController _musicController = SiteMusicController.instance;\n  final GlobalKey _lyricsColumnKey = GlobalKey();\n  final Map<int, GlobalKey> _itemKeys = {};\n\n  late ParsedAlbumLyrics _parsed;\n  int? _selectedItemIndex;\n  int? _hoveredItemIndex;\n  double _desktopCardTopOffset = 0.0;\n\n  @override\n  void initState() {\n    super.initState();\n    _parsed = parseAlbumLyrics(widget.item.lyrics);\n    _musicController.addListener(_onMusicChanged);\n  }\n\n  @override\n  void didUpdateWidget(covariant AnnotatedLyricsSection oldWidget) {\n    super.didUpdateWidget(oldWidget);\n    if (oldWidget.item.lyrics != widget.item.lyrics ||\n        oldWidget.item.title != widget.item.title) {\n      _parsed = parseAlbumLyrics(widget.item.lyrics);\n      _itemKeys.clear();\n      _selectedItemIndex = null;\n      _hoveredItemIndex = null;\n      _desktopCardTopOffset = 0.0;\n    } else if (oldWidget.isDesktop != widget.isDesktop &&\n        widget.isDesktop &&\n        _selectedItemIndex != null) {\n      WidgetsBinding.instance.addPostFrameCallback((_) {\n        _syncDesktopCardOffset();\n      });\n    }\n  }\n\n  @override\n  void dispose() {\n    _musicController.removeListener(_onMusicChanged);\n    super.dispose();\n  }\n\n  void _onMusicChanged() {\n    if (mounted) {\n      setState(() {});\n    }\n  }\n\n  GlobalKey _keyForItem(int index) {\n    return _itemKeys.putIfAbsent(index, () => GlobalKey());\n  }\n\n  int? get _playingTrackIndex {\n    if (!_musicController.isAlbumLoaded(widget.item.audioPath)) {\n      return null;\n    }\n    final idx = _musicController.currentTrackIndex;\n    if (idx < 0 || idx >= _parsed.tracks.length) return null;\n    return idx;\n  }\n\n  void _selectItem(\n    int index, {\n    bool toggleIfSelected = false,\n    bool scrollIntoView = false,\n  }) {\n    if (index < 0 || index >= _parsed.allItems.length) return;\n\n    if (toggleIfSelected && _selectedItemIndex == index) {\n      setState(() {\n        _selectedItemIndex = null;\n      });\n      return;\n    }\n\n    final int? previousIndex = _selectedItemIndex;\n    final bool shouldScroll =\n        scrollIntoView || (!widget.isDesktop && previousIndex != null);\n\n    setState(() {\n      _selectedItemIndex = index;\n    });\n\n    WidgetsBinding.instance.addPostFrameCallback((_) {\n      if (!mounted) return;\n      _syncDesktopCardOffset();\n      if (shouldScroll) {\n        final ctx = _itemKeys[index]?.currentContext;\n        if (ctx != null) {\n          Scrollable.ensureVisible(\n            ctx,\n            duration: const Duration(milliseconds: 220),\n            curve: Curves.easeOutCubic,\n            alignment: 0.18,\n          );\n        }\n      }\n    });\n  }\n\n  void _syncDesktopCardOffset() {\n    if (!mounted || !widget.isDesktop || _selectedItemIndex == null) return;\n\n    final columnBox =\n        _lyricsColumnKey.currentContext?.findRenderObject() as RenderBox?;\n    final itemBox = _itemKeys[_selectedItemIndex!]?.currentContext\n        ?.findRenderObject() as RenderBox?;\n\n    if (columnBox == null ||\n        itemBox == null ||\n        !columnBox.hasSize ||\n        !itemBox.hasSize) {\n      return;\n    }\n\n    final double itemTop = itemBox.localToGlobal(Offset.zero).dy;\n    final double columnTop = columnBox.localToGlobal(Offset.zero).dy;\n    final double rawOffset = itemTop - columnTop;\n    final double maxOffset = math.max(0.0, columnBox.size.height - 260.0);\n    final double clampedOffset = rawOffset.clamp(0.0, maxOffset);\n\n    if ((clampedOffset - _desktopCardTopOffset).abs() > 1.0) {\n      setState(() {\n        _desktopCardTopOffset = clampedOffset;\n      });\n    }\n  }\n\n  void _closeAnnotation() {\n    setState(() {\n      _selectedItemIndex = null;\n    });\n  }\n\n  void _stepSelection(int delta) {\n    if (_selectedItemIndex == null) return;\n    final next = _selectedItemIndex! + delta;\n    if (next < 0 || next >= _parsed.allItems.length) return;\n    _selectItem(next, scrollIntoView: true);\n  }\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    if (_parsed.tracks.isEmpty) {\n      return const SizedBox.shrink();\n    }\n\n    if (widget.isDesktop) {\n      return Row(\n        crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.start,\n        children: [\n          Expanded(\n            flex: 3,\n            child: KeyedSubtree(\n              key: _lyricsColumnKey,\n              child: _buildLyricsList(),\n            ),\n          ),\n          const SizedBox(width: 28),\n          Expanded(\n            flex: 2,\n            child: _buildDesktopAnnotationRail(),\n          ),\n        ],\n      );\n    }\n\n    return _buildLyricsList();\n  }\n\n  Widget _buildLyricsList() {\n    return Column(\n      crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.stretch,\n      children: [\n        for (int t = 0; t < _parsed.tracks.length; t++) ...[\n          if (t > 0) const SizedBox(height: 28),\n          _buildTrackSection(_parsed.tracks[t]),\n        ],\n      ],\n    );\n  }\n\n  Widget _buildTrackSection(ParsedLyricTrack track) {\n    final header = track.headerItem;\n    final bool isHeaderSelected = _selectedItemIndex == header.index;\n    final bool isHeaderHovered = _hoveredItemIndex == header.index;\n    final bool isPlayingTrack = _playingTrackIndex == track.trackIndex;\n\n    final double titleFontSize = widget.isDesktop ? 20 : 16.5;\n    final TextStyle titleStyle = TextStyle(\n      color: kAccentColor,\n      fontSize: titleFontSize,\n      fontWeight: FontWeight.bold,\n      letterSpacing: 0.6,\n      height: 1.5,\n      fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n    );\n\n    return Column(\n      crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.stretch,\n      children: [\n        MouseRegion(\n          cursor: SystemMouseCursors.click,\n          onEnter: (_) => setState(() => _hoveredItemIndex = header.index),\n          onExit: (_) {\n            if (_hoveredItemIndex == header.index) {\n              setState(() => _hoveredItemIndex = null);\n            }\n          },\n          child: GestureDetector(\n            key: Key('lyric_track_\${track.trackIndex}'),\n            behavior: HitTestBehavior.opaque,\n            onTap: () => _selectItem(header.index, toggleIfSelected: true),\n            child: AnimatedContainer(\n              key: _keyForItem(header.index),\n              duration: const Duration(milliseconds: 140),\n              padding: const EdgeInsets.symmetric(horizontal: 12, vertical: 8),\n              decoration: BoxDecoration(\n                color: isHeaderSelected\n                    ? kAccentColor.withValues(alpha: 0.2)\n                    : isHeaderHovered\n                        ? kAccentColor.withValues(alpha: 0.1)\n                        : kAccentColor.withValues(alpha: 0.04),\n                borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(6),\n                border: Border(\n                  left: BorderSide(\n                    color: isHeaderSelected || isHeaderHovered\n                        ? kAccentColor\n                        : kAccentColor.withValues(alpha: 0.55),\n                    width: isHeaderSelected ? 3.5 : 2.5,\n                  ),\n                ),\n              ),\n              child: Row(\n                crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.center,\n                children: [\n                  Expanded(\n                    child: Text.rich(\n                      TextSpan(\n                        children: [\n                          TextSpan(\n                            text: '// \${track.title}',\n                            style: titleStyle,\n                          ),\n                        ],\n                      ),\n                    ),\n                  ),\n                  const SizedBox(width: 8),\n                  if (isPlayingTrack)\n                    Container(\n                      margin: const EdgeInsets.only(right: 6),\n                      padding: const EdgeInsets.symmetric(\n                        horizontal: 6,\n                        vertical: 2,\n                      ),\n                      decoration: BoxDecoration(\n                        color: kAccentColor.withValues(alpha: 0.2),\n                        borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(4),\n                      ),\n                      child: const Text(\n                        '♪',\n                        style: TextStyle(\n                          color: kAccentColor,\n                          fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                          fontSize: 11,\n                          fontWeight: FontWeight.bold,\n                        ),\n                      ),\n                    ),\n                  Container(\n                    padding: const EdgeInsets.symmetric(\n                      horizontal: 7,\n                      vertical: 3,\n                    ),\n                    decoration: BoxDecoration(\n                      color: isHeaderSelected\n                          ? kAccentColor.withValues(alpha: 0.28)\n                          : Colors.white.withValues(alpha: 0.06),\n                      borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(4),\n                      border: Border.all(\n                        color: isHeaderSelected\n                            ? kAccentColor\n                            : Colors.white12,\n                      ),\n                    ),\n                    child: Text(\n                      isHeaderSelected ? '[ inspecting ]' : '[ track info ]',\n                      style: TextStyle(\n                        color: isHeaderSelected ? Colors.white : Colors.white60,\n                        fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                        fontSize: 10.5,\n                        fontWeight: isHeaderSelected\n                            ? FontWeight.bold\n                            : FontWeight.normal,\n                      ),\n                    ),\n                  ),\n                ],\n              ),\n            ),\n          ),\n        ),\n        if (!widget.isDesktop && isHeaderSelected)\n          Padding(\n            padding: const EdgeInsets.only(top: 10, bottom: 6),\n            child: _buildAnnotationCard(header),\n          ),\n        const SizedBox(height: 10),\n        for (final row in track.rows)\n          if (row.isStanzaBreak)\n            const SizedBox(height: 12)\n          else\n            _buildLyricLineRow(row.item!),\n      ],\n    );\n  }\n\n  Widget _buildLyricLineRow(AnnotatableItem item) {\n    final bool isSelected = _selectedItemIndex == item.index;\n    final bool isHovered = _hoveredItemIndex == item.index;\n    final double fontSize = widget.isDesktop ? 15.0 : 13.5;\n\n    return Column(\n      crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.stretch,\n      children: [\n        Padding(\n          padding: const EdgeInsets.symmetric(vertical: 2.0),\n          child: MouseRegion(\n            cursor: SystemMouseCursors.click,\n            onEnter: (_) => setState(() => _hoveredItemIndex = item.index),\n            onExit: (_) {\n              if (_hoveredItemIndex == item.index) {\n                setState(() => _hoveredItemIndex = null);\n              }\n            },\n            child: GestureDetector(\n              key: Key('lyric_line_\${item.index}'),\n              behavior: HitTestBehavior.opaque,\n              onTap: () => _selectItem(item.index, toggleIfSelected: true),\n              child: AnimatedContainer(\n                key: _keyForItem(item.index),\n                duration: const Duration(milliseconds: 130),\n                padding: const EdgeInsets.symmetric(\n                  horizontal: 10,\n                  vertical: 4,\n                ),\n                decoration: BoxDecoration(\n                  color: isSelected\n                      ? kAccentColor.withValues(alpha: 0.25)\n                      : isHovered\n                          ? kAccentColor.withValues(alpha: 0.13)\n                          : Colors.white.withValues(alpha: 0.045),\n                  borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(4),\n                  border: Border(\n                    left: BorderSide(\n                      color: isSelected\n                          ? kAccentColor\n                          : isHovered\n                              ? kAccentColor.withValues(alpha: 0.8)\n                              : kAccentColor.withValues(alpha: 0.24),\n                      width: isSelected ? 3.0 : 2.0,\n                    ),\n                  ),\n                ),\n                child: Row(\n                  crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.start,\n                  children: [\n                    Expanded(\n                      child: Text(\n                        item.text,\n                        style: TextStyle(\n                          color: isSelected\n                              ? Colors.white\n                              : Colors.white.withValues(alpha: 0.92),\n                          fontSize: fontSize,\n                          height: 1.5,\n                          fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                          fontWeight:\n                              isSelected ? FontWeight.w600 : FontWeight.normal,\n                        ),\n                      ),\n                    ),\n                    if (isSelected || isHovered) ...[\n                      const SizedBox(width: 8),\n                      Padding(\n                        padding: const EdgeInsets.only(top: 3),\n                        child: Text(\n                          isSelected ? '◄' : '?',\n                          style: TextStyle(\n                            color: isSelected\n                                ? kAccentColor\n                                : kAccentColor.withValues(alpha: 0.75),\n                            fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                            fontSize: 11,\n                            fontWeight: FontWeight.bold,\n                          ),\n                        ),\n                      ),\n                    ],\n                  ],\n                ),\n              ),\n            ),\n          ),\n        ),\n        if (!widget.isDesktop && isSelected)\n          Padding(\n            padding: const EdgeInsets.only(top: 6, bottom: 10),\n            child: _buildAnnotationCard(item),\n          ),\n      ],\n    );\n  }\n\n  Widget _buildDesktopAnnotationRail() {\n    if (_selectedItemIndex == null) {\n      return _buildDesktopGuideCard();\n    }\n\n    final item = _parsed.allItems[_selectedItemIndex!];\n    return AnimatedPadding(\n      duration: const Duration(milliseconds: 220),\n      curve: Curves.easeOutCubic,\n      padding: EdgeInsets.only(top: _desktopCardTopOffset),\n      child: _buildAnnotationCard(item),\n    );\n  }\n\n  Widget _buildDesktopGuideCard() {\n    final firstTrack = _parsed.tracks.first;\n\n    return Container(\n      key: const Key('annotation_guide_card'),\n      padding: const EdgeInsets.all(18),\n      decoration: BoxDecoration(\n        color: const Color(0xFF0E0B14),\n        borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(8),\n        border: Border.all(color: kAccentColor.withValues(alpha: 0.35)),\n      ),\n      child: Column(\n        crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.start,\n        children: [\n          const Row(\n            children: [\n              Icon(Icons.terminal, size: 16, color: kAccentColor),\n              SizedBox(width: 8),\n              Text(\n                '// ANNOTATIONS.MD',\n                style: TextStyle(\n                  color: kAccentColor,\n                  fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                  fontWeight: FontWeight.bold,\n                  fontSize: 12,\n                  letterSpacing: 1.0,\n                ),\n              ),\n            ],\n          ),\n          const SizedBox(height: 12),\n          const Text(\n            'Rap Genius-style breakdowns are loaded for every track and bar on this album.',\n            style: TextStyle(\n              color: Colors.white,\n              fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n              fontSize: 13,\n              height: 1.6,\n            ),\n          ),\n          const SizedBox(height: 10),\n          const Text(\n            '• click any // track title for song themes & context\\n'\n            '• click any highlighted lyric line to unpack wordplay, allusions & meaning\\n'\n            '• use prev / next inside the card to step line-by-line',\n            style: TextStyle(\n              color: Colors.white70,\n              fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n              fontSize: 12,\n              height: 1.65,\n            ),\n          ),\n          const SizedBox(height: 16),\n          MouseRegion(\n            cursor: SystemMouseCursors.click,\n            child: InkWell(\n              key: const Key('inspect_first_track_button'),\n              onTap: () => _selectItem(firstTrack.headerItem.index),\n              borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(6),\n              child: Container(\n                padding: const EdgeInsets.symmetric(\n                  horizontal: 12,\n                  vertical: 8,\n                ),\n                decoration: BoxDecoration(\n                  color: kAccentColor.withValues(alpha: 0.16),\n                  borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(6),\n                  border: Border.all(color: kAccentColor),\n                ),\n                child: Text(\n                  '[ inspect \"\${firstTrack.title}\" → ]',\n                  style: const TextStyle(\n                    color: Colors.white,\n                    fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                    fontSize: 12,\n                    fontWeight: FontWeight.bold,\n                  ),\n                ),\n              ),\n            ),\n          ),\n        ],\n      ),\n    );\n  }\n\n  Widget _buildAnnotationCard(AnnotatableItem item) {\n    final bool isTrack = item.kind == AnnotatableTargetKind.track;\n    final TrackBreakdown? trackBreakdown =\n        getTrackBreakdown(widget.item.title, item.trackTitle);\n    final LyricAnnotation? lineAnnotation = isTrack\n        ? null\n        : getLineAnnotation(widget.item.title, item.trackTitle, item.text);\n\n    final String breakdownText = isTrack\n        ? (trackBreakdown?.overview ??\n            'Track overview for \"\${item.trackTitle}\".')\n        : (lineAnnotation?.summary ??\n            'Lyric note for \"\${item.text}\" on \"\${item.trackTitle}\".');\n\n    final List<String> tags = isTrack\n        ? (trackBreakdown?.tags ?? const [])\n        : (lineAnnotation?.tags ?? const []);\n\n    final bool hasPrev = item.index > 0;\n    final bool hasNext = item.index < _parsed.allItems.length - 1;\n    final ParsedLyricTrack parentTrack = _parsed.tracks[item.trackIndex];\n\n    return Container(\n      key: const Key('annotation_card'),\n      decoration: BoxDecoration(\n        color: const Color(0xFF0E0B14),\n        borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(8),\n        border: Border.all(\n          color: kAccentColor.withValues(alpha: 0.55),\n          width: 1.0,\n        ),\n        boxShadow: [\n          BoxShadow(\n            color: kAccentColor.withValues(alpha: 0.12),\n            blurRadius: 18,\n            offset: const Offset(0, 6),\n          ),\n        ],\n      ),\n      child: ClipRRect(\n        borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(7),\n        child: Container(\n          decoration: const BoxDecoration(\n            border: Border(\n              left: BorderSide(color: kAccentColor, width: 3.5),\n            ),\n          ),\n          padding: const EdgeInsets.all(16),\n          child: Column(\n            crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.start,\n            children: [\n              // Card top header\n              Row(\n                children: [\n                  Container(\n                    padding: const EdgeInsets.symmetric(\n                      horizontal: 7,\n                      vertical: 3,\n                    ),\n                    decoration: BoxDecoration(\n                      color: kAccentColor.withValues(alpha: 0.2),\n                      borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(4),\n                    ),\n                    child: Text(\n                      isTrack ? 'TRACK BREAKDOWN' : 'LYRIC ANNOTATION',\n                      style: const TextStyle(\n                        color: kAccentColor,\n                        fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                        fontSize: 10.5,\n                        fontWeight: FontWeight.bold,\n                        letterSpacing: 0.8,\n                      ),\n                    ),\n                  ),\n                  const SizedBox(width: 8),\n                  Expanded(\n                    child: Text(\n                      isTrack\n                          ? 'TRACK \${item.trackIndex + 1} / \${_parsed.tracks.length}'\n                          : 'LINE \${item.lineNumber} / \${item.totalLinesInTrack}',\n                      style: const TextStyle(\n                        color: Colors.white54,\n                        fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                        fontSize: 10.5,\n                      ),\n                      overflow: TextOverflow.ellipsis,\n                    ),\n                  ),\n                  MouseRegion(\n                    cursor: SystemMouseCursors.click,\n                    child: InkWell(\n                      key: const Key('annotation_close_button'),\n                      onTap: _closeAnnotation,\n                      borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(4),\n                      child: const Padding(\n                        padding: EdgeInsets.symmetric(\n                          horizontal: 6,\n                          vertical: 2,\n                        ),\n                        child: Text(\n                          '[ x ]',\n                          style: TextStyle(\n                            color: Colors.white60,\n                            fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                            fontSize: 11.5,\n                            fontWeight: FontWeight.bold,\n                          ),\n                        ),\n                      ),\n                    ),\n                  ),\n                ],\n              ),\n              if (!isTrack) ...[\n                const SizedBox(height: 10),\n                MouseRegion(\n                  cursor: SystemMouseCursors.click,\n                  child: InkWell(\n                    key: const Key('annotation_track_breadcrumb'),\n                    onTap: () => _selectItem(\n                      parentTrack.headerItem.index,\n                      scrollIntoView: true,\n                    ),\n                    borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(4),\n                    child: Padding(\n                      padding: const EdgeInsets.symmetric(vertical: 2),\n                      child: Row(\n                        mainAxisSize: MainAxisSize.min,\n                        children: [\n                          Flexible(\n                            child: Text(\n                              '// \${item.trackTitle}',\n                              style: const TextStyle(\n                                color: kAccentColor,\n                                fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                                fontSize: 12,\n                                fontWeight: FontWeight.bold,\n                              ),\n                              overflow: TextOverflow.ellipsis,\n                            ),\n                          ),\n                          const SizedBox(width: 6),\n                          const Text(\n                            '(track info)',\n                            style: TextStyle(\n                              color: Colors.white38,\n                              fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                              fontSize: 10.5,\n                            ),\n                          ),\n                        ],\n                      ),\n                    ),\n                  ),\n                ),\n              ],\n              const SizedBox(height: 10),\n              // Quoted target\n              Container(\n                width: double.infinity,\n                padding: const EdgeInsets.symmetric(\n                  horizontal: 12,\n                  vertical: 10,\n                ),\n                decoration: BoxDecoration(\n                  color: Colors.black.withValues(alpha: 0.45),\n                  borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(5),\n                  border: Border(\n                    left: BorderSide(\n                      color: kAccentColor.withValues(alpha: 0.7),\n                      width: 2,\n                    ),\n                  ),\n                ),\n                child: Text(\n                  isTrack ? '// \${item.text}' : '\"\${item.text}\"',\n                  style: TextStyle(\n                    color: isTrack ? kAccentColor : Colors.white,\n                    fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                    fontSize: isTrack ? 15 : 13,\n                    fontWeight: isTrack ? FontWeight.bold : FontWeight.w500,\n                    fontStyle: isTrack ? FontStyle.normal : FontStyle.italic,\n                    height: 1.45,\n                  ),\n                ),\n              ),\n              const SizedBox(height: 14),\n              // Breakdown text\n              Text(\n                breakdownText,\n                style: TextStyle(\n                  color: Colors.white.withValues(alpha: 0.92),\n                  fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                  fontSize: 13,\n                  height: 1.65,\n                ),\n              ),\n              if (tags.isNotEmpty) ...[\n                const SizedBox(height: 14),\n                Wrap(\n                  spacing: 6,\n                  runSpacing: 6,\n                  children: tags.map((tag) {\n                    return Container(\n                      padding: const EdgeInsets.symmetric(\n                        horizontal: 7,\n                        vertical: 3,\n                      ),\n                      decoration: BoxDecoration(\n                        color: kAccentColor.withValues(alpha: 0.13),\n                        borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(4),\n                        border: Border.all(\n                          color: kAccentColor.withValues(alpha: 0.3),\n                        ),\n                      ),\n                      child: Text(\n                        '#\$tag',\n                        style: const TextStyle(\n                          color: kAccentColor,\n                          fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                          fontSize: 10.5,\n                        ),\n                      ),\n                    );\n                  }).toList(),\n                ),\n              ],\n              const SizedBox(height: 16),\n              const Divider(color: Colors.white12, height: 1),\n              const SizedBox(height: 10),\n              // Prev / Next footer navigation\n              Row(\n                mainAxisAlignment: MainAxisAlignment.spaceBetween,\n                children: [\n                  _buildNavAction(\n                    key: const Key('annotation_prev_button'),\n                    label: '[ ← prev ]',\n                    enabled: hasPrev,\n                    onTap: () => _stepSelection(-1),\n                  ),\n                  Text(\n                    '\${item.index + 1} / \${_parsed.allItems.length}',\n                    style: const TextStyle(\n                      color: Colors.white38,\n                      fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                      fontSize: 11,\n                    ),\n                  ),\n                  _buildNavAction(\n                    key: const Key('annotation_next_button'),\n                    label: '[ next → ]',\n                    enabled: hasNext,\n                    onTap: () => _stepSelection(1),\n                  ),\n                ],\n              ),\n            ],\n          ),\n        ),\n      ),\n    );\n  }\n\n  Widget _buildNavAction({\n    required Key key,\n    required String label,\n    required bool enabled,\n    required VoidCallback onTap,\n  }) {\n    return MouseRegion(\n      cursor: enabled ? SystemMouseCursors.click : SystemMouseCursors.basic,\n      child: InkWell(\n        key: key,\n        onTap: enabled ? onTap : null,\n        borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(4),\n        child: Padding(\n          padding: const EdgeInsets.symmetric(horizontal: 6, vertical: 4),\n          child: Text(\n            label,\n            style: TextStyle(\n              color: enabled ? kAccentColor : Colors.white24,\n              fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n              fontSize: 12,\n              fontWeight: FontWeight.bold,\n            ),\n          ),\n        ),\n      ),\n    );\n  }\n}\n",
  "lib/pages/music/annotations/blubber_annotations.dart": "import 'package:archbtw_sh/pages/music/lyric_annotations.dart';\n\nfinal Map<String, TrackBreakdown> blubberAnnotations = {\n  'why is it spicy?': const TrackBreakdown(\n    overview:\n        'The jittery, kaleidoscopic opener to \"blubber\"—whose title nods to the viral \"Why is it spicy?\" meme—dives headfirst into neurochemical chaos, imposter syndrome, and manic high-speed wordplay. Archer threads surreal imagery (filleting atoms with butter knives, bleeding gums, rubber drenched in glue) into a portrait of a mind racing ahead of its own stability.',\n    tags: ['opener', 'mental-health', 'wordplay', 'surreal'],\n    lineAnnotations: {\n      'it was 5 or 4pm when they held the ceremony.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Reversing the usual \"4 or 5pm\" immediately tilts the narrator\\'s sense of time slightly off-axis, setting up a hazy memory of hollow recognition.',\n        tags: ['opener', 'disorientation'],\n      ),\n      'gave him a third-rate secondhand 1st place trophy.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Stacks three diminishing modifiers (\"third-rate\", \"secondhand\", \"1st place\") to count down 3-2-1 while mocking an achievement that feels unearned or cheap.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'irony'],\n      ),\n      'blastoff. the shockwaves destroyed all the windows.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Captures the sudden onset of a manic or creative surge—launching skyward with enough force to shatter every fragile boundary around him.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'mental-health'],\n      ),\n      'crescent moon, starry eyed. silent crescendo.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Oxymoronic \"silent crescendo\" pairs starry-eyed wonder with an internal roar building inside his head that nobody else can hear.',\n        tags: ['oxymoron', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      'no strings attached so all the puppets ran free.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Twists the cliché \"no strings attached\" into a surreal image of untethered puppets bolting—freedom that tips immediately into lack of control.',\n        tags: ['idiom', 'surreal'],\n      ),\n      \"the forest feels familiar. the valley's uncanny.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'References the \"uncanny valley\" (something almost-human or almost-right that feels deeply unsettling)—capturing derealization where familiar places suddenly feel alien.',\n        tags: ['psychology', 'wordplay'],\n      ),\n      \"skyline's highlighted. in hindsight, i'd underline it.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Plays on text-formatting verbs (\"highlighted\" / \"underline\") and sunset light—only realizing after the fact which moments actually deserved emphasis.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'reflection'],\n      ),\n      'apple in the limelight. bronze-covered silver linings.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Layers idioms (\"apple of my eye\", \"in the limelight\", \"silver lining\") then downgrades the silver lining to bronze—optimism perpetually tarnished into third place.',\n        tags: ['idiom', 'wordplay'],\n      ),\n      'my gums are bleeding but the cottonmouth should soak it up.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Bleakly funny medication/smoking side-effect humor—treating one unpleasant symptom (dry mouth) as a makeshift bandage for another.',\n        tags: ['dark-humor', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      'jogging with a rabbit foot but running out of luck.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Literalizes \"running out of luck\" into a jogger clutching a lucky rabbit\\'s foot that can\\'t keep pace with his misfortune.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'idiom'],\n      ),\n      \"clearance sale saturday. monday, we're retro.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Pokes at how fast culture recycles what it discards—yesterday\\'s discounted leftovers rebranded as vintage chic forty-eight hours later.',\n        tags: ['satire', 'contrast'],\n      ),\n      \"he'll take all the hand-me-downs you outgrow.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Connects to the \"secondhand\" motif from line 2—picturing himself scavenging cast-off identities, clothes, or affections others have moved past.',\n        tags: ['self-deprecation', 'motif'],\n      ),\n      'majored in madness, minored in morose.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Clean alliterative M-sounds (\"majored\", \"madness\", \"minored\", \"morose\") turning bipolar swings between mania and melancholy into a college degree.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'mental-health'],\n      ),\n      'the rose does smell sweeter when you call it a rose.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Directly pushes back on Shakespeare\\'s \"Romeo and Juliet\" (\"a rose by any other name would smell as sweet\")—arguing that naming things honestly actually matters.',\n        tags: ['literary-reference', 'subversion'],\n      ),\n      'backgammon with receptors . backhanded undermine.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Frames adjusting psychiatric meds or brain chemistry as a board game of chance played directly with neurotransmitters, sabotaged from behind.',\n        tags: ['mental-health', 'metaphor'],\n      ),\n      'filleted the atom with a butter knife.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Absurdist micro-physics brag: splitting the atom with the dullest kitchen utensil imaginable—doing delicate, dangerous work with totally inadequate tools.',\n        tags: ['surreal', 'hyperbole'],\n      ),\n      \"it wasn't rocket science. it was barely ap.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Undercuts the nuclear-physics flex immediately—scaling down from rocket science to high-school Advanced Placement.',\n        tags: ['self-deprecation', 'humor'],\n      ),\n      'he had vivid visions but he made straight-ds.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Classic neurodivergent portrait: bursting with intense, vivid imagination while barely scraping by on conventional grades.',\n        tags: ['mental-health', 'wordplay'],\n      ),\n      'in high-speed pursuit of any good mood.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Likens chasing dopamine or emotional relief to a police chase—reckless, urgent, and exhausting.',\n        tags: ['metaphor', 'mental-health'],\n      ),\n      \"made of rubber that's drenched in glue.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Collapses the playground taunt (\"I\\'m rubber, you\\'re glue\") onto himself—trying to bounce criticism off while secretly coated in adhesive so everything sticks anyway.',\n        tags: ['idiom', 'confessional'],\n      ),\n    },\n  ),\n  'whale mail': const TrackBreakdown(\n    overview:\n        'An intimate, conversational letter addressed directly to Jesus (\"Dear Carpenter\")—introducing the Jonah-and-the-whale motif that anchors \"blubber.\" Balancing raw vulnerability about mood stabilizers, pacing restlessness, and loneliness with disarming warmth (\"How is Dad?\"), Archer turns prayer into an unvarnished pen-pal message signed \"Sincerely, Arch.\"',\n    tags: ['theology', 'epistolary', 'mental-health', 'confessional'],\n    lineAnnotations: {\n      \"dear carpenter, it's been a couple minutes.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Opens like a handwritten letter to Jesus by His earthly trade (Mark 6:3), casually downplaying how long it\\'s been since he last prayed.',\n        tags: ['theology', 'epistolary'],\n      ),\n      \"how have you been? i've been hitting my limit.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Establishes the disarmingly human tone of the song—checking in like an old friend before admitting he\\'s at his breaking point.',\n        tags: ['confessional', 'tone'],\n      ),\n      \"one more bad day, i know i'll flip the table.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Cleverly invokes Jesus flipping the moneychangers\\' tables in the temple (Matthew 21:12) to describe his own simmering frustration.',\n        tags: ['theology', 'idiom'],\n      ),\n      \"they gave me mood stabilizers. i'm still unstable.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Blunt, dryly rhymed confession about psychiatric medication falling short of silencing internal turbulence.',\n        tags: ['mental-health', 'wordplay'],\n      ),\n      \"can you give me a hand? i'm almost out of options.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Simple, unadorned plea for divine intervention when every self-help route feels exhausted.',\n        tags: ['prayer', 'confessional'],\n      ),\n      \"i wanna drown it out but i'd settle for a dropkick.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Contrasts numbing the pain (\"drown it out\", also echoing the ocean/whale theme) with wanting a violent jolt just to snap out of the spiral.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'mental-health'],\n      ),\n      \"i want my day of rest but i can't sit down.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Alludes to the Sabbath (Genesis 2:2 / Exodus 20:8) while describing akathisia or anxious agitation that makes true rest physically impossible.',\n        tags: ['theology', 'mental-health'],\n      ),\n      \"my legs get so sore because i can't stop pacing around.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Concrete physical detail of anxiety—literally pacing grooves into the floor while longing for peace.',\n        tags: ['realism', 'mental-health'],\n      ),\n      'i need some good news. i turned off the tv.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Double meaning on \"good news\": escaping doomscrolling/cable news AND seeking the Gospel (literally Greek \"euangelion\" = \"good news\").',\n        tags: ['theology', 'double-entendre'],\n      ),\n      'i can switch to other mediums or sit under the tree.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            '\"Mediums\" puns on media channels vs. spiritual mediums; \"sit under the tree\" evokes both Buddha under the Bodhi tree, Nathanael under the fig tree (John 1:48), and Jonah under the shade plant (Jonah 4).',\n        tags: ['theology', 'double-entendre'],\n      ),\n      'i have no friends. how did you do it?': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Heartfelt, slightly humorous envy of Jesus gathering twelve disciples (and crowds) while Archer feels deeply isolated.',\n        tags: ['confessional', 'theology'],\n      ),\n      \"i know you're reading this but i really wish you'd prove it.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Captures the ache of faith during silence—believing God hears the letter while desperately wanting an unmistakable reply.',\n        tags: ['theology', 'doubt'],\n      ),\n      'how is dad? i hope he reads it too': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Casually refers to God the Father as \"Dad,\" keeping the prayer conversational and familial rather than stiffly liturgical.',\n        tags: ['theology', 'epistolary'],\n      ),\n      \"and when he's done could you pass it to the spirit in the room?\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Completes the Trinity in two lines—Jesus (\"Carpenter\"), the Father (\"Dad\"), and the Holy Spirit already present right there in the room.',\n        tags: ['theology', 'trinity'],\n      ),\n      'your footsteps are so hard to follow. what a trek.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Acknowledges how demanding discipleship (\"follow me\") feels in everyday life.',\n        tags: ['theology', 'metaphor'],\n      ),\n      \"i cast it all out but there's still no fish in the net.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Alludes to the disciples fishing all night and catching nothing before Jesus tells them to cast on the other side (Luke 5:5 / John 21:3)—pouring out effort with empty results.',\n        tags: ['theology', 'nautical'],\n      ),\n      'the sick all need a doctor and you can make them better.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Paraphrases Mark 2:17 (\"It is not the healthy who need a doctor, but the sick\").',\n        tags: ['theology', 'scripture'],\n      ),\n      'i thought that i could heal. somehow i became the leper.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Sharp self-awareness: trying to fix others or heal himself, only to feel like an outcast in desperate need of Christ\\'s touch (Matthew 8:2-3).',\n        tags: ['theology', 'confessional'],\n      ),\n      \"got some stories for you later. we'll have a couple laughs.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Looks ahead to eternity with warmth and humor—imagining trading stories with God like an old friend.',\n        tags: ['hope', 'epistolary'],\n      ),\n      'sincerely, arch. i really hope you write back': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Signs the letter with his own name (also subtly echoing Eminem\\'s \"Stan\" letter-closing cadence, flipped into an earnest prayer to God).',\n        tags: ['epistolary', 'personal'],\n      ),\n    },\n  ),\n  \"i'll have the ribs please\": const TrackBreakdown(\n    overview:\n        'A charming, tender retelling of Genesis 2 from Adam\\'s point of view—simultaneously functioning as a heartfelt love song to Archer\\'s wife. Turning the creation of Eve from Adam\\'s rib into playful restaurant-order wordplay and a Seinfeld punchline (\"it\\'s real and it\\'s spectacular\"), the track celebrates partnership as the one cure for Edenic loneliness.',\n    tags: ['romance', 'theology', 'genesis', 'wordplay'],\n    lineAnnotations: {\n      'he made me out of dust pulled from the ground': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Direct reference to Genesis 2:7, where God forms Adam from the dust of the earth.',\n        tags: ['scripture', 'genesis'],\n      ),\n      'it was eerily quiet. the birds were the only sound.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Imagines the surreal stillness of pre-Eve Eden—paradise on paper, yet strangely hushed without human conversation.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'genesis'],\n      ),\n      'life was pretty lonely in this garden.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Echoes Genesis 2:18 (\"It is not good for the man to be alone\")—even paradise feels incomplete in solitude.',\n        tags: ['theology', 'romance'],\n      ),\n      'with pure gold. onyx for carving.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Deep-cut Genesis 2:12 detail: the text specifically mentions that the land near Eden holds \"pure gold\" and \"onyx stone.\"',\n        tags: ['scripture', 'detail'],\n      ),\n      'he tried to entertain me. i got to name the beasts': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'References Genesis 2:19-20, where God brings every creature to Adam to name—yet no suitable companion is found among them.',\n        tags: ['scripture', 'humor'],\n      ),\n      'but i kept finding myself looking west from the east.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Eden was planted \"in the east\" (Genesis 2:8); staring west hints at longing for something beyond the horizon—and subtly foreshadows later exile.',\n        tags: ['scripture', 'symbolism'],\n      ),\n      'he had a bone to pick with me.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Classic pun setting up the rib extraction: \"a bone to pick\" normally means a grudge, here taken completely literally.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'idiom'],\n      ),\n      \"maybe it's an idiom but he did it surgically.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Plays on Genesis 2:21—God puts Adam into a deep sleep, removes one rib, and closes the flesh back up like the first surgeon in history.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'scripture'],\n      ),\n      'sewn. do the stitches make me look cool?': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Endearingly boyish vanity upon waking up from divine surgery—trying to impress Eve with his scar.',\n        tags: ['humor', 'romance'],\n      ),\n      \"i didn't need that bone. the only thing missing here was you.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Sweet, earnest hook turning the missing rib into a declaration of devotion.',\n        tags: ['romance', 'refrain'],\n      ),\n      'becoming one flesh. now i want a piece of your mind.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Quotes Genesis 2:24 (\"become one flesh\") and flips the angry idiom \"give you a piece of my mind\" into genuine curiosity about her thoughts.',\n        tags: ['scripture', 'wordplay'],\n      ),\n      \"there's plenty of things to do here but i don't want to just pass the time.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Rejects killing time in favor of being fully present and intentional with the person he loves.',\n        tags: ['romance', 'refrain'],\n      ),\n      \"naked but not ashamed. it's just us and the weather's nice.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Directly cites Genesis 2:25 (\"naked and they felt no shame\"), evoking complete vulnerability and comfort with a partner.',\n        tags: ['scripture', 'romance'],\n      ),\n      'i love the way your fingers trace my chest and its lopside.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Intimate physical callback to the missing rib leaving his chest playfully lopsided.',\n        tags: ['romance', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      'this seems too good to be true but no one here knows how to lie.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Pre-Fall innocence before the serpent introduces deception—mirroring the rare safety of complete trust in love.',\n        tags: ['theology', 'romance'],\n      ),\n      \"i don't want this day to end. let's stay up and talk all night.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Captures early-love euphoria—staying up past dawn simply talking.',\n        tags: ['romance', 'confessional'],\n      ),\n      'i could stay awake for days here in this scene.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Extends the sleeplessness of infatuation into wanting to freeze the moment forever.',\n        tags: ['romance', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      'and when i crash, i still see you in my dreams.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Even sleep doesn\\'t interrupt the devotion—echoing how Adam originally slept to wake up to her.',\n        tags: ['romance', 'callback'],\n      ),\n      'maybe this is all just some metaphor': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Winks at the age-old theological debate over whether Genesis 2 is literal history or poetic allegory—as well as his own song being an allegory for his wife.',\n        tags: ['theology', 'meta'],\n      ),\n      \"but i really think it's real and it's spectacular.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Iconic Seinfeld reference (Teri Hatcher\\'s famous line, \"They\\'re real, and they\\'re spectacular\") repurposed as a joyful affirmation of both Scripture and love.',\n        tags: ['pop-culture', 'humor'],\n      ),\n    },\n  ),\n  'beached': const TrackBreakdown(\n    overview:\n        'Deepening \"blubber\"\\'s whale motif, \"beached\" portrays dissociation, emotional whiplash, and feeling stranded in limbo between extremes—heatwaves and freeze warnings, mania and crash landings. The narrator feels reduced to a \"voice in a head\" or a \"brain exercise\" inside someone else\\'s fever dream, longing for a partner\\'s warmth (\"her summer dress\") to anchor him back to reality.',\n    tags: ['dissociation', 'mental-health', 'nautical', 'surreal'],\n    lineAnnotations: {\n      'powdered sugar on mountain peaks.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Opens with a bright, slightly surreal image of snowcapped peaks—also carrying a faint double reading of stimulants (\"powdered sugar\") fueling an artificial high.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'double-entendre'],\n      ),\n      'weak geek. fatigued pipsqueak physique.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Rapid-fire internal ee-rhymes deliver biting, cartoonish self-deprecation about feeling frail and worn down.',\n        tags: ['internal-rhyme', 'self-deprecation'],\n      ),\n      \"plane's going down. preparing for the masquerade.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Putting on a social mask (\"masquerade\") even while everything internally is nose-diving.',\n        tags: ['metaphor', 'mental-health'],\n      ),\n      \"one stitch away. lacerations don't exaggerate.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Barely holding together at the seams—unlike the mind, real wounds don\\'t lie or overdramatize how badly something hurts.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'confessional'],\n      ),\n      'duck duck goose. swan dove into the autumn foliage.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Links three birds in one breathless line (duck, goose, swan) to depict a reckless plunge (\"swan dive\") from childhood games straight into seasonal decay.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      \"thought i'd get a point but i don't know what the goal is.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Sports pun (\"point\" / \"goal\") voicing existential confusion—playing hard without knowing what winning even looks like.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'existential'],\n      ),\n      \"i live inside someone else's fever dream.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Textbook depersonalization/derealization: feeling like an unwilling side character trapped in an overheated hallucination.',\n        tags: ['dissociation', 'surreal'],\n      ),\n      \"i'm just a voice in a head. no matter what i scream.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Being trapped inside your own skull—even at maximum volume, nobody outside hears the panic.',\n        tags: ['mental-health', 'isolation'],\n      ),\n      'no contest but pleading nonetheless.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Legal wordplay on a \"no contest\" (*nolo contendere*) plea—surrendering the fight while still begging for mercy.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'refrain'],\n      ),\n      'freeze warning. daydreaming of her summer dress.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Weather-alert imagery for emotional numbness, clinging to the warm memory of his partner during a cold spell.',\n        tags: ['contrast', 'romance'],\n      ),\n      'the heatwave sucked but the cold wind blows.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Puns on \"sucked\" and \"blows\" while tracing the pendulum swing between manic overheating and depressive chill.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'mental-health'],\n      ),\n      \"i'm not quite convinced that this isn't limbo.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Stuck in purgatorial suspension—neither thriving nor completely gone, just stranded (\"beached\").',\n        tags: ['theology', 'refrain'],\n      ),\n      'heart started beating at a faster pace.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Captures the sudden physiological rush of adrenaline, panic, or infatuation.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'anxiety'],\n      ),\n      'started sweet but it had a bitter aftertaste.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Contrasts an intoxicating beginning (a high, an impulse, or a memory) with the sour crash that follows.',\n        tags: ['contrast', 'metaphor'],\n      ),\n      \"i'm not a human anymore, i'm a brain exercise.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Overthinking to the point of losing bodily personhood—feeling like a thought experiment rather than a flesh-and-blood person.',\n        tags: ['dissociation', 'confessional'],\n      ),\n      \"it's just a shame that the origin is not so bright.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Self-deprecating punchline: if he\\'s a thought experiment, the mind dreaming him up isn\\'t very smart (and his beginnings feel dim).',\n        tags: ['self-deprecation', 'double-entendre'],\n      ),\n      \"wisdom takes time. i'll just wait and cram later.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Relatable procrastination joke—treating lifelong spiritual maturity like a college final you can pull an all-nighter for.',\n        tags: ['humor', 'self-deprecation'],\n      ),\n      'crash landing. we created a crater.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Payoff to line 3\\'s falling plane—touchdown leaves an unmistakable scar.',\n        tags: ['callback', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      \"hopefully the catering is good. don't cheap out.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Absurdist deadpan humor treating the aftermath of the crash (or his own funeral) like a catered event.',\n        tags: ['dark-humor', 'surreal'],\n      ),\n      \"i'm sure i'll wake up soon but i don't know how.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Closes back in the \"fever dream\" loop—hopeful the fog will lift, yet clueless about how to force himself awake.',\n        tags: ['dissociation', 'closer'],\n      ),\n    },\n  ),\n  's.o.s.': const TrackBreakdown(\n    overview:\n        'A whimsical, candy-coated shipwreck romance—the playful flip side to \"beached.\" Stranded on an island made of \"dessert\" (punning on \"desert island\"), Archer turns distress signals into love letters: even as the tide sweeps away their Twizzlers and the boat sinks, he crosses his fingers that rescue never arrives so he can stay marooned with her forever.',\n    tags: ['romance', 'wordplay', 'whimsical', 'nautical'],\n    lineAnnotations: {\n      'stranded on an island made purely of dessert.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Classic spelling pun turning a barren \"desert island\" into a decadent \"dessert island\"—launching the track\\'s Candy Land imagery.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'opener'],\n      ),\n      'delightful dancing dandelions donning dress shirts.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Playful six-word D-alliteration painting a whimsical, storybook paradise.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'whimsical'],\n      ),\n      'mint-chocolate winds carrying spores.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Blends ice-cream flavors with earthy nature imagery for a dreamy, slightly psychedelic breeze.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'surreal'],\n      ),\n      'pixie stick sand. the crabs do chores.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Sugary beach sand and helpful crustacean housekeepers—an idyllic escape where nobody has to worry about real-world drudgery.',\n        tags: ['whimsical', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      'time stops when i look into the hourglass.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Clever double meaning: losing track of time staring at an hourglass AND admiring her hourglass figure.',\n        tags: ['double-entendre', 'romance'],\n      ),\n      'always in a good way but a little bit crass.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Cheekily owns the double entendre from the previous line with a grin.',\n        tags: ['humor', 'self-aware'],\n      ),\n      'headlights were bright. frozen like deer.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Dazzled and stunned by her presence—setting up a surreal punchline on the next line.',\n        tags: ['idiom', 'setup'],\n      ),\n      'whatever did you have to do to get the car here?': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Breaks the \"deer in headlights\" cliché literally by asking how on earth a car ended up on a deserted candy island.',\n        tags: ['humor', 'surreal'],\n      ),\n      'the tide is coming in. it dragged out all of our twizzlers.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Even disaster on this island is charmingly absurd—the ocean stealing licorice ropes instead of real supplies.',\n        tags: ['whimsical', 'refrain'],\n      ),\n      'smoke signals or not, all i want to do is kiss her.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Ties into the title \"s.o.s.\"—whether rescue spots their distress smoke or not, his only priority is kissing her.',\n        tags: ['romance', 'refrain'],\n      ),\n      \"maybe the boat won't come through.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Subverts the shipwreck survival trope—secretly rooting against being rescued.',\n        tags: ['romance', 'subversion'],\n      ),\n      \"fingers crossed, i'll stay stuck here with you\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Turns being marooned into a wish come true, contrasting sharply with the lonely isolation elsewhere on \"blubber.\"',\n        tags: ['romance', 'refrain'],\n      ),\n      'cotton candy laughter with sour patch speech.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Captures her personality in candy contrasts: airy sweetness in her laugh paired with playfully sharp, \"first they\\'re sour, then they\\'re sweet\" banter.',\n        tags: ['romance', 'metaphor'],\n      ),\n      \"sugar in your veins and i'm addicted to sweets.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Playfully frames his devotion to her as a full-blown sweet tooth.',\n        tags: ['romance', 'metaphor'],\n      ),\n      'moonbeams reflect off of caramel eyes.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Shifts from playful candy puns into genuinely luminous romantic imagery.',\n        tags: ['romance', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      'stars barely shining through the amethyst sky.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Deep purple night-sky imagery—also echoing the purple color palette woven throughout Archer\\'s site and lyrics.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'color-motif'],\n      ),\n      \"behind the optics' butterscotch, you illuminate.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Sees an inner glow radiating behind her warm brown (\"butterscotch\") eyes.',\n        tags: ['romance', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      'a gingerbread tent that you can decorate.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Turns a makeshift castaway shelter into a cozy holiday gingerbread house—a home made sweet just by sharing it.',\n        tags: ['whimsical', 'romance'],\n      ),\n      'pop rocks in my head. my legs are jello.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Nervous, fizzy infatuation rendered in nostalgic candy textures—crackling thoughts and weak knees.',\n        tags: ['romance', 'simile'],\n      ),\n      'just let the ship sink and enjoy the cello.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Nods to the Titanic string quartet playing as the ship went down—choosing to savor the music and moment rather than panic.',\n        tags: ['pop-culture', 'historical-reference'],\n      ),\n    },\n  ),\n  \"all aboard that's going aboard\": const TrackBreakdown(\n    overview:\n        'Named after the classic train/boat boarding call (and famous Bugs Bunny / Looney Tunes refrain), this track captures the restless urge to step out of hermit-like hiding and claim the driver\\'s seat (\"player one\", \"fastpass\"). Blending Super Mario references, tech puns (\"random access\"), purple rain-smudged notebook pages, and a smoke break with an angel, it wrestles with ambition, imperfection, and letting go of the past.',\n    tags: ['ambition', 'wordplay', 'pop-culture', 'confessional'],\n    lineAnnotations: {\n      \"filled up the tank. now i'm on a spiteful ego trip.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Literalizes \"ego trip\" as a road trip fueled by pure spite—running on defiance instead of calm confidence.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'opener'],\n      ),\n      \"i'm never coming back. sun's up but i'm shadowless.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Either moving at high noon with the sun directly overhead or feeling so detached from his old self that he leaves no shadow behind.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'surreal'],\n      ),\n      'treehouse is way too high. did you even get a permit?': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Pokes fun at adult bureaucracy intruding on childhood escapism—even a backyard sanctuary isn\\'t safe from zoning laws.',\n        tags: ['humor', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      \"i've been stuck inside a shell. just another hermit.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Hermit-crab metaphor for social withdrawal and protective isolation.',\n        tags: ['metaphor', 'confessional'],\n      ),\n      'carelessly took care of carefully carved characters.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Dense tongue-twister of C-sounds and \"care\" roots—describing treating meticulously written lyrics or relationships with accidental recklessness.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'wordplay'],\n      ),\n      'left the paper in the rain. it smudged all of the lavender.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Notebook pages written in purple/lavender ink ruined by rain—symbolizing carefully laid plans dissolving in real life.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'color-motif'],\n      ),\n      \"if i'm being honest though, the purple blur's still gorgeous.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Finds beauty in the accident—imperfection and smudged boundaries turning into art of their own.',\n        tags: ['reflection', 'color-motif'],\n      ),\n      'the lack of structure makes me feel just a little bit more curious.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Embraces improvisation and uncertainty instead of letting chaos trigger panic.',\n        tags: ['reflection', 'growth'],\n      ),\n      \"shared smokes with an angel. i don't know if they fell.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Puns on \"fell\" (fallen angel / Lucifer\\'s host) during an ambiguous late-night conversation with a charismatic stranger or muse.',\n        tags: ['theology', 'double-entendre'],\n      ),\n      \"i didn't think to ask at the time. instead, we just shared tales.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Too caught up in the stories and camaraderie to vet whether the influence was heavenly or demonic.',\n        tags: ['narrative', 'refrain'],\n      ),\n      'arachnophobic weaving webs highlighted by fluorescence.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Irony of someone afraid of spiders spinning intricate webs himself under harsh office fluorescent lights—getting tangled in his own overthinking or code.',\n        tags: ['irony', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      'time is a commodity and money is the essence.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Deliberately swaps the famous proverb (\"time is of the essence / money is a commodity\") to show how capitalism scrambles human priorities.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'anti-capitalism'],\n      ),\n      \"i'm player one this go. you can wear the green.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Classic Super Mario Bros. nod: claiming Mario (Player 1) and handing Player 2 the Luigi controller (\"wear the green\").',\n        tags: ['pop-culture', 'gaming'],\n      ),\n      'on platforms with toadstool-power, so it seems.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Extends the Mario metaphor—platforming levels powered by Super Mushrooms (\"toadstool-power\"), with a sly nod to psychedelic mushrooms.',\n        tags: ['gaming', 'double-entendre'],\n      ),\n      \"usually, i'd go last. not chasing wins, just laughs.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Admits his default mode is self-effacing comedy rather than cutthroat competition.',\n        tags: ['confessional', 'personal'],\n      ),\n      'this time i bought a fastpass. cutting lines like class.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Theme-park FastPass meets skipping school (\"cutting lines\" / \"cutting class\")—tired of waiting patiently at the back of the queue.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'double-entendre'],\n      ),\n      \"you'll never have enough of anything that you desire\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'A sobering truth about hedonic adaptation—the goalpost of human craving always moves further away.',\n        tags: ['philosophy', 'reflection'],\n      ),\n      \"but i'll keep making it rain with my corduroy's on fire.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Collides hip-hop \"making it rain\" with \"liar, liar, pants on fire\" (wearing indie-kid corduroys)—parodying flashy bravado while putting out his own flames.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'humor'],\n      ),\n      'total eclipse. he skimped on random access.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Computer-science pun: skimping on RAM (\"random access\" memory) leaves the brain lagging and blacked out like an eclipse.',\n        tags: ['tech', 'wordplay'],\n      ),\n      \"hand me another paper. i'll roll the past, then pass it.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Clever homophone close (\"past\" / \"pass it\"): rolling yesterday\\'s baggage into a joint and passing it along so he doesn\\'t have to hold onto it.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'closer'],\n      ),\n    },\n  ),\n  'we just need to budget better': const TrackBreakdown(\n    overview:\n        'A deeply moving, grounded portrait of financial hardship and layoffs—ironically titled after the condescending advice people love giving to anyone struggling to make ends meet. Splitting a free app-signup junior burger, putting \\\$3 on pump 2, and finding the lights shut off, Archer leans on the Sermon on the Mount (Matthew 6) and the love beside him to remind himself that real wealth can\\'t be measured by a bank balance.',\n    tags: ['theology', 'realism', 'romance', 'working-class'],\n    lineAnnotations: {\n      'out on the balcony, sharing our last smoke': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Opens with a quiet, intimate snapshot of rationing what little is left—together.',\n        tags: ['realism', 'opener'],\n      ),\n      'we tried to save it for the am but we both started to jones': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Honest human detail: good budgeting intentions colliding with stress and cravings before morning even arrives.',\n        tags: ['realism', 'confessional'],\n      ),\n      \"we napped all day. there's nothing else to do.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Captures the heavy, aimless stillness of unemployment or being flat broke—sleeping to pass hours you can\\'t afford to spend.',\n        tags: ['realism', 'mental-health'],\n      ),\n      'can we get 3 dollars on pump number 2?': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Unmistakable working-class lived experience—walking inside the gas station to prepay a few crumpled dollars just to keep the tank off empty.',\n        tags: ['working-class', 'detail'],\n      ),\n      \"noodles again. i think we're both sick of it.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Ramen-for-dinner monotony when groceries are stretched to the bone.',\n        tags: ['working-class', 'realism'],\n      ),\n      \"the tap water's not bad here. well, maybe just a bit.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Finding tiny comic optimism in rough tap water before immediately admitting it actually does taste a little off.',\n        tags: ['humor', 'realism'],\n      ),\n      \"the lights didn't come on when we hit the switch.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'A gut-punch understatement: the electricity got shut off.',\n        tags: ['working-class', 'somber'],\n      ),\n      'but i heard its better to be poor than to be rich.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Pivots toward Jesus\\'s Beatitudes (Luke 6:20, \"Blessed are you who are poor\")—wryly testing Scripture against the dark apartment.',\n        tags: ['theology', 'contrast'],\n      ),\n      \"we don't need to worry about food or what to wear.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Direct paraphrase of the Sermon on the Mount (Matthew 6:25: \"do not worry about your life, what you will eat or drink; or about your body, what you will wear\").',\n        tags: ['scripture', 'refrain'],\n      ),\n      'he feeds and clothes the birds and probably the bears.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'References Matthew 6:26 (\"Look at the birds of the air... your heavenly Father feeds them\") and playfully extends God\\'s providence to bears too.',\n        tags: ['scripture', 'humor'],\n      ),\n      \"money equals camels passing through the needle's eye.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Cites Matthew 19:24 (\"it is easier for a camel to go through the eye of a needle than for someone who is rich to enter the kingdom of God\").',\n        tags: ['scripture', 'theology'],\n      ),\n      \"there's gonna be a big party when we finally arrive.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Looks forward to the biblical wedding banquet / heavenly feast—where scarcity finally ends.',\n        tags: ['theology', 'hope'],\n      ),\n      \"we'll get to see our grandparents and the terriers we miss.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Heart-meltingly specific vision of heaven: not golden mansions, just reuniting with departed grandparents and beloved family dogs.',\n        tags: ['personal', 'heartfelt'],\n      ),\n      \"so we don't need to fear, or dread, or even be anxious.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Echoes Philippians 4:6 (\"do not be anxious about anything\") as a gentle pep talk to himself and his wife.',\n        tags: ['scripture', 'comfort'],\n      ),\n      \"yeah, it'd be nice to have variety. even just a big mac.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Keeps the spirituality grounded in real hunger—acknowledging that even fast food feels like a luxury when money is tight.',\n        tags: ['realism', 'working-class'],\n      ),\n      'but we can get a free junior burger if we sign up on this app.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Peak modern-poverty resourcefulness: hunting fast-food promo deals just to get a hot meal.',\n        tags: ['working-class', 'modern-life'],\n      ),\n      \"we'll cut it in half and have a couple bites each.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Quiet, tender solidarity—splitting one tiny free burger down the middle without resentment.',\n        tags: ['romance', 'heartfelt'],\n      ),\n      \"maybe there's enough in the couch for a small sweet tea.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Digging through couch cushions for spare change to turn half a burger into a proper meal.',\n        tags: ['working-class', 'detail'],\n      ),\n      'i promise god will make it better. layoffs or not.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Names the concrete culprit (\"layoffs\") and anchors the track in stubborn faith and reassurance.',\n        tags: ['theology', 'personal'],\n      ),\n      \"you can't buy this kind of happiness. if you could, it'd cost a lot.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'A priceless closing twist: their love and resilience in hard times is worth more than anything money could ever purchase.',\n        tags: ['romance', 'closer'],\n      ),\n    },\n  ),\n  'is that real wool?': const TrackBreakdown(\n    overview:\n        'A blistering prophetic critique of performative Christianity and spiritual hypocrisy. The title directly references Jesus\\'s warning about \"wolves in sheep\\'s clothing\" (Matthew 7:15)—tugging on a churchgoer\\'s fleece to ask if it\\'s real. Weaving Matthew 7 (logs in eyes), Matthew 23 (whitewashed tombs), Luke 21 (the widow\\'s two mites), and deep-sea anglerfish imagery, Archer calls out hollowed-out megachurch aesthetics while keeping his own posture humble (\"I\\'ll keep singing the sinner\\'s prayer\").',\n    tags: ['theology', 'critique', 'scripture', 'wordplay'],\n    lineAnnotations: {\n      \"there's a bump on the log in the hole of your eye.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Blends the children\\'s song \"There\\'s a Hole in the Bottom of the Sea\" (\"a bump on the log...\") with Jesus\\'s teaching about ignoring the plank/log in your own eye (Matthew 7:3-5).',\n        tags: ['scripture', 'wordplay'],\n      ),\n      'get comfy. the abyss has no night light.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Extends the \"bottom of the sea\" riff into spiritual darkness—warning against getting comfortable in shallow complacency.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'nautical'],\n      ),\n      'sea floor. watch the angler fish escape.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'The anglerfish uses a glowing lure in total darkness to trap prey—an eerie parallel to false teachers dangling shiny distractions.',\n        tags: ['metaphor', 'nautical'],\n      ),\n      'they tried to show you how. even saw them demonstrate.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Points out that genuine humility and mercy were modeled plainly in front of them, leaving no excuse for willful blindness.',\n        tags: ['theology', 'critique'],\n      ),\n      \"come out and see the son. it's worth a little death.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Homophone wordplay on \"Son\" (Christ) / \"sun\" rising above the ocean floor, paired with \"dying to self\" (Luke 9:23)—also winking at the French phrase *la petite mort*.',\n        tags: ['theology', 'double-entendre'],\n      ),\n      'just swim up. though, your puddle has no depth.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Sharp dismissal of superficial faith: acting like you\\'re exploring spiritual depths while splashing in a shallow puddle.',\n        tags: ['metaphor', 'critique'],\n      ),\n      'whitewashed tombs full of bones and dust and fingernails.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Directly quotes Jesus rebuking the Pharisees in Matthew 23:27—\"whitewashed tombs, which look beautiful on the outside but on the inside are full of the bones of the dead.\"',\n        tags: ['scripture', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      \"high and mighty you might be but i'll keep singing the sinner's prayer.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Echoes the Parable of the Pharisee and the Tax Collector (Luke 18:9-14)—refusing smug superiority and choosing honest repentance.',\n        tags: ['scripture', 'humility'],\n      ),\n      \"why pretend that we're something that we're not?\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Cuts straight to the core of the song: rejecting Sunday-morning performance and fake perfection.',\n        tags: ['confessional', 'critique'],\n      ),\n      'we sat in your pew, forgot the answers that you sought.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Describes sitting through rigid church orthodoxy that prizes memorized talking points over lived compassion.',\n        tags: ['theology', 'critique'],\n      ),\n      \"you heard but didn't comprehend. whatever did he say?\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Echoes Jesus quoting Isaiah 6:9 (\"You will be ever hearing but never understanding\") about listeners who miss the heart of His parables.',\n        tags: ['scripture', 'theology'],\n      ),\n      'one ear to the other even if it gets replayed.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Playing sermons on repeat means nothing if the message goes in one ear and straight out the other.',\n        tags: ['idiom', 'critique'],\n      ),\n      \"at least we know that we're confused and lost and dropped all the directions.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Honest self-awareness beats fake certainty—admitting you\\'re lost is the first step toward actually being found.',\n        tags: ['humility', 'metaphor'],\n      ),\n      \"the subscription gps in your suv's defective.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Hilariously modernizes \"blind guides\" (Matthew 23:16) into a broken paywalled luxury-SUV navigation system—skewering suburban prosperity-gospel status symbols.',\n        tags: ['satire', 'modern-life'],\n      ),\n      '\"forgive us of our debts and please forgive our debtors.\"': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Quotes the Lord\\'s Prayer (Matthew 6:12) directly before contrasting lip service with real generosity.',\n        tags: ['scripture', 'theology'],\n      ),\n      'all she had was 2 cents and she still tipped better.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Brilliant modern flip of the Widow\\'s Mite (Mark 12:41-44 / Luke 21:1-4)—punning on \"two cents\" (both coins and opinions) and contrasting her sacrificial generosity with stingy Sunday-lunch church crowds.',\n        tags: ['scripture', 'wordplay'],\n      ),\n      'you can raise your hands and recite any words thrown on the screen.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Targets automated contemporary worship routines—hands lifted to projector lyrics without inward transformation.',\n        tags: ['critique', 'modern-life'],\n      ),\n      \"but as you think in your heart, so you do. don't be deceived.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Synthesizes Proverbs 23:7 (\"as he thinks in his heart, so is he\") and Galatians 6:7 (\"Do not be deceived: God cannot be mocked\").',\n        tags: ['scripture', 'theology'],\n      ),\n      'either give up or give and do your best to take away.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Triple play on \"give up\", \"give\" (generosity), and \"take away\" (extracting a lesson—or greedily taking from others).',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'theology'],\n      ),\n      \"there's lessons in the parchment, open up to any page.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Closes by pointing straight back to the actual text of Scripture rather than performative church culture.',\n        tags: ['scripture', 'closer'],\n      ),\n    },\n  ),\n  \"i don't like you very much\": const TrackBreakdown(\n    overview:\n        'A gleefully unhinged comedic revenge fantasy—escalating from duct-taping someone inside a fridge to time-traveling just to ruin their favorite movie—only to pull the rug out on the very last line with the pettiest possible motive: they stole his parking spot. Sitting right in the middle of \"blubber\"\\'s heavier spiritual and emotional tracks, it showcases Archer\\'s sharp comic timing and absurd escalation.',\n    tags: ['comedy', 'dark-humor', 'twist-ending', 'satire'],\n    lineAnnotations: {\n      'i want to shove you in the refrigerator and duct tape it shut.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Opens at full cartoon-villain intensity—starting absurdly dark so the final twist lands even harder.',\n        tags: ['dark-humor', 'opener'],\n      ),\n      'then take a long vacation and check back in a month': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Casual follow-through that treats locking his nemesis in an appliance like leaving a casserole behind before a trip.',\n        tags: ['dark-humor', 'comedy'],\n      ),\n      \"i'll go wherever you dream of going and send you a post card.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Petty psychological warfare: stealing their bucket-list destination solely to rub it in by mail.',\n        tags: ['comedy', 'petty'],\n      ),\n      \"i don't wish you were here. xoxo heart.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Inverts the classic postcard cliché (\"Wish you were here\") and signs it with sarcastically sweet \"XOXO heart.\"',\n        tags: ['sarcasm', 'subversion'],\n      ),\n      'i wanna learn a hundred languages just to have more curse words': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Weaponized polyglot ambition—dedicating years of linguistic study purely to expand his profanity vocabulary.',\n        tags: ['comedy', 'hyperbole'],\n      ),\n      \"to throw your way. i won't resort to slurs.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Hysterical moral boundary in the middle of an unhinged rant: he\\'ll tape you in a fridge, sure, but he still has standards.',\n        tags: ['comedy', 'contrast'],\n      ),\n      'break off all your pencil lead before filling up your pencil box.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Drops from grand villainy down to exquisitely annoying grade-school sabotage.',\n        tags: ['petty', 'comedy'],\n      ),\n      'take the blade from the sharpener and hide it in your socks.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Immediately whiplash-escalates from mild classroom inconvenience back to a Saw-movie trap.',\n        tags: ['dark-humor', 'contrast'],\n      ),\n      'i wanna buy you groceries and then let them expire.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Spiteful financial commitment: spending his own money just to watch food rot out of petty malice.',\n        tags: ['comedy', 'absurd'],\n      ),\n      'donate them to your favorite cause before setting them on fire.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Doubles down on theatrical cruelty—spoiling both the groceries and a charity gesture in one ridiculous stroke.',\n        tags: ['dark-humor', 'hyperbole'],\n      ),\n      \"let's play doctor but let's not play pretend.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Flips an innocent childhood game (and suggestive double entendre) into unlicensed horror-comedy surgery.',\n        tags: ['dark-humor', 'wordplay'],\n      ),\n      \"i don't have any experience but i'll carve out your pretense\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Crisp rhyme linking \"pretend\" and \"pretense\"—promising amateur surgery specifically to excise their fake attitude.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'dark-humor'],\n      ),\n      'sugar in your gas tank just sounds so kindergarten.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Dismisses the classic petty car-vandalism prank as amateur hour.',\n        tags: ['comedy', 'escalation'],\n      ),\n      \"i'll use a flaming rag right before it's started.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Swaps schoolyard sabotage for a full-blown Molotov cocktail right as they turn the ignition.',\n        tags: ['dark-humor', 'escalation'],\n      ),\n      'put handwarmers in your pillows and then move in next door.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Diabolical comfort sabotage—permanently denying someone the bliss of the cool side of the pillow, then becoming their neighbor forever.',\n        tags: ['petty', 'comedy'],\n      ),\n      \"blaring genres that you hate and then i'll laugh and laugh some more.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Commits to buying real estate next door just to wage 24/7 musical warfare.',\n        tags: ['petty', 'comedy'],\n      ),\n      \"i'm scared of spiders but you are too so i'll tough it out\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Willing to conquer his own arachnophobia (also mentioned on \"all aboard\") purely out of dedication to pettiness.',\n        tags: ['comedy', 'callback'],\n      ),\n      \"and build up a collection i'll pour in your sleeping mouth\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Weaponizes the famous urban legend about swallowing spiders in your sleep—except now it\\'s deliberate.',\n        tags: ['dark-humor', 'pop-culture'],\n      ),\n      \"what's your favorite movie? i'll rewrite the story\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Ascends to sci-fi levels of spite just to sabotage someone\\'s comfort media.',\n        tags: ['absurd', 'comedy'],\n      ),\n      'and then go back in time and make sure they make it boring.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Inventing a time machine solely to turn a stranger\\'s favorite film into a snoozefest—peak disproportionate effort.',\n        tags: ['comedy', 'hyperbole'],\n      ),\n      'i think you see where i\\'m going but you seem dumb so maybe not.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Pauses right before the big reveal to insult their intelligence one last time.',\n        tags: ['setup', 'comedy'],\n      ),\n      \"next time you'll think twice before taking my parking spot.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'The killer punchline: twenty lines of homicidal, time-traveling rage were sparked by the most mundane everyday annoyance on earth.',\n        tags: ['twist-ending', 'punchline'],\n      ),\n    },\n  ),\n  \"where's the boat?\": const TrackBreakdown(\n    overview:\n        'A raw, 4:30 AM wrestling match with God over calling, waiting, and unanswered prayers. Echoing the album\\'s maritime/Jonah imagery (\"waiting for a boat at the dock\"), Archer voices the agonizing friction between believing God is omnipotent and watching his wife hurt while every sign feels contradictory—desperate for direction and begging for breakthrough right now.',\n    tags: ['theology', 'prayer', 'insomnia', 'confessional'],\n    lineAnnotations: {\n      \"it's 4:30am. i've already been up for hours.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Drops the listener straight into pre-dawn insomnia—the quietest, heaviest hour for spiraling thoughts.',\n        tags: ['insomnia', 'opener'],\n      ),\n      'contemplating life and death and my own lack of power.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Confronts mortality and human helplessness head-on in the dark.',\n        tags: ['existential', 'confessional'],\n      ),\n      'was that just a weird dream or was it a vision from an angel?': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Captures the disorienting blur between vivid late-night dreams, racing thoughts, and genuine spiritual discernment.',\n        tags: ['theology', 'mental-health'],\n      ),\n      \"when will the son rise? i know that it can't just be a fable.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Dual meaning on \"Son rise\": waiting both for morning daylight after a sleepless night and for Christ\\'s return/deliverance, clinging to faith against doubt.',\n        tags: ['theology', 'double-entendre'],\n      ),\n      'where are we headed? do you want me overseas?': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Willing to drop everything—even become an overseas missionary—if only God would hand over clear marching orders.',\n        tags: ['theology', 'calling'],\n      ),\n      \"i'll go door to door if needed. just guide me please.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Not asking for an easy assignment—just clarity. Even uncomfortable door-to-door evangelism beats directionless waiting.',\n        tags: ['prayer', 'calling'],\n      ),\n      \"i've never been so confused. everything is a sign.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Relatable portrait of hyper-vigilant pattern-seeking (apophenia): when you crave guidance desperately, every coincidence starts looking like a cryptic clue.',\n        tags: ['psychology', 'theology'],\n      ),\n      \"but there's a lot of contradictions. it's hard to discern what's yours and mine.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Honestly distinguishes between God\\'s actual voice and his own anxious projections colliding inside his head.',\n        tags: ['theology', 'self-aware'],\n      ),\n      'what is my purpose? just to spin around on a rock?': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Strips existential angst down to cosmic scale—orbiting the sun on a spinning planet without knowing why.',\n        tags: ['existential', 'refrain'],\n      ),\n      \"i know you've got a plan. we're waiting for a boat at the dock.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Ties directly to the track title and \"blubber\"\\'s nautical theme: trusting God\\'s rescue or voyage is scheduled, even while staring at an empty harbor.',\n        tags: ['nautical', 'refrain'],\n      ),\n      'how long will you make us wait? this is getting harder by the second.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Echoes the raw lament of the Psalms (\"How long, O Lord?\", Psalm 13:1)—faith that doesn\\'t sanitize impatience.',\n        tags: ['scripture', 'lament'],\n      ),\n      \"i know that i'm impatient but i also know that you're omnipotent.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'The heart of the dilemma: if God is all-powerful, why delay? Pairing \"impatient\" and \"omnipotent\" sharpens the human-vs-divine tension.',\n        tags: ['theology', 'wordplay'],\n      ),\n      'where am i needed? i hate these idle hands.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Alludes to the proverb \"idle hands are the devil\\'s workshop\"—restless to serve and feel useful rather than stuck waiting.',\n        tags: ['idiom', 'calling'],\n      ),\n      'what is my calling? what are your demands?': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Strips prayer down to direct, urgent questions—ready to obey if only the instructions were plain.',\n        tags: ['prayer', 'calling'],\n      ),\n      'we read your book everyday while we pray and cry and plead.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Shows that this isn\\'t casual doubt—he and his wife are genuinely seeking God in Scripture every single day.',\n        tags: ['theology', 'personal'],\n      ),\n      \"i hate to see her sad. i can't fix it. what do you want from me?\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'The emotional gut-punch of the track: his deepest ache isn\\'t just his own pain, it\\'s feeling powerless to lift the weight off his wife.',\n        tags: ['romance', 'heartfelt'],\n      ),\n      \"i'll shave my head. starve myself. whatever it takes.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Evokes Old Testament vows of fasting and shaving one\\'s head in mourning or devotion (Job 1:20, Acts 18:18)—offering extreme sacrifice just to break the silence.',\n        tags: ['scripture', 'desperation'],\n      ),\n      \"just to know you heard my voice. lord, i'm about to break.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Raw vulnerability at the breaking point—needing reassurance more than anything else.',\n        tags: ['lament', 'confessional'],\n      ),\n      \"i know you'll get us out of this rut. i can't wait to see how.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Starts with classic optimistic faith language—setting up a brutally honest clarification on the next line.',\n        tags: ['hope', 'setup'],\n      ),\n      'emphasis on \"can\\'t wait\". we\\'re going crazy. can it happen now?': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Reclaims the polite idiom \"I can\\'t wait\" literally—no, seriously, we cannot wait much longer.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'confessional'],\n      ),\n    },\n  ),\n  'specter': const TrackBreakdown(\n    overview:\n        'A nocturnal, Gothic-tinted fever dream of sleep deprivation, stale coffee, cigarette smoke, and eerie blue-screen hallucinations. Written in detached third-person until the final punchline (\"I ghost-wrote these sentences\"), \"specter\" turns a burned-out insomniac shuffling through his house into a literal phantom haunting his own life.',\n    tags: ['insomnia', 'gothic', 'imagery', 'wordplay'],\n    lineAnnotations: {\n      'white membrane worlds bulged out of his skull': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Surreal, unsettling anatomical imagery for bloodshot, exhausted eyes straining out of a sleep-deprived head.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'surreal'],\n      ),\n      'a cup of red-eye coffee with emerald mold': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'A \"red-eye\" is drip coffee spiked with an espresso shot (also evoking red-eye exhaustion); forgetting a mug long enough for green mold to grow signals deep burnout.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'double-entendre'],\n      ),\n      'joints stiffening while he shuffles around': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Zombie-like physical inertia after too many hours awake or slumped in front of a screen.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'gothic'],\n      ),\n      'dragging his feet to the beat of the clouds': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Moves in a slow, foggy drift disconnected from normal time.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'surreal'],\n      ),\n      'the mattress is calling like telephone rings': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Personifies exhaustion—bed beckoning persistently while his mind still won\\'t answer.',\n        tags: ['simile', 'insomnia'],\n      ),\n      'a classic red with a coiling spring': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Double visual linking a vintage red landline phone with a coiled cord AND an old innerspring mattress (plus a subtle nod to Marlboro Reds).',\n        tags: ['double-entendre', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      'monotonous monotone terrors on checkerboards': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Repetitive nighttime dread arranged like a black-and-white chess match or Twin Peaks floor—trapped in predictable mental loops.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'surreal'],\n      ),\n      'the moonlight falls safely with no need for bungee cords': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Playful, eerie contrast: moonlight drops effortlessly through the window while he feels perpetually on the edge of a plunge.',\n        tags: ['whimsical', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      'a zealot for nightmares. a phantom fanatic.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Alliterative F/P sounds cast him as a devoted worshipper of his own bad dreams—haunting his own waking hours.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'gothic'],\n      ),\n      \"there's bones in the closet and some in the attic.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Expands \"skeletons in the closet\" upward into the attic—suggesting repressed secrets and baggage packed into every corner of the mind.',\n        tags: ['idiom', 'metaphor'],\n      ),\n      'an omen for certain. it might be a wraith.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Deepens the ghost vocabulary (\"specter\", \"phantom\", \"wraith\"), blurring whether he\\'s seeing ghosts or becoming one.',\n        tags: ['gothic', 'motif'],\n      ),\n      'he prays the lord his soul to take.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Directly echoes the classic bedtime prayer \"Now I Lay Me Down to Sleep\" (\"if I should die before I wake, I pray the Lord my soul to take\")—here turning dark and weary.',\n        tags: ['theology', 'reference'],\n      ),\n      \"blue-light gaze into a snow-globe's heat wave\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Staring at a glowing phone or monitor screen in the dark, trapped inside a tiny sealed world (\"snow-globe\") that somehow feels suffocatingly hot.',\n        tags: ['tech-imagery', 'oxymoron'],\n      ),\n      'might be hazed, frontal lobe betrayed': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Points directly to the prefrontal cortex—the seat of impulse control and rational judgment—failing under exhaustion and haze.',\n        tags: ['psychology', 'mental-health'],\n      ),\n      'sugared periques make up his smile': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Perique is a famously strong, dark, pungent Louisiana tobacco (used in American Spirit Black packs)—implying heavy smoking staining his grin.',\n        tags: ['detail', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      \"if he had any foresight, he would've picked mild\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Self-mocking regret over choosing the harshest blend of tobacco—and metaphorically the hardest path in general.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'self-deprecation'],\n      ),\n      'haunted hellhounds hover over his head': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Five-word H-alliteration conjuring classic blues/gothic folklore (\"Hellhound on My Trail\") for relentless anxiety and guilt.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'gothic'],\n      ),\n      'maybe the eggshell-white paint contains lead': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Darkly funny attempt to blame his unraveling mind on old apartment lead paint rather than facing deeper inner turmoil.',\n        tags: ['dark-humor', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      'dreamscape dares or truths in the messages': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Plays on \"truth or dare\" inside feverish night visions—wondering whether the thoughts in his head are dares or hidden truths.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'surreal'],\n      ),\n      \"either one's the same, i ghost-wrote these sentences\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Mic-drop closing pun tying back to the title \"specter\": \"ghost-wrote\" works both as hip-hop terminology and as a spectral narrator writing from beyond the edge of burnout.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'closer'],\n      ),\n    },\n  ),\n  'tightrope': const TrackBreakdown(\n    overview:\n        'Arguably the heaviest, most haunting track on \"blubber.\" Told from the chilling perspective of a hallucinated \"figment\" sitting beside someone unconscious in a hospital bed (\"EKG beeps\", \"decided by doses\"), the track confronts overdose, self-destruction, and the razor-thin tightrope between sleep and death—closing with a devastating domestic morning image (\"Coffee\\'s brewing, bacon sizzles / I bought you some roses\") that the sleeper can no longer wake up to.',\n    tags: ['mental-health', 'somber', 'narrative', 'perspective'],\n    lineAnnotations: {\n      'the ekg beeps seep into your sleep.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Internal ee-rhymes (\"EKG\", \"beeps\", \"seep\", \"sleep\") mirror the steady rhythmic pulse of a hospital heart monitor.',\n        tags: ['internal-rhyme', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      \"i'd wake you up but i've never seen so much peace.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Heartbreaking tenderness laced with dread—reluctant to disturb a rare moment of quiet even under dire medical circumstances.',\n        tags: ['somber', 'contrast'],\n      ),\n      \"i'm a figment. your mind is wrecked.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Reveals the narrator\\'s eerie perspective: an imaginary voice inside a fractured, sedated consciousness.',\n        tags: ['perspective', 'surreal'],\n      ),\n      'crashed. existential side effects.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Uses both computing (\"crashed\") and prescription-label language (\"side effects\") for an emotional and physical collapse.',\n        tags: ['tech', 'mental-health'],\n      ),\n      'deflected insecurities. perplexing similarities.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Diagnoses defense mechanisms—pushing pain outward while noticing unsettling reflections of oneself in others.',\n        tags: ['psychology', 'wordplay'],\n      ),\n      'incomplete corpse. complex clarity.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Suspended between life and death (\"incomplete corpse\"), yet paradoxically seeing life with brutal lucidity.',\n        tags: ['oxymoron', 'somber'],\n      ),\n      'infrequently tuned frequencies': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Radio/audio-engineering metaphor for an erratic mind rarely dialed into the right station.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'metaphor'],\n      ),\n      'to free himself in secrecy.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Isolating oneself to chase private escape rather than letting anyone see the struggle.',\n        tags: ['isolation', 'mental-health'],\n      ),\n      'jumped the gun. offsides.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Sports-penalty metaphors (track false start + football offsides) for rushing recklessly past the boundary of life.',\n        tags: ['metaphor', 'wordplay'],\n      ),\n      'slumber is the penalty.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Completes the referee call—forced unconsciousness or coma as the consequence of jumping the gun.',\n        tags: ['somber', 'metaphor'],\n      ),\n      'most are deprived. but you overate.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Dark euphemism for taking too much—swallowing far beyond what the body can handle while others starve for relief.',\n        tags: ['metaphor', 'somber'],\n      ),\n      'loosen the belt and dull the blade.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Stark, compassionate plea to step back from self-harm and tension—softening the instruments of pain.',\n        tags: ['mental-health', 'somber'],\n      ),\n      'on a tightrope. decided by doses.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Names the track: balancing precariously between medicine and poison, determined by milligrams.',\n        tags: ['title-drop', 'mental-health'],\n      ),\n      'playing tug of war against death and hypnosis.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Pulled between fatal finality and numbed-out sedation—neither side truly being awake.',\n        tags: ['metaphor', 'somber'],\n      ),\n      'hiding signs from yourself. you want to wake up.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Self-deception collapsing at the last moment—recognizing too late that you actually want to live.',\n        tags: ['psychology', 'somber'],\n      ),\n      \"there's no re-entry. you lost your stub.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Concert/venue ticket metaphor (\"no re-entry without a stub\") made chillingly permanent—you can\\'t just walk back through the doors.',\n        tags: ['metaphor', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      'i hit the snooze button for you too many times.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'The figment confesses to enabling avoidance—repeatedly delaying the wake-up call.',\n        tags: ['metaphor', 'guilt'],\n      ),\n      \"maybe i'm reaching, i read between lines.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Self-aware hesitation, wondering if it\\'s over-interpreting unspoken cries for help.',\n        tags: ['idiom', 'reflection'],\n      ),\n      \"i like it in your head. it's so spacious.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Eerily wry remark from the imaginary companion—either mocking empty silence or the vast expanse of an overactive mind.',\n        tags: ['dark-humor', 'perspective'],\n      ),\n      'blamed it on god. does he ever blame us?': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'A stunning theological question amid crisis: humans routinely put God on trial for suffering, yet grace refuses to condemn us back.',\n        tags: ['theology', 'reflection'],\n      ),\n      \"coffee's brewing, bacon sizzles.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Warm, ordinary morning domesticity—reminding the listener of simple everyday joys worth waking up for.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'contrast'],\n      ),\n      'i bought you some roses.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'A tender romantic gesture that doubles uneasily as funeral flowers depending on whether the listener wakes up.',\n        tags: ['symbolism', 'somber'],\n      ),\n      \"i'm sorry i cant wake you up.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Because the narrator is only a figment of the mind, it has no power to pull the body back to consciousness.',\n        tags: ['perspective', 'somber'],\n      ),\n      'in my defense, you chose this.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Brutally unsentimental final line—forcing full accountability for walking out onto the tightrope in the first place.',\n        tags: ['closer', 'somber'],\n      ),\n    },\n  ),\n  'i swear, the fish was this big': const TrackBreakdown(\n    overview:\n        'The centerpiece narrative of \"blubber\"—retelling the entire Book of Jonah in twenty punchy lines while mapping Jonah\\'s stubbornness directly onto Archer\\'s own songwriting, faith, and resentment. From fleeing to Tarshish (\"home is in the rearview\") to screaming prayers inside the belly of the fish, getting vomited onto shore, preaching to Nineveh, and sulking when God withers his shade plant (Jonah 4), the title flips the miracle into a classic fisherman\\'s tall tale.',\n    tags: ['theology', 'jonah', 'narrative', 'humor'],\n    lineAnnotations: {\n      'given one job. walked out the first day.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Summarizes Jonah 1:1-3 with dry modern slang (\"you had one job\"): God sends Jonah to Nineveh, and Jonah immediately bolts in the opposite direction.',\n        tags: ['scripture', 'humor'],\n      ),\n      'they wont listen to anything that i say.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Captures both Jonah\\'s cynical excuse for skipping Nineveh and an independent artist\\'s fear that nobody hears his music.',\n        tags: ['meta', 'jonah'],\n      ),\n      \"so i'll dip out of here and hide, not knowing what i seek\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Running away without an actual destination—pure avoidance masquerading as escape.',\n        tags: ['jonah', 'confessional'],\n      ),\n      \"but i'll hit the ground running with alternating feet.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Playfully literal deadpan addition (\"with alternating feet\") to the cliché \"hit the ground running.\"',\n        tags: ['humor', 'idiom'],\n      ),\n      'stowed away. homeward bound but my home is in the rearview.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Jonah boarding the ship to Tarshish—convincing himself he\\'s heading toward safety while speeding further from where he belongs.',\n        tags: ['jonah', 'nautical'],\n      ),\n      \"it's a little inefficient but i can't see through what's not see-through.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Dry understatement for spiritual blindness—trying to navigate without seeing God\\'s bigger picture.',\n        tags: ['humor', 'wordplay'],\n      ),\n      \"i know it's terrifying. one way to stop this rain:\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Enters the raging tempest of Jonah 1:4-12, where the terrified sailors realize the storm is supernatural.',\n        tags: ['scripture', 'narrative'],\n      ),\n      \"walk the plank. overboard. i'm the one to blame.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Jonah owning his guilt and telling the sailors to throw him into the sea so the storm will calm (Jonah 1:12).',\n        tags: ['scripture', 'nautical'],\n      ),\n      'the belly of this fish is cold and damp and full of prayers i scream.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Jonah 2: hitting rock bottom inside the great fish—the very imagery that gives the album \"blubber\" its name.',\n        tags: ['scripture', 'title-motif'],\n      ),\n      \"i'll quit running away. i'm begging now. let me be redeemed.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Surrender at the bottom of the ocean—promising obedience in exchange for rescue and second chances.',\n        tags: ['theology', 'refrain'],\n      ),\n      \"puked out. god, i'm alive and i'm racing through these city streets.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Jonah 2:10–3:3 in vivid modern language: the fish vomits Jonah onto dry land, and he sprints straight into Nineveh.',\n        tags: ['scripture', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      \"should've listened in the first place or at least sent out a tweet.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Hilarious anachronism—wishing he could have just fired off a quick tweet warning Nineveh instead of getting swallowed by a whale.',\n        tags: ['humor', 'modern-life'],\n      ),\n      'they listened and they fell at the sound of your name.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Jonah 3:5-9: shockingly, the wicked city of Nineveh immediately repents in sackcloth and ashes.',\n        tags: ['scripture', 'narrative'],\n      ),\n      'no flames ignite or embers fall on this unholy place.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Unlike Sodom and Gomorrah, God spares Nineveh—withholding the judgment Jonah secretly wanted to watch.',\n        tags: ['scripture', 'theology'],\n      ),\n      \"you saw them change, you changed your mind but i'll be bitter until the end.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Jonah 4:1-3: Jonah is furious that God is merciful and forgives his enemies—exposing human petty resentment.',\n        tags: ['scripture', 'psychology'],\n      ),\n      'you give and take away. that plant was my last friend.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Merges Job 1:21 (\"the Lord gave and the Lord has taken away\") with Jonah 4:6-9, where Jonah melts down over a withered shade vine while caring nothing for a whole city.',\n        tags: ['scripture', 'humor'],\n      ),\n      'why do i write when the songs just go unheard?': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Drops the Jonah mask for a sudden, vulnerable line about pouring his heart into archBTW songs and feeling invisible.',\n        tags: ['meta', 'confessional'],\n      ),\n      'he said, \"there\\'s no pity where it\\'s undeserved\"': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Echoes God\\'s closing challenge to Jonah (Jonah 4:10-11), confronting self-pity and entitlement.',\n        tags: ['scripture', 'theology'],\n      ),\n      'do i do well to be angry? maybe not.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Directly quotes God\\'s piercing question in Jonah 4:4 (\"Is it right for you to be angry?\")—and unlike Jonah in the Bible, Archer actually softens and concedes.',\n        tags: ['scripture', 'growth'],\n      ),\n      'closed the door. slammed, in fact, but closure is an afterthought.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Mirrors the Book of Jonah\\'s famously abrupt open ending: slamming the door emotionally while realizing neat closure rarely arrives on demand.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'closer'],\n      ),\n    },\n  ),\n  'spouted (ft. christian rigdon)': const TrackBreakdown(\n    overview:\n        'The cathartic breakthrough of \"blubber\"—finally rising out of the belly of the whale (\"spouted\") into baptism, surrender, and honest worship. Archer opens up about bad habits, chasing distractions (\"talk to a lotus\"), and breaking harp strings while playing for Jesus, before handing the mic to guest vocalist Christian Rigdon for a blistering testimony verse that ties the Jonah arc directly to redemption through the Lamb.',\n    tags: ['theology', 'redemption', 'feature', 'jonah'],\n    lineAnnotations: {\n      \"i'm finally feeling good regardless of my situation.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Signals a genuine spiritual shift—echoing Paul\\'s contentment in Philippians 4:11 regardless of external circumstances.',\n        tags: ['hope', 'theology'],\n      ),\n      'the doctors said theyd fix me with bad enunciation.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Dry jab at rushed clinical appointments and unpronounceable pharmaceutical names promising an easy cure.',\n        tags: ['humor', 'mental-health'],\n      ),\n      \"money might be tight but i trust we'll dine like birds tonight.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Callbacks directly to \"we just need to budget better\" and Matthew 6:26—trusting God to provide even when pockets are thin.',\n        tags: ['callback', 'scripture'],\n      ),\n      'lies in limelights. the light of day through cloudy skies.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Contrasts fake stage-lit fame (\"lies in limelights\") with authentic daylight finally breaking through overcast weather.',\n        tags: ['contrast', 'wordplay'],\n      ),\n      \"raising our hands is not enough. i'll worship with these words\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Callbacks to \"Is that real wool?\" (\"raise your hands\")—moving past hollow gestures into honest songwriting as worship.',\n        tags: ['callback', 'theology'],\n      ),\n      'with an orchestra behind me, singing songs for each third.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Capitalized \"Third\" honors all three Persons of the Trinity (Father, Son, Holy Spirit) with full symphonic devotion.',\n        tags: ['theology', 'trinity'],\n      ),\n      'anointed with oil, submerged in a lake.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Classic biblical imagery of consecration (Psalm 23:5) and water baptism—also contrasting drowning in the sea with being submerged into new life.',\n        tags: ['scripture', 'baptism'],\n      ),\n      'can you really wash away all of my mistakes?': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Honest vulnerability at the water\\'s edge—marvelling that grace could actually erase a messy past.',\n        tags: ['theology', 'confessional'],\n      ),\n      \"heal me. save me from this person i've become.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Core chorus plea—recognizing the biggest enemy isn\\'t outside circumstances, it\\'s the broken self.',\n        tags: ['prayer', 'refrain'],\n      ),\n      '\"i wanna hear you too\", at the top of darkened lungs.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Smoking-stained (\"darkened\") lungs shouting back at heaven, desperate for mutual dialogue with God.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'refrain'],\n      ),\n      \"fix me, i'm shattered in pieces.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Unfiltered admission of brokenness—laying the shards plainly at God\\'s feet.',\n        tags: ['confessional', 'refrain'],\n      ),\n      'snapped harp and lyre strings while playing for jesus.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Alludes to King David playing the harp and lyre in the Psalms—strumming so passionately and imperfectly that the strings break.',\n        tags: ['scripture', 'music'],\n      ),\n      'a lot of bad habits inhabit this temple.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Puns on \"habits\" / \"inhabit\" while invoking 1 Corinthians 6:19 (\"your bodies are temples of the Holy Spirit\").',\n        tags: ['scripture', 'wordplay'],\n      ),\n      'out of the cardboard. ready to assemble.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Humorous IKEA-furniture metaphor for being rebuilt from scratch into something new.',\n        tags: ['humor', 'metaphor'],\n      ),\n      \"i get lost in the art and l can't focus.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Admits that even making music can become an idol or hyperfixation that pulls attention away from what matters most.',\n        tags: ['meta', 'confessional'],\n      ),\n      'i chase the wrong things. even tried to talk to a lotus.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'References flirting with Eastern mysticism / New Age symbolism (\"lotus\")—or psychedelics—while searching for answers in the wrong places.',\n        tags: ['theology', 'personal'],\n      ),\n      'you lead me home, no more loco locomotive.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Playful internal wordplay (\"loco\" = crazy / \"locomotive\" = runaway train) celebrating finally slowing down and heading home.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'hope'],\n      ),\n      'i tried to jump and roll while it was still in motion.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Describes reckless past attempts to bail out of his own runaway habits mid-speed.',\n        tags: ['metaphor', 'confessional'],\n      ),\n      \"i missed you more than life and i can't wait to see you after.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Tender, homesick longing for reunion with God in eternity.',\n        tags: ['theology', 'heartfelt'],\n      ),\n      'i think you missed me too. after all, you were my crafter.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Circles back to the Creator-craftsman theme (\"Carpenter\" on \"whale mail\", \"dust\" on \"ribs\")—imagining a Maker who misses His handiwork.',\n        tags: ['theology', 'callback'],\n      ),\n      '(christian rigdon)': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Marks the guest verse from featured artist Christian Rigdon, who picks up Archer\\'s Jonah narrative with an urgent, testimony-driven hip-hop cadence.',\n        tags: ['feature', 'structure'],\n      ),\n      'thinking back': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Christian opens his verse in reflective retrospect, rewinding to his own season of rebellion.',\n        tags: ['feature', 'testimony'],\n      ),\n      \"i didn't wanna go your way and so i hit the gas\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Mirrors Jonah\\'s flight in modern terms—flooring the pedal in the exact opposite direction of God\\'s call.',\n        tags: ['feature', 'jonah'],\n      ),\n      'the other way and went astray, and i was spitting raps': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Connects straying from faith with pouring his gift of lyricism into empty pursuits.',\n        tags: ['feature', 'meta'],\n      ),\n      \"chilling, i was kicking back, sinnin 'till i hit the mat\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Boxing/wrestling imagery (\"hit the mat\")—coasting casually in sin until life knocked him flat.',\n        tags: ['feature', 'rhyme-scheme'],\n      ),\n      'i went overboard with it': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Double meaning tying everyday excess (\"went overboard\") directly back to Jonah plunging off the ship.',\n        tags: ['feature', 'double-entendre'],\n      ),\n      'i saw my life, i was bored with it': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Names the hollow numbness underneath chasing thrills—boredom with a self-centered existence.',\n        tags: ['feature', 'confessional'],\n      ),\n      'thought that i could make it on my own': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'The classic prodigal illusion of total self-sufficiency.',\n        tags: ['feature', 'theology'],\n      ),\n      'never worked, did it?': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Rhetorical check-in that punctures pride in three blunt words.',\n        tags: ['feature', 'tone'],\n      ),\n      'hated everything that i was and wanted to kill me': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Unflinching testimony of hitting suicidal self-hatred at the bottom of the spiral.',\n        tags: ['feature', 'mental-health'],\n      ),\n      \"i even turned to the fallen one and i thought he'd heal me\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Admits looking to darkness / Satan (\"the fallen one\") for relief, only to discover the deception.',\n        tags: ['feature', 'theology'],\n      ),\n      'a fool with a hell-sent death wish': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Blunt self-assessment of how destructive that detour became.',\n        tags: ['feature', 'testimony'],\n      ),\n      \"now i'm sitting in a fish with regrets\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Lands squarely inside \"blubber\"\\'s central Jonah metaphor—trapped in the belly of consequence.',\n        tags: ['feature', 'jonah'],\n      ),\n      'i messed this whole thing up': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Stripped-back confession with zero excuses—just owning the wreckage.',\n        tags: ['feature', 'humility'],\n      ),\n      \"but a message i heard said it's never too late\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'The turning point of the verse: the Gospel breaking into despair.',\n        tags: ['feature', 'hope'],\n      ),\n      \"cuz there's a lamb who was slain for even the worst shame\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'References Revelation 5:12 and Isaiah 53—Christ as the sacrificial Lamb whose grace covers even the deepest shame.',\n        tags: ['feature', 'scripture'],\n      ),\n      'so i\\'m on my knees crying out \"can you fix me?\"': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Directly echoes Archer\\'s chorus (\"Fix me, I\\'m shattered in pieces\"), uniting both voices in the same prayer.',\n        tags: ['feature', 'callback'],\n      ),\n      \"i should've went to ninevah and shouted\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Explicitly names Nineveh—bringing the album\\'s Jonah thread full circle.',\n        tags: ['feature', 'jonah'],\n      ),\n      'when you sent me': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Acknowledges the cost of delayed obedience.',\n        tags: ['feature', 'theology'],\n      ),\n      'now im reaching out cuz im bout to go six feet down': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Urgent life-or-death reach before sinking permanently into the grave.',\n        tags: ['feature', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      'i need you now, spirit spout, come and cleanse me': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Brilliant closer merging the whale\\'s blowhole (\"spout\", tying to the title \"spouted\") with the cleansing waters of the Holy Spirit.',\n        tags: ['feature', 'title-drop'],\n      ),\n    },\n  ),\n  'before the before': const TrackBreakdown(\n    overview:\n        'The cosmic, childlike, philosophically curious closer to \"blubber.\" Rewinding all the way past Jonah, past Eden, to before Genesis 1:1 (\"No stars or moon or glimpse of light\"), Archer asks God the big late-night questions—predestination vs. free will, math and magic, whether God ever got bored in the void—before landing on humble, honest unknowing: \"Will anything ever be something I know?\"',\n    tags: ['theology', 'philosophy', 'genesis', 'closer'],\n    lineAnnotations: {\n      'no stars or moon or glimpse of light': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Sets the scene before Genesis 1:3 (\"Let there be light\")—total pre-creation darkness.',\n        tags: ['scripture', 'opener'],\n      ),\n      \"what's your angle, there's not a shape in sight.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Clever geometric pun on \"What\\'s your angle?\" (both \"what\\'s your motive?\" and literal geometry before space or shapes even existed).',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'philosophy'],\n      ),\n      'it can all change in a couple of days.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Alludes to the six days of Creation in Genesis 1—going from empty void to a living universe almost overnight.',\n        tags: ['scripture', 'genesis'],\n      ),\n      'a couple dimensions. plants that glaze.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Blends physics (fabricating spacetime dimensions) with botanical creation—plants glistening with morning dew (or resin).',\n        tags: ['science', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      \"i can't imagine. what was it like in the void?\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Genuine awe at God\\'s eternal existence outside time and matter before Creation began.',\n        tags: ['theology', 'wonder'],\n      ),\n      'were you ever bored or did you play with toys?': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Disarmingly childlike curiosity—imagining an eternal Creator inventing galaxies out of sheer playful joy.',\n        tags: ['humor', 'wonder'],\n      ),\n      'do you ever pray? if so, then why?': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'A sharp theological riddle—actually nodding to the Gospels where Jesus Himself prays to the Father.',\n        tags: ['theology', 'philosophy'],\n      ),\n      'sometimes i talk to myself when i lie.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Double meaning on \"lie\": lying awake in bed talking to himself AND rehearsing self-deceptions aloud.',\n        tags: ['double-entendre', 'confessional'],\n      ),\n      'how did you come up with math and magic?': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Wonders at a universe governed simultaneously by rigorous mathematical laws and inexplicable beauty/miracles.',\n        tags: ['philosophy', 'refrain'],\n      ),\n      'i had all the same asks before all the acid.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Clarifies that his cosmic questioning isn\\'t just drug-induced stoner philosophy—those existential questions lived in him long before psychedelics.',\n        tags: ['confessional', 'humor'],\n      ),\n      'serpents with fruit in a beautiful garden.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Jumps straight to Genesis 3 and the Fall—contrasting Eden\\'s beauty with the moment everything fractured.',\n        tags: ['scripture', 'refrain'],\n      ),\n      \"the good and the bad. i hope that we're pardoned.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'References the Tree of the Knowledge of Good and Evil (Genesis 2:17) and closes the thought in quiet hope for forgiveness.',\n        tags: ['scripture', 'hope'],\n      ),\n      'predetermined free will. questions on questions.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Names theology\\'s oldest paradox (divine sovereignty vs. human free will) in a tight two-word oxymoron.',\n        tags: ['theology', 'philosophy'],\n      ),\n      \"am i a robot or not? what's the lesson?\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Software-engineer framing of determinism: if everything is foreknown, are we autonomous agents or just executing code?',\n        tags: ['tech', 'philosophy'],\n      ),\n      'left in the dark, searching for the light switch.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Mirrors the pre-creation darkness of line 1 on a personal scale—fumbling around trying to understand life.',\n        tags: ['metaphor', 'callback'],\n      ),\n      \"the world won't respond to my voice or my crisis.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Captures the indifference of the material universe when you cry out into it.',\n        tags: ['existential', 'confessional'],\n      ),\n      \"i accept and give up but i'll still overthink.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Honest self-portrait: surrendering control in faith doesn\\'t magically turn off an analytical, overthinking brain.',\n        tags: ['self-aware', 'mental-health'],\n      ),\n      \"you gave me that trait so i don't lip sync.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Reframes overthinking as a gift—insisting on writing authentic, lived-in lyrics rather than mouthing someone else\\'s canned answers.',\n        tags: ['meta', 'theology'],\n      ),\n      \"one more question and i'll let you go.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Ends the album like a late-night phone call with God, reluctant to hang up.',\n        tags: ['epistolary', 'closer'],\n      ),\n      'will anything ever be something i know?': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Socratic humility at the close of \"blubber\"—accepting mystery and stepping out of certainty into trust.',\n        tags: ['philosophy', 'closer'],\n      ),\n    },\n  ),\n};\n",
  "lib/pages/music/annotations/lifes_lemons_annotations.dart": "import 'package:archbtw_sh/pages/music/lyric_annotations.dart';\n\nfinal Map<String, TrackBreakdown> lifesLemonsAnnotations = {\n  'it seemed like a good idea at the time': const TrackBreakdown(\n    overview:\n        'A sharp, self-deprecating thesis statement opening the 13-track album \"life\\'s lemons\" (\"under 13 revisions\"). Preempting critics by roasting himself first—calling himself \"a make believe ego with no self-esteem\" and \"a prick who wrote a couple good songs\"—Archer frames the record as an unfiltered musical diary set over rhythmic collisions, squeezing sharp humor out of life\\'s sour moments.',\n    tags: ['opener', 'meta', 'confessional', 'wordplay'],\n    lineAnnotations: {\n      \"this'll probably end up in a cringe compilation\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Preemptively roasts his own vulnerability—echoing his About page confession about looking back on his old SoundCloud rap days as cringe.',\n        tags: ['self-deprecation', 'opener'],\n      ),\n      'with my societal state-wide violations': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Exaggerates social awkwardness and oversharing as full-blown legal infractions.',\n        tags: ['hyperbole', 'humor'],\n      ),\n      'sarcastic kamikaze, humor swirling in the dryer': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Describes self-destructive comedy (\"kamikaze\")—tossing his ego into a tumble-dry spin cycle just to get a laugh.',\n        tags: ['metaphor', 'humor'],\n      ),\n      \"the line punched me but i'll never be a liar\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Inverts \"punchline\" so the bar hits the writer himself—insisting the confessional honesty still stings because it\\'s true.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'confessional'],\n      ),\n      \"so i'm altering my frown into a big chagrin\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Subverts \"turn that frown upside down\": instead of a real grin, he only manages \"chagrin\" (embarrassed grimace, literally containing the word \"grin\").',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'subversion'],\n      ),\n      \"no more melancholy, only life's lemons\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Title drop for the album—leaning into the \"when life gives you lemons\" proverb by turning bitterness into tart, punchy songs.',\n        tags: ['title-drop', 'theme'],\n      ),\n      'thought i was a poet, i forgot my place.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Checks his own artistic pretensions with wry humility.',\n        tags: ['self-deprecation', 'meta'],\n      ),\n      'nobody believes all the goats i scape': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Cleverly splits \"scapegoat\" into a verb phrase (\"goats I scape\")—admitting people see right through his excuses.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'self-aware'],\n      ),\n      \"maybe i'll redeem myself or maybe i'll receive\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Sets up a retail/theological pun on \"redeem\" (salvation vs. returning merchandise).',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'setup'],\n      ),\n      \"tried to return it but i lost my soul's receipt\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Pays off the \"redeem\" setup: wishing he could exchange his flawed soul at customer service, only to realize he lost the receipt.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'humor'],\n      ),\n      'to my confidant, my confidence is too condescending': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Tight con-prefix wordplay (\"confidant\", \"confidence\", \"condescending\") unpacking how insecurity often masks itself as arrogance.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'alliteration'],\n      ),\n      'all pretend but i come across as just too pretentious': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Continues the root-word chain (\"pretend\" / \"pretentious\"): imposter syndrome wearing a snobbish disguise.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'confessional'],\n      ),\n      \"i'm just connecting these dots with a combative complex\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Alliterative hard-C sounds illustrate an over-analytical mind turning pattern recognition into an argument.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'psychology'],\n      ),\n      'oratorical flex in a conceptual test': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Deliberately deploys oversized, polysyllabic vocabulary purely to set up the self-mocking punchline on the very next bar.',\n        tags: ['meta', 'setup'],\n      ),\n      'is that line okay or are the words too long?': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Breaks the fourth wall immediately after flexing \"oratorical\" and \"conceptual,\" poking fun at lyrical over-engineering.',\n        tags: ['meta', 'humor'],\n      ),\n      \"i'm really just a prick who wrote a couple good songs\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Bluntly deflates his own mystique—equal parts brutal self-deprecation and quiet pride in the catalog.',\n        tags: ['self-deprecation', 'meta'],\n      ),\n      \"i'm probably digging myself a deeper hole\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Acknowledges that oversharing on wax usually creates more vulnerability, not less.',\n        tags: ['idiom', 'confessional'],\n      ),\n      'trying to put the words into sleeperholds': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Pro-wrestling submission metaphor (\"sleeperhold\") for wrestling unruly syllables into submission on the page.',\n        tags: ['metaphor', 'craft'],\n      ),\n      'a make believe ego with no self-esteem': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'A razor-sharp one-line diagnosis of bravado rap: loud swagger built over paper-thin confidence.',\n        tags: ['confessional', 'contrast'],\n      ),\n      'but honestly, i do sing myself to sleep': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Drops the tough-guy pose entirely—revealing that writing and humming songs is literally how he self-soothes at night.',\n        tags: ['confessional', 'heartfelt'],\n      ),\n      'so i hope you consider this my apology': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Offers the whole track as an advance disclaimer before the listener dives into the rest of the album.',\n        tags: ['meta', 'opener'],\n      ),\n      \"i'm always trying to be one step ahead of me\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Self-consciousness as a race against yourself—trying to criticize your own flaws before anyone else gets the chance.',\n        tags: ['psychology', 'self-aware'],\n      ),\n      \"i'll take the first shot with the letters i scribble\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Confirms the preemptive self-roast strategy: firing the opening volley at himself with his own notebook.',\n        tags: ['metaphor', 'meta'],\n      ),\n      \"i'd fight myself back but my bones are too brittle\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Admits he can dish out harsh self-criticism far better than he can absorb it.',\n        tags: ['vulnerability', 'humor'],\n      ),\n      \"i'll read my own diary over rhythmic collisions\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Echoes his bio almost verbatim (\"pretty much my diary\")—confessional journaling laid over indie/hip-hop percussion.',\n        tags: ['meta', 'personal'],\n      ),\n      \"there's a lot to unpack under 13 revisions\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Directly references the 13 tracks of \"life\\'s lemons,\" treating each song as another draft of unpacking his own head.',\n        tags: ['meta', 'structure'],\n      ),\n    },\n  ),\n  'elixir': const TrackBreakdown(\n    overview:\n        'A stinging, visually dense portrait of a fracturing relationship wrapped in astrology-and-crystal aesthetics (\"amethyst\", \"chakras\") and modern social-media performance (\"TikTok enhancing\", \"dopamine hits\"). Contrasting cozy winter memories with cold silent treatments and quiet score-keeping, Archer dissects how intimacy curdles into mutual surveillance and curated outrage.',\n    tags: ['breakup', 'modern-life', 'imagery', 'wordplay'],\n    lineAnnotations: {\n      \"i'm a silent treatment agonist.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Pharmacology/biochemistry term (\"agonist\" = a chemical that activates a receptor, plus echoing \"antagonist\")—admitting he triggers or escalates cold-shoulder standoffs.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'confessional'],\n      ),\n      'a violent, greedy alchemist.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Connects to the title \"elixir\"—trying desperately to transmute toxic emotions into something golden, yet making things worse.',\n        tags: ['title-motif', 'metaphor'],\n      ),\n      'amethyst, channeling, chakras aligned.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Evokes curated New Age wellness aesthetics—healing crystals and spiritual buzzwords masking unresolved tension underneath.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'satire'],\n      ),\n      \"panning the camera, there's red to the right.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Cinematic reveal: step slightly outside the serene, curated frame and the red flags (or spilled blood/anger) immediately come into view.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'contrast'],\n      ),\n      'the snowfall drift keeps us glued to our bed.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Starts with an idyllic snowed-in memory—intimate warmth trapped indoors together.',\n        tags: ['romance', 'setup'],\n      ),\n      \"it used to be so cozy 'til we ripped it to shreds.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Shatters the warmth in half a line—turning the sanctuary of the bed into the battlefield of a breakup.',\n        tags: ['contrast', 'breakup'],\n      ),\n      'deletion of memories, precious and fragile,': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Tech phrasing (\"deletion\") for trying to erase shared photos, texts, and tender history.',\n        tags: ['tech', 'breakup'],\n      ),\n      'while gathering evidence. slow game and agile.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Captures the chilling shift from lovers to courtroom adversaries—quietly screenshotting receipts for future arguments.',\n        tags: ['psychology', 'breakup'],\n      ),\n      'circles get broken or bent into ovals.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Geometric metaphor for social circles fracturing or relationships warping slowly out of shape.',\n        tags: ['metaphor', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      'astounded with sonder. no longer the chosen.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            '\"Sonder\" (coined by John Koenig) is the sudden realization that every passerby lives a life as complex as your own—humbling someone who used to feel uniquely special.',\n        tags: ['vocabulary', 'reflection'],\n      ),\n      'centered by cubes. forgetting specifics.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Rigid, boxy routine or screen geometry crowding out the nuanced memories of who they used to be.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'geometric'],\n      ),\n      'cuneiform words with eyes hieroglyphic.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Ancient indecipherable scripts (Mesopotamian cuneiform + Egyptian hieroglyphs)—two people speaking and staring at each other without being able to read one another anymore.',\n        tags: ['metaphor', 'historical-reference'],\n      ),\n      'inaudible whispers of curses and damning': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Muttered resentment under the breath—too quiet to confront directly, too bitter to hide.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'conflict'],\n      ),\n      'partially filtered for tiktok enhancing.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Skewers algorithm-friendly self-censorship and beauty filters—polishing real ugliness for short-form social media clout.',\n        tags: ['modern-life', 'satire'],\n      ),\n      'ascension in pitch to viola strings picked.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Pizzicato strings climbing higher in pitch—mirroring escalating tension like a thriller film score.',\n        tags: ['music', 'tension'],\n      ),\n      'refreshing our screens for our dopamine hits.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Pull-to-refresh addiction numbing heartbreak with tiny algorithmic jolts instead of real healing.',\n        tags: ['modern-life', 'tech'],\n      ),\n      'deconstructed sentences and destructed sentiments.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Tight phonetic pairing (\"deconstructed\" / \"destructed\", \"sentences\" / \"sentiments\") showing how nitpicking every word kills the love behind them.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'breakup'],\n      ),\n      'disrupted innocence with words of cinnamon.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Words that look warm and sweet-spiced on the surface yet burn on contact.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'contrast'],\n      ),\n      'inhaling inflation. deflated defeat.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Breath/balloon pun (\"inhaling\" / \"inflation\" / \"deflated\") linking economic pressure and inflated egos with total collapse.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'metaphor'],\n      ),\n      'delayed his responses with plague on his teeth': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Stalling replies while bitter, venomous words rot behind clenched teeth (also a sly nod to dental \"plaque\" / \"plague\").',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'closer'],\n      ),\n    },\n  ),\n  \"third time's a charm\": const TrackBreakdown(\n    overview:\n        'A smoky, fluorescent-lit portrait of gambling compulsion—equating Vegas slot machines (\"Circus²\", sticky seats, repetitive sevens) with phone-screen penny-stock trading (\"refreshing penny stocks\"). Capturing the brutal psychology of near-misses (\"an almost perfect row but the third one\\'s too askew\"), Archer grounds the casino haze in everyday broke reality with the dry closer about expired car tags.',\n    tags: ['addiction', 'gambling', 'satire', 'realism'],\n    lineAnnotations: {\n      'tired eyes turn from their casino game daze.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Drops us onto a dimly lit casino floor where hours blur together in hypnotic trance.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'opener'],\n      ),\n      'ashtrays and crumpled napkins with makeup stains.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Gritty sensory clutter evoking stale cigarette smoke, cheap cocktails, and fading glamour.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'realism'],\n      ),\n      'ante up, surely your luck is bound to change.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Voices the classic Gambler\\'s Fallacy—convincing yourself the next spin is finally \"due.\"',\n        tags: ['psychology', 'gambling'],\n      ),\n      'the panic attacks you feel are nothing but phantom pains.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Denial talking: brushing off genuine financial dread as an imaginary itch.',\n        tags: ['mental-health', 'denial'],\n      ),\n      \"there's adhesives on the seats with some sort of residue.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Literally sticky casino stools—and figuratively how casinos are engineered to glue players to their chairs.',\n        tags: ['metaphor', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      \"you tell yourself it's not but even that's see-through.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Double meaning on \"see-through\": transparent grime and totally transparent self-deception.',\n        tags: ['double-entendre', 'psychology'],\n      ),\n      'chimes of failure accompany dreams to nose-dive.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Irony of upbeat slot-machine jingles ringing merrily even as bank accounts plummet.',\n        tags: ['contrast', 'gambling'],\n      ),\n      'are you a black sheep or just a goat telling white lies?': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Packs three color/animal idioms into one bar: \"black sheep\" (outcast), \"goat\" (stubborn/fall guy, or GOAT), and \"white lies\" (excuses told to justify one more bet).',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'idiom'],\n      ),\n      '10th cup of colombian, refreshing penny stocks.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Bridges brick-and-mortar casinos with modern retail trading apps—jittery on coffee, gambling on volatile penny stocks.',\n        tags: ['modern-life', 'addiction'],\n      ),\n      'the new york minutes pass but not the petty thoughts.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Ties \"New York minute\" directly to Wall Street speed while noting that anxious resentment lingers much longer.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'idiom'],\n      ),\n      'you won three cents but you lost 3 bucks': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Classic slot-machine psychology (\"losses disguised as wins\"): celebrating a tiny chime payout while steadily bleeding cash.',\n        tags: ['gambling', 'realism'],\n      ),\n      \"and you can't cash out unless the balance is up.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Names both predatory app withdrawal minimums and the psychological trap of refusing to walk away in the red.',\n        tags: ['gambling', 'psychology'],\n      ),\n      'negligently negative. the sevens are repetitive.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Bank balance in the red while lucky 7s flash past on spinning reels—also referenced directly in the \"lifes_lemons.sh\" puzzle game!',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'easter-egg'],\n      ),\n      'cherry on top of cherry-flavored sedatives.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Links classic slot-machine cherry symbols with cough-syrup/candy-coated numbness keeping the player zoned out.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'gambling'],\n      ),\n      \"we know you want to leave but this next one's on the house.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'The casino\\'s oldest trick—free comped drinks or bonus spins designed to keep you right at the machine.',\n        tags: ['gambling', 'satire'],\n      ),\n      'if you really need a break, you can just crash on the couch.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Insists you never leave the premises—turning hospitality into captivity.',\n        tags: ['satire', 'addiction'],\n      ),\n      'circus², flamingos make for slowly dying wishes.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Clever Las Vegas math pun: \"Circus²\" = Circus Circus, paired with The Flamingo hotel—iconic faded Strip landmarks where big dreams slowly bleed out.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'pop-culture'],\n      ),\n      'cycled names and numbers, pining to push the switches.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Captures the tactile dopamine itch of pulling levers, tapping spin buttons, and watching numbers roll.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'addiction'],\n      ),\n      \"an almost perfect row but the third one's too askew.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'The devastating near-miss effect (two sevens lined up, the third one notch off)—directly mocking the track title \"third time\\'s a charm.\"',\n        tags: ['title-motif', 'gambling'],\n      ),\n      \"but hey man, life's a bitch. eventually you'll get your tags renewed.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Hilariously deflating Oklahoma/working-class reality check: chasing Vegas jackpots while driving around on expired car registration tags.',\n        tags: ['humor', 'closer'],\n      ),\n    },\n  ),\n  'i may not be a smart man but i know what love is': const TrackBreakdown(\n    overview:\n        'Titled after Tom Hanks\\'s iconic line in \"Forrest Gump,\" this track is a dazzling technical showcase of cascading single-letter alliteration—moving through M, N, P, T, W, I, L, B, and C stanzas like a tongue-twister fever dream. Beneath the acrobatic soundplay, it wrestles with manufactured desire, commodified attraction (\"patented hotties\", \"porcelain princess\"), guilt, and the confusion between real love and hollow obsession.',\n    tags: ['alliteration', 'pop-culture', 'wordplay', 'technical'],\n    lineAnnotations: {\n      'mega meta-metaphor, metabolizing my muse.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Opens with a pure six-word M-alliteration flex—self-referentially devouring his own inspiration and converting it straight into layered metaphors.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'meta'],\n      ),\n      'machine-made madness magically maintaining the mood.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Sustains the M-chain to describe synthetic beats and frantic mental loops keeping the atmosphere electrically charged.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'tech'],\n      ),\n      'nightly ninja, no name, never knowingly nodding.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Pivots cleanly to N-alliteration—late-night stealthy insomnia, wide awake and anonymous in the dark.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'insomnia'],\n      ),\n      'plastered polaroid pictures of patented hotties.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Shifts to P-alliteration, critiquing pin-up walls and commodified, trademarked standards of attractiveness.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'critique'],\n      ),\n      'pining for some playtime with a porcelain princess': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Paints idealized desire as chasing a fragile doll (\"porcelain princess\") rather than a real human being.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'metaphor'],\n      ),\n      'or platinum-plated plastic plugs peddle as incense.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Continuing the breathless P-run—skewering fake luxury trinkets and cheap vices marketed as something sacred or aromatic.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'satire'],\n      ),\n      'placed on a pedestal or pressed in the pages.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Contrasts idolizing someone unrealistically (\"pedestal\") with flattening them into a keepsake memory (\"pressed in the pages\").',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'romance'],\n      ),\n      'preserved and presented with the piss-stains that he painted.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Intentionally jarring coarse contrast puncturing the pretty \"porcelain princess\" romanticism with ugly human mess.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'contrast'],\n      ),\n      'trophy for the tragedy, true trauma, and the triumph.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Switches to T-alliteration, mocking how modern culture hands out badges for both pain and victory alike.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'irony'],\n      ),\n      \"those who trust in traitors' treason, drama, and die-cuts.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Pairs betrayal (\"traitors\\' treason\") with mass-produced stickers (\"die-cuts\")—shallow loyalties stamped out on demand.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'critique'],\n      ),\n      'willow wilting westward while we wallow along.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Soft W-alliteration shifts the tempo into mournful weeping-willow melancholy.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      'totally together. twist, totaled and tarred.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Abruptly snaps back to hard T-consonants—mirroring a sudden car-wreck plot twist (\"totaled\") ruining the togetherness.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'contrast'],\n      ),\n      'imported indigo intimates increment inches and influence idiots.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Staggering eight-word I-alliteration lampooning high-priced lingerie/fashion hype (\"imported indigo intimates\") manipulating gullible buyers.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'satire'],\n      ),\n      'lividly losing lucidity. liquidly lusted and lovingly lit it up.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Fluid L-alliteration mimics slipping out of rational control into intoxicated infatuation.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'technical'],\n      ),\n      \"he's basically blissful with blasphemy.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'B-alliteration spotlighting the guilty thrill of chasing forbidden things while pretending there\\'s no cost.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'theology'],\n      ),\n      'puts it politely when praying protectively.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'P-alliteration captures sanitizing your prayers—asking God for safety while keeping your sins politely hidden.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'theology'],\n      ),\n      \"cautiously, captured cadaver's complexion.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Enters the closing C-alliteration sequence with pale, lifeless imagery—emotional numbness setting in.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      'curtain-closed cinema, coma concession.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Double play on \"concession\" (movie-theater snack stand AND surrendering into a mental coma after the show ends).',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'double-entendre'],\n      ),\n      \"confusion creates all the colors we can't.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Poetic flash amidst the tongue-twister: chaos and uncertainty conjure vivid emotional shades that neat logic never could.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'poetic'],\n      ),\n      'conclusively, calling all cars and all hands.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Merges police dispatch (\"calling all cars\") with nautical emergency (\"all hands on deck\") for a punchy alliterative sign-off.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'closer'],\n      ),\n    },\n  ),\n  'almost intelligent': const TrackBreakdown(\n    overview:\n        'A razor-sharp, prescient DevOps-engineer critique of generative AI and LLM companionship. Mocking AI\\'s \"temperature\" knobs, \\\$20 subscription tiers, and training corpora scraped from dead authors (\"lofty Ouija goals\"), Archer cuts deeper than tech satire—asking whether outsourcing poetry, code, and intimacy to machines is modern idolatry (\"automate His rival\") born from crushing human loneliness.',\n    tags: ['tech', 'ai', 'theology', 'satire'],\n    lineAnnotations: {\n      'artificial friends but firmly grounded enemies.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Flips \"Artificial Intelligence\" into \"Artificial friends\" while warning that the real-world adversaries profiting off it are very real—and \"grounded\" adds an electrical-engineering pun.',\n        tags: ['tech', 'wordplay'],\n      ),\n      'look out for the incisiors and enter the anemone.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Natural-world trap imagery (sharp teeth + stinging sea anemone, plus a slant-rhyme echo of \"enemy\")—inviting yet venomous once you step inside.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      'algorithmic synapes emulating fallen souls.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Neural networks mimicking human neurons—and human flaws—because they learn from fallen humanity.',\n        tags: ['tech', 'theology'],\n      ),\n      'trained on dead words with lofty ouija goals.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Standout bar comparing LLM training data (billions of texts by deceased writers) to a digital Ouija board summoning ghosts on command.',\n        tags: ['ai', 'metaphor'],\n      ),\n      \"this one is too fun so let's lower its temperature.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Insider ML reference: \"temperature\" controls randomness/creativity in LLM sampling—companies dialing it down to keep models corporate-safe and predictable.',\n        tags: ['ai', 'tech'],\n      ),\n      \"raise it back up a bit because it's getting too sinister.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Jokes about frantically tweaking model hyperparameters as the output swings unpredictably between sterile and creepy.',\n        tags: ['ai', 'humor'],\n      ),\n      '\"please analyze my poems and write me out some code\".': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Hilariously self-aware prompt directly reflecting Archer\\'s own two worlds—songwriting and software engineering—outsourced to a chat box.',\n        tags: ['meta', 'tech'],\n      ),\n      'is this worship of a man-made brain or do we all just feel alone?': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'The philosophical heart of the track: is the AI obsession hubris or just a symptom of an epidemic of loneliness?',\n        tags: ['philosophy', 'confessional'],\n      ),\n      'you could probably get a girlfriend or one could just be downloaded.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Targets the booming AI-companion app market substituting frictionless code for messy real-life love.',\n        tags: ['ai', 'satire'],\n      ),\n      \"why's it taste so sour when the words are sugar-coated?\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Captures sycophantic AI flattery—endlessly polite, affirming outputs that still leave a hollow, bitter (\"lemons\") taste behind.',\n        tags: ['contrast', 'ai'],\n      ),\n      \"god's probably not too pleased. idle hands worshipping idols.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Sharp homophone (\"idle\" / \"idols\") linking automation-induced idleness with Old Testament idolatry—bowing down to things crafted by human hands.',\n        tags: ['theology', 'wordplay'],\n      ),\n      'we want to see his face and yet we automate his rival.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Frames building an all-knowing artificial oracle as a modern Tower of Babel—trying to manufacture a synthetic god instead of seeking the real one.',\n        tags: ['theology', 'ai'],\n      ),\n      'choose a personality to make your friend your own.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Parodies system-prompt customization screens—picking traits from a dropdown menu instead of accepting another person\\'s autonomy.',\n        tags: ['satire', 'ai'],\n      ),\n      'it has a decent memory and can talk you through your lows.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Nods to LLM context windows/memory features quietly replacing human confidants and therapists.',\n        tags: ['ai', 'mental-health'],\n      ),\n      r\"did you see the newest update? it's only \$20\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Direct jab at the ubiquitous \\\$20/month AI Pro subscription tier (with a clever rhyme setup on \"dollar\" in the next line—pronouncing \"\\\$20\" as \"twenty dollars\").',\n        tags: ['satire', 'tech'],\n      ),\n      \"but you're too inefficient to wear any hues of collar.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Chilling labor critique: neither blue-collar nor white-collar workers (\"any hues of collar\") feel safe from being deemed \"inefficient\" by automation.',\n        tags: ['anti-capitalism', 'wordplay'],\n      ),\n      \"we can't afford therapy or food 'cause we are not eligible.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Exposes the dystopian irony of cutting-edge AI thriving while basic healthcare and groceries stay locked behind means-testing and layoffs.',\n        tags: ['social-commentary', 'realism'],\n      ),\n      \"we built our own demise in cyberspace. it's inevitable.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Echoes classic sci-fi fatalism (Matrix/Terminator)—humanity enthusiastically engineering its own obsolescence.',\n        tags: ['sci-fi', 'tech'],\n      ),\n      \"was this written my machines? it's getting so hard to tell.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Wry meta-irony (even leaving the human typo \"my\" for \"by\" intact, ironically proving a human actually typed it!).',\n        tags: ['meta', 'humor'],\n      ),\n      'ceasefire with brimstone. the final war before hell.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Closes on apocalyptic Revelation imagery—comparing humanity\\'s uneasy truce with unchecked technology to the calm right before judgment.',\n        tags: ['theology', 'closer'],\n      ),\n    },\n  ),\n  'midnight oil': const TrackBreakdown(\n    overview:\n        'An atmospheric, hyper-specific vignette of acute insomnia lying wide awake beside a peacefully sleeping partner until sunrise. Blending medication references (Mirtazapine, Benadryl), 90s sitcom reruns, 4:20 humor (\"40 til 20\"), and staring at a lonely bedroom light fixture until morning breaks, Archer captures the surreal tenderness and madness of surviving the whole night without closing your eyes.',\n    tags: ['insomnia', 'romance', 'imagery', 'mental-health'],\n    lineAnnotations: {\n      'her breathing sets the mood while his dreams of dreams diminish': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'The steady rhythm of his sleeping partner contrasts with his fading hope of ever falling asleep himself (\"dreams of dreams\").',\n        tags: ['insomnia', 'opener'],\n      ),\n      \"as he's flipping through his rolodex of all of her best skin flicks.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Cheeky, restless mind wandering through private romantic memories of her like a vintage desktop Rolodex.',\n        tags: ['romance', 'humor'],\n      ),\n      'freeze-framed his memories. between the spokes he gathered magic.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Like glimpsing flashes of light through a spinning bicycle wheel or ceiling fan—savoring fleeting moments of stillness.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'poetic'],\n      ),\n      'pre-gamed a little early. 40 til 20 and then cashed it.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Clock-watching stoner wordplay: counting from 3:40 to 4:20 (\"40 til 20\") and finishing the bowl (\"cashed it\") while the rest of the world sleeps.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'humor'],\n      ),\n      \"mathematics on the mind but he won't look at the clock.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Every insomniac\\'s rule: refuse to check the time because calculating \"if I fall asleep right now I\\'ll get 3 hours\" only makes it worse.',\n        tags: ['insomnia', 'realism'],\n      ),\n      \"there's a permanent solution but he wrote it in chalk.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'A chilling flash of dark intrusive thought (\"permanent solution\") deliberately rendered erasable (\"written in chalk\")—acknowledging the impulse without letting it become permanent.',\n        tags: ['mental-health', 'metaphor'],\n      ),\n      'hours pass and eyes are glass. the ceiling has a story.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Glazed-over eyes projecting patterns and narratives onto textured drywall in the dark.',\n        tags: ['insomnia', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      \"if you stare into the center long enough, it's not so boring.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Hypnotic sleep-deprived boredom turning a plain bedroom ceiling into a strange optical illusion.',\n        tags: ['insomnia', 'detail'],\n      ),\n      'a half-assed chandelier or just a bulb trying its best?': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Hilariously relatable 3 AM thought: gently defending a humble apartment ceiling light (\"just a bulb trying its best\").',\n        tags: ['humor', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      'oscillating voices, vices. anything besides rest.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Pairs the swiveling hum of an oscillating bedroom fan with racing thoughts and late-night habits.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'insomnia'],\n      ),\n      'mirtazipine and candlewax - his favorite nightly snack.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Mirtazapine (Remeron) is a sedating antidepressant commonly prescribed for insomnia and appetite—paired absurdly with scented bedroom candlewax.',\n        tags: ['mental-health', 'detail'],\n      ),\n      'staring at the hardwood floors, counting each crack.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Classic sleepless ritual—counting floorboard seams like sheep that never work.',\n        tags: ['insomnia', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      'rosehips and chamomile, replaying 90s sitcoms.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Every sleepytime tea ingredient and comfort rerun (Seinfeld, Frasier, Friends) thrown at a stubbornly awake brain.',\n        tags: ['realism', 'pop-culture'],\n      ),\n      'black widows, benadryl, and her vanilla lip balm.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Nods to the infamous internet lore of high-dose Benadryl causing spider hallucinations (\"Black Widows\"), anchored gently by the familiar scent of his wife\\'s vanilla lip balm.',\n        tags: ['pop-culture', 'contrast'],\n      ),\n      'clothespinned eye-lids or load-bearing toothpicks': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Cartoon imagery (Tom & Jerry propping eyelids open with toothpicks) flipped—here he can\\'t shut his eyes even if he wants to.',\n        tags: ['pop-culture', 'humor'],\n      ),\n      \"there's nothing playing but he still hears music.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Both sleep-deprivation auditory pareidolia (hearing phantom melodies in white noise) and a songwriter\\'s curse of nonstop songs looping inside his head.',\n        tags: ['insomnia', 'music'],\n      ),\n      'lullabies of alibis, drowning out the fan-blades.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Making up excuses to himself in the dark louder than the whir of the ceiling fan.',\n        tags: ['internal-rhyme', 'insomnia'],\n      ),\n      \"sun's high, low-tide. the moon responds with hand waves.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Morning finally arrives as the moon politely waves goodbye—another night completely survived without sleep.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'whimsical'],\n      ),\n      'the room grows bright, eyes still wide.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Daylight pours across the bed while he\\'s still staring straight ahead, completely wired.',\n        tags: ['insomnia', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      'good morning love, did you sleep tight?.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Sweet, deadpan closer: greeting his waking partner lovingly as if he hadn\\'t just spent eight straight hours battling the ceiling.',\n        tags: ['romance', 'closer'],\n      ),\n    },\n  ),\n  'crosstops': const TrackBreakdown(\n    overview:\n        'The sprawling, 77-line emotional and lyrical centerpiece of \"life\\'s lemons.\" Named after \"crosstops\"—old-school street slang for white-cross amphetamine pills—the track is an unfiltered, breathless stream-of-consciousness tour inside an ADHD brain cycling through Ritalin, manic grandiosity, insomnia, imposter syndrome, and raw longing for stability. Its standout technical Easter egg hides four consecutive A-D-H-D backronyms right in the middle of the song (\"All Day HyperDrive\", \"Affecting my Dreams to the Hues and the Dyes\", \"Angels and Demons. Harmonies Denied.\", \"Attacking, Destroying, Hating \\'til I Die.\").',\n    tags: ['adhd', 'mental-health', 'centerpiece', 'technical'],\n    lineAnnotations: {\n      \"i'm the protege\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Opens with crisp multi-syllabic cadence—casting himself as the eager student still trying to prove he belongs.',\n        tags: ['opener', 'rhyme-scheme'],\n      ),\n      'that wants to be a prodigy': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Pairs \"protege\" with \"prodigy\"—the aching gap between having potential and being effortlessly brilliant.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'ambition'],\n      ),\n      'maybe then, i ought to be': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Sustains the four-syllable \"-odigy / ought to be\" bounce while questioning his own identity.',\n        tags: ['rhyme-scheme', 'reflection'],\n      ),\n      'the person that the wanna see.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Masking pressure: trying to bend himself into the version of Archer everyone else expects.',\n        tags: ['adhd', 'confessional'],\n      ),\n      'pill pop in peace,': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Playful spin on \"Rest in Peace\" (R.I.P.) applied to quietly taking daily psychiatric prescriptions.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'mental-health'],\n      ),\n      'praying for lobotomies': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Dark hyperbole for wishing there were an off-switch to quiet an overactive mind.',\n        tags: ['dark-humor', 'mental-health'],\n      ),\n      'to make my brain more fond of me': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Frames living with ADHD and self-criticism like being stuck inside a skull that actively dislikes you.',\n        tags: ['mental-health', 'confessional'],\n      ),\n      'and less of an anomaly.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Longing simply to feel normal instead of an outlier wired differently from everyone else.',\n        tags: ['adhd', 'vulnerability'],\n      ),\n      'synthetic dopamine': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Names the exact mechanism of ADHD stimulant medication—outsourcing the neurotransmitter the brain under-produces.',\n        tags: ['adhd', 'science'],\n      ),\n      \"i'm finding in amphetamines.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Calls Adderall / stimulant scripts plainly by their chemical class—connecting back to the title \"crosstops.\"',\n        tags: ['adhd', 'title-motif'],\n      ),\n      'another dope fiend': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Puns on \"dopamine\" / \"dope fiend,\" confronting the stigma that makes medicated people feel like addicts.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'mental-health'],\n      ),\n      'whose manic thoughts are pestering.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Captures relentless racing thoughts buzzing nonstop even on meds.',\n        tags: ['mental-health', 'adhd'],\n      ),\n      'so riddle me with ritalin': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Riddler-style wordplay (\"riddle me\" / \"Ritalin\")—asking methylphenidate to solve the puzzle of his scattered focus.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'adhd'],\n      ),\n      \"and hopefully i'll finish this\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Meta joke about executive dysfunction—hoping the meds stay active long enough just to finish writing the song.',\n        tags: ['meta', 'adhd'],\n      ),\n      'without being vindicative': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Resisting bitterness toward his own neurology.',\n        tags: ['reflection', 'mental-health'],\n      ),\n      'to chemicals mis-signalling.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Clinical honesty: blaming misfiring synapses rather than moral failure.',\n        tags: ['science', 'adhd'],\n      ),\n      'my attention deficits': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Explicitly names Attention Deficit Disorder right before accelerating the rhyme scheme.',\n        tags: ['adhd', 'confessional'],\n      ),\n      'have got me in these restless fits.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Describes the physical fidgeting and mental restlessness that won\\'t let him sit still.',\n        tags: ['adhd', 'realism'],\n      ),\n      'taking breathless hits.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Short, clipped phrasing mimics gasping for air—and leaning on nicotine/smoke to chase focus.',\n        tags: ['rhythm', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      \"the future's where i reminisce.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Brilliant paradox: living so obsessively inside future daydreams that they already feel like nostalgia.',\n        tags: ['paradox', 'adhd'],\n      ),\n      'where everything i manifest is evidence of excellence.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Switches into double-time grandiosity—imagining a future where every creative impulse turns to gold.',\n        tags: ['rhyme-scheme', 'ambition'],\n      ),\n      'reverends will read upon my testament of decadence.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Theatrical eulogy fantasy—imagining preachers dissecting his wild life story after he\\'s gone.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'hyperbole'],\n      ),\n      \"i'll haunt you like a revenant, can't stop me with an exorcist.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Gothic bravado promising his art will outlive him and keep echoing stubbornly.',\n        tags: ['gothic', 'rhyme-scheme'],\n      ),\n      'posthumous success in this post-mortem expressionist.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Cynical nod to the \"starving artist only appreciated after death\" trope (Van Gogh style).',\n        tags: ['art-reference', 'wordplay'],\n      ),\n      \"but presently, my brain's on all day hyperdrive.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Backronym #1 of 4: **A**ll **D**ay **H**yper**D**rive (A-D-H-D)! Snaps back from future daydreams into the buzzing present.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'adhd', 'easter-egg'],\n      ),\n      'affecting my dreams to the hues and the dyes.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Backronym #2 of 4: **A**ffecting my **D**reams to the **H**ues and the **D**yes (A-D-H-D)—showing how ADHD bleeds even into the color of his dreams.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'adhd', 'easter-egg'],\n      ),\n      'angels and demons. harmonies denied.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Backronym #3 of 4: **A**ngels and **D**emons. **H**armonies **D**enied (A-D-H-D)—internal spiritual tug-of-war refusing to settle into harmony.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'adhd', 'easter-egg'],\n      ),\n      \"attacking, destroying, hating 'til i die.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Backronym #4 of 4: **A**ttacking, **D**estroying, **H**ating \\'til I **D**ie (A-D-H-D)—the darkest peak of the four-bar acrostic spiral.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'adhd', 'easter-egg'],\n      ),\n      \"what in god's name is going on in my mind?\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Drops the clever wordplay for a sudden, raw cry of exhaustion right after the manic four-bar run.',\n        tags: ['confessional', 'shift'],\n      ),\n      'quit trying to tell me everything is alright': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Pushes back against hollow toxic-positivity platitudes from people who don\\'t feel the storm.',\n        tags: ['mental-health', 'frustration'],\n      ),\n      \"when you don't see the things that i see in the night\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Points to the lonely 3 AM battles nobody witnesses during polite daytime conversations.',\n        tags: ['insomnia', 'isolation'],\n      ),\n      \"when i'm stuck wide awake and the masses sleep tight.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Echoes the previous track \"midnight oil\"—isolated in sleeplessness while the world rests effortlessly.',\n        tags: ['insomnia', 'callback'],\n      ),\n      \"i can't bear to see\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Strips the beat and bars down to stark, unadorned vulnerability.',\n        tags: ['vulnerability', 'shift'],\n      ),\n      'this sort of clarity.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'When the fog lifts suddenly, seeing your own life too sharply can feel terrifying rather than comforting.',\n        tags: ['psychology', 'confessional'],\n      ),\n      \"it's scaring me.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Three completely unguarded words—no puns, no irony.',\n        tags: ['vulnerability', 'confessional'],\n      ),\n      'for once, this is sincerity.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Flags that the sarcasm shield from track 1 is completely down right now.',\n        tags: ['confessional', 'meta'],\n      ),\n      'i need some solidarity.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Asking simply not to fight his brain alone.',\n        tags: ['vulnerability', 'connection'],\n      ),\n      'somebody to take care of me.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Admits a longing for gentle support that proud adults rarely confess aloud.',\n        tags: ['vulnerability', 'confessional'],\n      ),\n      \"i don't mean like charity\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Clarifies he isn\\'t asking for pity or handouts.',\n        tags: ['clarification', 'pride'],\n      ),\n      'and surely not more therapy.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Weariness with endless clinical talk sessions that analyze the problem without steadying daily life.',\n        tags: ['mental-health', 'realism'],\n      ),\n      'no, more like regularity.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'The standalone line stands out structurally—naming what an ADHD mind craves most: steady, predictable rhythm.',\n        tags: ['adhd', 'structure'],\n      ),\n      'i need some consistency': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Expands on \"regularity\"—craving a stable baseline instead of wild peaks and crashes.',\n        tags: ['adhd', 'confessional'],\n      ),\n      'to balance the chaos in me': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Seeking equilibrium rather than erasing who he is.',\n        tags: ['mental-health', 'hope'],\n      ),\n      'and help me to see differently': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Wanting fresh perspective beyond old anxious lenses.',\n        tags: ['growth', 'confessional'],\n      ),\n      'and get rid of these tendencies.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Naming the urge to break self-sabotaging autopilot patterns.',\n        tags: ['growth', 'adhd'],\n      ),\n      'to begin my distancing': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Stepping back to put healthy daylight between impulse and action.',\n        tags: ['growth', 'psychology'],\n      ),\n      'myself from impulsivities': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Calls out hallmark ADHD impulsivity head-on.',\n        tags: ['adhd', 'confessional'],\n      ),\n      'leftover from conditioning': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Traces reactive habits back to years of learned survival patterns.',\n        tags: ['psychology', 'reflection'],\n      ),\n      'and doing too much listening': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Enjambs straight into the next stanza—showing how over-attuning to the wrong voices feeds the spiral.',\n        tags: ['enjambment', 'setup'],\n      ),\n      'to voices in my head and voices in my wallet.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Links internal anxiety directly with financial stress—two choruses nagging at once.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'realism'],\n      ),\n      \"'cause money talks and it listens to my problems.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Extends the cliché \"money talks\" into a counterfeit therapist that pretends to listen.',\n        tags: ['idiom', 'satire'],\n      ),\n      'it solves them with vodka; dissolves them in solvents': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Sharp chemistry wordplay (\"solves\" / \"dissolves\" / \"solvents\")—numbing problems in alcohol only melts them temporarily without fixing anything.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'addiction'],\n      ),\n      \"or attempts to anyway. they're always revolving.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Completes the \"-olving\" chain (\"solving\" / \"dissolving\" / \"revolving\")—every numbed problem circles right back around.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'cycle'],\n      ),\n      'stuck in the same circle: ouroborus.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'The Ouroboros—the ancient serpent eating its own tail—perfect emblem for self-feeding addiction and rumination loops.',\n        tags: ['mythology', 'symbolism'],\n      ),\n      'still chasing after the same green auras.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Chasing cash (and green smoke) as though money radiates spiritual glow.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'anti-capitalism'],\n      ),\n      'currency printed with the eye of horus.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Nods to the All-Seeing Eye / Eye of Providence on the U.S. one-dollar bill, casting cash as an occult watcher.',\n        tags: ['symbolism', 'pop-culture'],\n      ),\n      \"for the people but the people aren't for us.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Flips Lincoln\\'s Gettysburg Address (\"of the people, by the people, for the people\") into disillusionment with a society that leaves misfits behind.',\n        tags: ['historical-reference', 'social-commentary'],\n      ),\n      'since nativity, raised in captivity.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Feels born into a cage of expectations and systemic traps from day one.',\n        tags: ['internal-rhyme', 'metaphor'],\n      ),\n      \"don't have a lot of friends but i've made a lot of enemies.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Blunt social tally echoing \"whale mail\"\\'s loneliness with a sharper defensive edge.',\n        tags: ['confessional', 'callback'],\n      ),\n      'well-fed because i feed off negativity.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Admits how easy it is to let spite and criticism become your primary fuel source.',\n        tags: ['self-aware', 'wordplay'],\n      ),\n      'dropping spirit bombs like \"lend me your energy\".': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Direct Dragon Ball Z reference: Goku raising his hands and asking everyone on Earth \"Lend me your energy!\" to charge the Spirit Bomb—here channeling raw emotion into explosive verses.',\n        tags: ['pop-culture', 'anime'],\n      ),\n      'there i go again, down another rabbit trail': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Classic ADHD tangent awareness—catching himself mid-verse drifting off onto another wild metaphor.',\n        tags: ['adhd', 'meta'],\n      ),\n      'but the path i walk was uncovered by a rabid hare.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Twists Alice in Wonderland\\'s White Rabbit (\"rabbit trail\") into a frantic, rabid hare—no wonder the route feels unhinged.',\n        tags: ['literary-reference', 'wordplay'],\n      ),\n      'thinking like my brain cells are smothered, lacking air.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Mental suffocation when racing thoughts crowd out breathing room.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'mental-health'],\n      ),\n      \"i'm ready for my slumber so gather up my casket nails.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Double meaning on \"casket nails\" (\"coffin nails\" = slang for cigarettes, plus literal exhaustion longing for permanent rest).',\n        tags: ['double-entendre', 'somber'],\n      ),\n      \"in dependence in the sense i'm sitting in my habit's lair\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Splits \"independence\" into \"in dependence\"—a brilliant pun exposing how chasing freedom landed him right inside addiction\\'s den.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'addiction'],\n      ),\n      \"i'm sick of this and i don't mean to re-invent the addict's tale\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Self-aware refusal to romanticize substance dependence as something unique or glamorous.',\n        tags: ['self-aware', 'addiction'],\n      ),\n      'but these prescriptions that are written make it not so bad to bear': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Honest nuance about psychiatric medication: imperfect, complicated, yet genuinely helping make everyday life survivable.',\n        tags: ['mental-health', 'nuance'],\n      ),\n      \"this life i'm living, intermittent, singing out this spaz's prayer.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Calls the whole song a \"spaz\\'s prayer\"—raw, erratic, hyperactive honesty offered upward.',\n        tags: ['adhd', 'theology'],\n      ),\n      \"grin in fear, my mood's swinging from the chandelier.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Literalizes \"mood swings\" into Sia-style chandelier-swinging extremes with a nervous smile.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'mental-health'],\n      ),\n      \"write it all down because i'm hoping that the pen'll heal\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Art as therapy: putting the chaos on paper hoping catharsis works where pills and lectures fell short.',\n        tags: ['meta', 'hope'],\n      ),\n      \"i'll overshare until chagrin's the only thing i feel\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Callbacks to track 1 (\"big chagrin\")—knowing total honesty risks embarrassment, and doing it anyway.',\n        tags: ['callback', 'confessional'],\n      ),\n      'or until i finally find a way to bridge these hemispheres.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Longing to reconcile the left/right hemispheres of his brain—logic vs. emotion, stability vs. chaos.',\n        tags: ['science', 'metaphor'],\n      ),\n      \"but bridges burn so i'm bound to keep them separated.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Puns on \"burning bridges\" (and subtly echoes The Offspring\\'s \"Come Out and Play\": \"gotta keep \\'em separated\") to resign himself to his divided mind.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'pop-culture'],\n      ),\n      \"i'm not an addict really, i'm just being medicated.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Draws the razor-thin, often misunderstood boundary between self-medicating addiction and prescribed mental-health treatment.',\n        tags: ['mental-health', 'adhd'],\n      ),\n      \"aggravated but i'm not as gloomy as i implicated.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Pulls back from the dark ledge with a reassuring wink—venting intensely doesn\\'t mean he\\'s hopeless.',\n        tags: ['self-aware', 'tone'],\n      ),\n      \"i'm just venting to myself. i hope you found it captivating.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Closes the 77-bar marathon with a charmingly polite sign-off, turning a private therapy rant into an unforgettable performance.',\n        tags: ['meta', 'closer'],\n      ),\n    },\n  ),\n  \"and that's how it happened\": const TrackBreakdown(\n    overview:\n        'A warm, deeply endearing origin story of meeting and falling head-over-heels for his wife—serving as a bright, grounded refuge right after the marathon intensity of \"crosstops.\" Packed with hyper-specific personal details (Pall Mall menthols, Soap & Glory lotion, Doc Martens, Scholastic book fairs, and hanging her drawings on the walls), it charts the whirlwind leap from an awkward first date to making sure she finally feels home.',\n    tags: ['romance', 'personal', 'storytelling', 'heartfelt'],\n    lineAnnotations: {\n      'she was worried about the wind messing up her hair': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Opens with a vivid, nervous first-date snapshot—capturing classic pre-meeting self-consciousness in Oklahoma wind.',\n        tags: ['romance', 'opener'],\n      ),\n      'but i pleaded and i begged, \"i really don\\'t care\".': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Immediate reassurance: he was already completely charmed regardless of windblown hair.',\n        tags: ['romance', 'sweet'],\n      ),\n      \"greeted with a hug but i want to taste her paul mall's.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Unmistakably grounded sensory detail—wanting to kiss her right off the hug, tasting Pall Mall cigarettes.',\n        tags: ['detail', 'romance'],\n      ),\n      \"i can smell it through the soap & glory and i'm enthralled.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Soap & Glory (cult-favorite bath/body lotion brand) mingling with cigarette smoke—a gritty, hyper-specific scent memory of falling in love.',\n        tags: ['detail', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      'we started with lies: mandolins, tarantulas.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Playful early-dating exaggeration and silly tall tales used to impress each other and break the ice.',\n        tags: ['humor', 'storytelling'],\n      ),\n      \"i tried to play a game but i didn't read the manual.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Admits he had zero smooth \"dating game\" strategy—just improvising awkwardly from the heart.',\n        tags: ['self-deprecation', 'wordplay'],\n      ),\n      '\"if you need a place to stay, you can always crash at my place\".': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'A vulnerable, slightly bold invitation offered with fingers crossed.',\n        tags: ['storytelling', 'romance'],\n      ),\n      \"holding my breath 'til i'm blue in the face.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Nervous anticipation waiting to see if she\\'ll take him up on the offer.',\n        tags: ['idiom', 'tension'],\n      ),\n      \"couldn't figure her out so i studied her figure\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Clever double use of \"figure\" (solving a mystery vs. admiring her silhouette).',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'romance'],\n      ),\n      \"with elevator eyes. it's just how i was configured.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Checking her out head-to-toe (\"elevator eyes\"), excusing his smitten staring with a software-engineer pun (\"configured\").',\n        tags: ['tech', 'humor'],\n      ),\n      'but her menthol words got me; her cynical blizzard.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Connects her cool, sharp, dry wit (\"cynical blizzard\") back to her menthol Pall Malls—it wasn\\'t just looks, her mind hooked him.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'romance'],\n      ),\n      'thanks for meeting me in the middle, little desert lizard.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Affectionate pet-name wordplay (and a lovely wink to Archer\\'s household, which includes a bearded dragon!).',\n        tags: ['personal', 'heartfelt'],\n      ),\n      \"she's 5 feet in doc's yet i still look up to her.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Standout romantic bar: even with chunky Doc Martens boosting her to five feet tall, his admiration makes her tower above him.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'romance'],\n      ),\n      'we left our first date and started picking out furniture.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Captures \"when you know, you know\" whirlwind devotion—practically moving in together after date one.',\n        tags: ['romance', 'humor'],\n      ),\n      \"she's smarter than me; there's no jealousy there.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Zero fragile ego—genuinely proud to love someone sharper than he is.',\n        tags: ['romance', 'heartfelt'],\n      ),\n      \"i'm enticed by her collections from scholastic book fairs.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Adorable nostalgic detail celebrating her nerdy, lifelong love of books and curiosities.',\n        tags: ['nostalgia', 'detail'],\n      ),\n      'hung every drawing that she made on the walls': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Tender act of devotion—turning their shared apartment into a gallery of her art.',\n        tags: ['romance', 'heartfelt'],\n      ),\n      'not knowing the ghosts that haunted this doll.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'A poignant touch of shadow: realizing only later the past hurts she was carrying beneath her bright exterior.',\n        tags: ['depth', 'empathy'],\n      ),\n      'unpacked her bags and hung up her clothes.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Quiet, practical love expressed through domestic care rather than grand speeches.',\n        tags: ['romance', 'realism'],\n      ),\n      \"just want to make sure that she knows that she's home.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Warm, tear-jerking closer—building a safe harbor where she never has to feel transient again.',\n        tags: ['romance', 'closer'],\n      ),\n    },\n  ),\n  'c u next tuesday': const TrackBreakdown(\n    overview:\n        'A jaw-dropping all-C alliteration tour de force! Subverting the cheeky profanity acronym of its title (\"C-U-N-T\") into a relentless barrage of hard- and soft-C syllables, Archer fires satirical darts at soulless corporate conferences, insulting office \"pizza party\" perks, credit collapse, and cubicle confinement—before landing on an unexpectedly earnest closer contrasting dead cable TV with the enduring candor of the \"crucifix canon.\"',\n    tags: ['alliteration', 'satire', 'anti-capitalism', 'technical'],\n    lineAnnotations: {\n      \"here's a cryptic, criminal, clinical, crayon critique.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Opens with five straight C-words blending shady corporate behavior (\"criminal\"), cold detachment (\"clinical\"), and childlike scribbling (\"crayon\").',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'opener'],\n      ),\n      \"the chronic-flow chronicle's covert chlorine.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Describes his relentless lyrical flow as a subtle chemical bleach (\"covert chlorine\") scrubbing through corporate grime.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'metaphor'],\n      ),\n      'cloth-covered cave-dweller with a closeted conscience.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Portrays a suited corporate worker (\"cloth-covered\") retreating into Plato\\'s Cave while locking their moral compass in a closet.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'satire'],\n      ),\n      'cash-coated curriculum cruelly crafted at some conference.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Skewers overpriced corporate leadership seminars and hustle-culture workshops cooked up solely to extract money.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'anti-capitalism'],\n      ),\n      'a classic corporation of closed caskets and courses': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Pairs deadly consequences (\"closed caskets\") with glossy corporate training modules and golf courses.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'satire'],\n      ),\n      'that carefully collects cocaine and cola-crusted corpses.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Pokes at the dark history of Coca-Cola and stimulant-fueled corporate excess grinding workers into husks.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'dark-humor'],\n      ),\n      'come contribute currency until collections are completed.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Captures endless debt collectors, subscriptions, and corporate profit extraction demanding every last dollar.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'anti-capitalism'],\n      ),\n      \"here's a coupon for a couple cheese pizzas.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Devastating workplace meme punchline: instead of a raise or bonus after record profits, management throws the staff a cheap office pizza party.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'workplace'],\n      ),\n      'a caterpillar coughing cracks the continuity.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Surreal Lewis Carroll (\"Alice in Wonderland\" hookah-smoking caterpillar) glitch interrupting the corporate simulation.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'literary-reference'],\n      ),\n      'common crickets crying while cicadas caberet.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Turns noisy Southern summer insects (very Oklahoma!) into a dramatic late-night theater show.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      'concrete carbon creatures collectively cooperate.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Zooms out to a clinical sci-fi view of humanity—carbon-based lifeforms marching in sync through concrete cities.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'sci-fi'],\n      ),\n      'cells crudley combine when they communicate.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Works on three levels at once: biological cells, prison/cubicle cells, and cell phones clashing clumsily.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'double-entendre'],\n      ),\n      \"counterfeit co-sign. my credit's catastrophic.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Puns on hip-hop \"co-signs\" (endorsements) vs. loan co-signers—admitting his credit score is in ruins.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'double-entendre'],\n      ),\n      \"i'd counter with a check but i'm too cozy with a cartridge\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Double meaning on \"cartridge\": both an old video-game cartridge and a vape/THC cart keeping him checked out instead of writing checks.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'double-entendre'],\n      ),\n      'we crave the cosmic - space screensavers in cubicles.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Poignant, iconic modern-worker image: longing for the infinite universe while staring at a Windows starfield screensaver inside a gray office box.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'tech-imagery'],\n      ),\n      'cited collateral can chew down to your cuticles.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Stress over repossessed collateral literally making you bite your nails down to the quick.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      'caught, cornered, caged, and casually confined.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Four rapid-fire C-verbs snap shut like cubicle walls around the narrator.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'rhythm'],\n      ),\n      'a concept for cartoons where cans and calves combine.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Absurdist surrealist flash—like vintage rubber-hose animation mashing canned products and livestock (\"calves\") together.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'surreal'],\n      ),\n      \"in closing, cable's dead so why channel companions\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Puns on TV \"channels\" and spiritual \"channeling\"—asking why we tune into hollow media companions when the old broadcast era is over.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'wordplay'],\n      ),\n      'when the crucifix canon is consistently candid?': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Sticking to the C-constraint until the very last syllable, he pivots back to Christian Scripture (\"crucifix canon\") as the one unvarnished, honest truth.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'theology'],\n      ),\n    },\n  ),\n  'drinking outta cups': const TrackBreakdown(\n    overview:\n        'Named after the legendary 2007 viral Dan Deacon video \"Drinking Out of Cups\" (famous for its absurdist seahorse/sea-hell rant), this is Archer at his most playful, braggadocious, and self-roasting. Flexing his web-developer day job (\"div-slinging hacker\", \"Finds, refactors\"), dropping a SpongeBob \"sentence enhancers\" nod, and mocking his own emo tendencies, he pulls off the funniest fourth-wall closer on the record: swearing there\\'s deep meaning in every syllable—\"...but admittedly, that\\'s most of it.\"',\n    tags: ['comedy', 'meta', 'pop-culture', 'tech'],\n    lineAnnotations: {\n      \"everybody sucks. i'm my own favorite rapper.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Hilariously cocky opener—embracing full DIY arrogance as a bedroom indie-rapper who listens to his own demos.',\n        tags: ['humor', 'opener'],\n      ),\n      \"bump my own rhymes while i'm sitting on the crapper.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Instantly undercuts the rap-star ego with maximum bathroom-scroll realism.',\n        tags: ['self-deprecation', 'humor'],\n      ),\n      'the cracker, the slacker, the div-slinging hacker.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Brilliant developer brag: \"div-slinging\" directly references HTML `<div>` tags from Archer\\'s background as a software developer and DevOps engineer.',\n        tags: ['tech', 'personal'],\n      ),\n      'rhyming in circles like a rap protractor.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Geometry pun for looping rhyme schemes—measuring angles and syllables like a schoolroom protractor.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'simile'],\n      ),\n      \"abstractor. hiding what he's after.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Bridges software abstraction (hiding implementation details behind interfaces) with cryptic lyricism.',\n        tags: ['tech', 'meta'],\n      ),\n      \"got the midas touch but there's no x-factor.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Claims his craft turns concepts to gold while joking he lacks mainstream pop-star polish (\"The X Factor\").',\n        tags: ['mythology', 'self-deprecation'],\n      ),\n      'rhyme extracter. finds, refactors.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Pure programmer workflow applied to songwriting: treating verses like messy code—extracting functions, finding patterns, and refactoring.',\n        tags: ['tech', 'craft'],\n      ),\n      'always reads ahead to the next 2 chapters.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Brags about thinking steps ahead—both plotting album arcs and impatiently flipping forward in life.',\n        tags: ['craft', 'adhd'],\n      ),\n      \"i'm in a sea-hell drinking outta cups.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Direct quote-mashup of Dan Deacon\\'s viral \"Drinking Out of Cups\" (\"seahorse-seahell... drinking out of cups, being a bitch\").',\n        tags: ['pop-culture', 'title-drop'],\n      ),\n      'writing down punchlines, thinking up puns.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Lays bare his playful songwriting process with effortless internal rhyme (\"punchlines\" / \"puns\").',\n        tags: ['meta', 'craft'],\n      ),\n      \"the kid isn't evil. i think that he's nuts.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Imagines listeners trying to figure out whether his dark lyrics make him sinister or just wonderfully unhinged.',\n        tags: ['humor', 'meta'],\n      ),\n      \"he's writing so emo and crying too much.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Roasts his own \"emo confessionals\" aesthetic (explicitly named on his About page) before any critic can.',\n        tags: ['self-deprecation', 'meta'],\n      ),\n      \"always revealing his feelings and healing by dealing this villainous venom he's spitting.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Locks into an intense multi-syllabic internal rhyme chain (\"revealing\" / \"feelings\" / \"healing\" / \"dealing\" / \"villainous\")—demonstrating lyrical precision while mocking his own catharsis.',\n        tags: ['internal-rhyme', 'technical'],\n      ),\n      'killing his demons and serving his beats like croissants that you drop when you see the precision.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Playful nod to the classic \"Stop! I could\\'ve dropped my croissant!\" Vine meme, equating flaky pastry precision with crisp BandLab beatmaking.',\n        tags: ['pop-culture', 'humor'],\n      ),\n      'the sentence enhancers he throws in his rhymes are the reason you listen so fuck your opinion.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Genius SpongeBob SquarePants reference (\"Sailor Mouth\" episode, where SpongeBob and Patrick think swear words are fancy \"sentence enhancers\")—immediately followed by dropping an actual f-bomb to prove the joke!',\n        tags: ['pop-culture', 'humor'],\n      ),\n      \"the kitchen is closed and the genie is hoping 3 wishes will fix it but it's your decision.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Extends the bakery/kitchen metaphor into a genie-lamp challenge—no magical quick fix, you decide what to make of the music.',\n        tags: ['metaphor', 'rhyme-scheme'],\n      ),\n      \"spongebob is screaming at night and we're meme-ing and being a typical atypical.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Makes the SpongeBob nod explicit while oxymoronically embracing internet-brained neurodivergent humor (\"typical atypical\").',\n        tags: ['pop-culture', 'oxymoron'],\n      ),\n      \"looking for meaning. believe me, there's meaning. not just trying to fit these rhyme syllables\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Earnestly defends the lyrical depth behind his dense rhyme schemes—setting up the ultimate comedic rug-pull.',\n        tags: ['meta', 'setup'],\n      ),\n      \"...but admittedly, that's most of it.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Deadpan fourth-wall-shattering closer that winks straight at every lyric nerd (and every Genius annotator!) overanalyzing his bars.',\n        tags: ['punchline', 'meta'],\n      ),\n    },\n  ),\n  'you call this mercy?': const TrackBreakdown(\n    overview:\n        'A gut-wrenching, morally anguished track grappling with the nightmare of having to put down a beloved pet after an instinctual animal tragedy (\"fear in the cat\\'s eyes\", \"Instincts kicked in, it\\'s just the hex of the species / but those puppy dog eyes don\\'t make this so easy\"). Questioning whether euthanasia is mercy, murder, or playing God, the track builds to a devastating farewell note sealed with \"bunny kisses.\"',\n    tags: ['grief', 'animals', 'morality', 'somber'],\n    lineAnnotations: {\n      'does he do it for the lulz, the antics, and the anecdotes?': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Opens with bitter disbelief—questioning whether fate or a cruel observer treats heartbreak as cheap entertainment (\"for the lulz\").',\n        tags: ['grief', 'opener'],\n      ),\n      'anesthesia served with an anti-antidote.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Stark clinical description of euthanasia drugs—sedation followed by an irreversible lethal injection (\"anti-antidote\").',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'somber'],\n      ),\n      'euthanize, murder, self-defense, or a white lie?': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Lists the four competing moral labels racing through his head—refusing to hide behind polite euphemisms.',\n        tags: ['morality', 'grief'],\n      ),\n      'suffocating softly in a glass room; no light.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Claustrophobic, silent vet-room dread—watching helplessly behind sterile walls.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'somber'],\n      ),\n      'temperatures boil and temperaments soiled.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Captures the explosive moment an animal\\'s temperament snaps and chaos erupts.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'narrative'],\n      ),\n      'mauled jowls and howls. to the victims go spoils.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Inverts \"to the victor go the spoils\" amid visceral animal-fight imagery—showing nobody truly wins when pets turn on each other.',\n        tags: ['subversion', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      \"princess bed, a stretcher, and fear in the cat's eyes\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Heartbreaking domestic details—a cozy pet \"princess bed\" suddenly replaced by an emergency vet stretcher and a terrified cat.',\n        tags: ['narrative', 'grief'],\n      ),\n      'but do the consequences even fit the crime?': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Wrestles with the crushing unfairness of punishing an animal with death for acting on blind biology.',\n        tags: ['morality', 'somber'],\n      ),\n      'bloodstained remnants, ripped garments, and stitches.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Raw aftermath details of the attack and frantic emergency care.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'realism'],\n      ),\n      'incisive delusions, injections, incisions.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Sharp surgical consonant sounds mirror clinical blades, needles, and spiraling second-guessing.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      'the matrix is glitching, he played god with decisions.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'The unbearable surrealism of signing a euthanasia form—feeling forced to play God over a creature that trusts you completely.',\n        tags: ['pop-culture', 'guilt'],\n      ),\n      'last words, the predicate of the death sentence.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Grammar wordplay (\"predicate\" / \"sentence\") turning \"death sentence\" into a heartbreaking linguistic double meaning.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'somber'],\n      ),\n      'vicious vermin or precious persians,': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Contrasts how harshly people categorize animals—rats and pests vs. pampered Persian cats.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'contrast'],\n      ),\n      'shepherds, rats. a cathode burn-in.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Images of German Shepherds and trauma seared permanently into memory like static burned onto an old CRT (\"cathode\") television screen.',\n        tags: ['tech-imagery', 'grief'],\n      ),\n      'true atrocities or just another tuesday?': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Echoes the famous \"For me, it was Tuesday\" trope—shocked at how the outside world moves on routinely during a private catastrophe.',\n        tags: ['contrast', 'pop-culture'],\n      ),\n      \"why don't we ask and see what the wounds say?\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Lets the physical scars speak louder than rationalizations.',\n        tags: ['somber', 'rhetorical'],\n      ),\n      \"instincts kicked in, it's just the hex of the species\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Deep compassion even in tragedy: recognizing prey drive isn\\'t evil malice, just the tragic wiring (\"hex\") of animal instinct.',\n        tags: ['empathy', 'animals'],\n      ),\n      \"but those puppy dog eyes don't make this so easy.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'A devastating punch to the gut—looking into a trusting dog\\'s innocent eyes while knowing what\\'s about to happen.',\n        tags: ['grief', 'heartfelt'],\n      ),\n      'he wrote her a note, it read \"best wishes.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Tender, tear-inducing goodbye letter written to the pet at the end.',\n        tags: ['grief', 'epistolary'],\n      ),\n      'good night, sweetie.\", sealed with bunny kisses.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Devastatingly gentle final words—closing a song of violent grief with soft, loving affection.',\n        tags: ['heartfelt', 'closer'],\n      ),\n    },\n  ),\n  'florence': const TrackBreakdown(\n    overview:\n        'A luminous, affectionate tribute to a beloved elderly matriarch (likely a grandmother or family elder named Florence). Painted in vivid tactile snapshots—a cashmere sweater, translucent veined hands, stainless-steel sweet tea pitchers, pecan pie glimpsed through bifocals, and Meals on Wheels—the track celebrates fierce, unfiltered Southern hospitality: \"She spoke her mind even if it was ugly / but she\\'d rather die than let anyone go hungry.\"',\n    tags: ['family', 'tribute', 'nostalgia', 'imagery'],\n    lineAnnotations: {\n      'blue candle wax drips onto bolded yellow letters.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Opens with a cozy, close-up domestic still life—colored wax dripping across vintage yellow lettering or old stationery.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'opener'],\n      ),\n      'a fiber inbound from a cashmere sweater.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Zooms in to microscopic warmth—a single soft thread drifting through the air off her sweater.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'detail'],\n      ),\n      'but the focus of the moths are on the butane flames.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Shifts gently to moths circling a lighter or candle flame—hinting at fragility and mortality.',\n        tags: ['symbolism', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      'you can really see their beauty between each keyframe.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Animation/video-editing metaphor (\"keyframe\"): real grace hides in the small, unposed everyday moments between major life milestones.',\n        tags: ['tech-imagery', 'poetic'],\n      ),\n      'a wrinkled map of veins much thinner than my college thesis.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Tender, vivid portrait of elderly hands with papery skin and visible blue veins—setting up a cheeky self-deprecating joke.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'setup'],\n      ),\n      \"i didn't go to school but i'm barely facetious.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Winks at the fact that he never wrote a college thesis—making the \"much thinner\" comparison hilariously literal while staying warm.',\n        tags: ['humor', 'personal'],\n      ),\n      'now picture frames are smashed as well as all the glassware.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'A sudden burst of family chaos or grief shattering fragile keepsakes.',\n        tags: ['contrast', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      'spaghetti code-words for confetti-covered nightmares.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Programmer slang (\"spaghetti code\" = tangled, messy logic) blended with forced festive cheer (\"confetti\") hiding messy family trauma.',\n        tags: ['tech', 'metaphor'],\n      ),\n      'dancing in the sprinkler of a manicured lawn.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Sun-drenched childhood summer memory in her well-tended yard.',\n        tags: ['nostalgia', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      'ice-cream water and the yodeling of songs.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Pure, quirky childhood sensory nostalgia—melted ice-cream puddles and silly front-porch singing.',\n        tags: ['nostalgia', 'whimsical'],\n      ),\n      'tea-leaves excrete love inside of stainless steel.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Turns brewing iced tea in an old metal pitcher into a sacrament of Southern grandmotherly love.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'family'],\n      ),\n      'it might have lost its shine but it still feels real.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Honors aging and weathered heirlooms: tarnished metal—and aging love—never loses its authenticity.',\n        tags: ['heartfelt', 'metaphor'],\n      ),\n      'immobile meals for mailmen to bring to all the locals.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Clever nod to Meals on Wheels and neighborhood care packages—food made to travel outward to everyone in the community.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'detail'],\n      ),\n      'pecan pie on both sides of bifocals.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Unforgettable visual: slices of Southern pecan pie reflected right in her bifocal lenses as she serves them up.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'family'],\n      ),\n      'she spoke her mind even if it was ugly': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Refuses to flatten her into a saintly caricature—affectionately remembering her blunt, unfiltered honesty.',\n        tags: ['realism', 'family'],\n      ),\n      \"but she'd rather die than let anyone go hungry.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'A timeless, deeply moving epitaph: fierce, unconditional love shown through always making sure everyone\\'s plate was full.',\n        tags: ['heartfelt', 'closer'],\n      ),\n    },\n  ),\n  \"let's take it apart and put it back together\": const TrackBreakdown(\n    overview:\n        'The introspective, quietly hopeful closer to \"life\\'s lemons.\" Walking the listener through the dimly lit interior architecture of his own mind—cobwebs, broken glass on the floor, a swing set hidden behind a rollercoaster, filing cabinets stuffed with \"accidents,\" and a chilling \"flash sale on rope\"—Archer refuses to end in despair. Instead, the final couplet extends a gentle hand toward himself (and the listener): \"Get out of bed and pick it up. I promise that you\\'re better now.\"',\n    tags: ['closer', 'mental-health', 'hope', 'metaphor'],\n    lineAnnotations: {\n      'cobwebs behind your eyes, reverb between your ears.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Audio-production imagery (\"reverb\") meets haunted-attic mental fog—turning the inside of the skull into a echoing, dusty room.',\n        tags: ['music', 'opener'],\n      ),\n      'an empty space for thinking and for facing all your fears.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Frames that cavernous inner room as a workshop where hard introspection finally has to happen.',\n        tags: ['reflection', 'metaphor'],\n      ),\n      'a little dusty but there\\'s a broom and a rug.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Alludes to \"sweeping things under the rug\"—temporary coping tools sitting right there in the corner.',\n        tags: ['idiom', 'metaphor'],\n      ),\n      'the glass on the floor explains all the blood.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Callbacks to \"florence\"\\'s smashed glassware and reminds us that suppressed wreckage still cuts anyone walking barefoot through memory.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'callback'],\n      ),\n      \"obfuscated reminiscing, scared of what's to come.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Software term (\"obfuscated\" = deliberately tangled/obscured) for cloudy memories paired with dread of the future.',\n        tags: ['tech', 'anxiety'],\n      ),\n      'barely coughed the words out with smoke in his lungs.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Struggling to speak honest vulnerability through physical and emotional haze.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'confessional'],\n      ),\n      \"there's a swing set in the corner behind the rollercoaster.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Childlike simplicity (\"swing set\") tucked quietly behind the wild manic-depressive rides (\"rollercoaster\") dominating his brain.',\n        tags: ['metaphor', 'mental-health'],\n      ),\n      'to get a better view, just move the serotonin over.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Playfully treats brain chemistry like bulky furniture blocking the window to everyday peace.',\n        tags: ['mental-health', 'humor'],\n      ),\n      \"anti-this, anti-that. he's psychotic as it is.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Puns on prescription prefixes (antidepressants, antipsychotics, anti-anxiety) and knee-jerk contrarianism.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'mental-health'],\n      ),\n      'feel-good and do-little are his only friends.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Personifies escapist dopamine habits and depressive inertia as two unhelpful companions.',\n        tags: ['personification', 'mental-health'],\n      ),\n      'resting in isolation while coveting peace.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Exposes the difference between hiding out alone and actually feeling at peace.',\n        tags: ['isolation', 'psychology'],\n      ),\n      'spiders on the ceiling that crawl into your dreams.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Revisits Archer\\'s recurring spider/insomnia motif (from \"midnight oil\" and \"blubber\")—anxieties creeping straight from waking hours into sleep.',\n        tags: ['callback', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      \"it's dim but you can still read all the files in the cabinets.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Pictures memory as a dim, dusty archive room—even in low light, every old regret stays painfully legible.',\n        tags: ['metaphor', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      \"pick a drawer, any drawer. they're all filled with accidents.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Magician\\'s patter (\"pick a card, any card\") applied to pulling open a lifetime of embarrassing mistakes and trauma.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'dark-humor'],\n      ),\n      'time capsules capturing classical hopes.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Old dreams buried carefully for a future self who never turned out quite as planned.',\n        tags: ['nostalgia', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      \"are you disappointed yet? there's a flash sale on rope.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'A stark, bleak intrusive suicidal thought dressed in cynical retail language (\"flash sale\")—naming the darkest temptation out loud so it loses its secrecy.',\n        tags: ['mental-health', 'somber'],\n      ),\n      \"deja vu's moving in so get used to his habits.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Personifies repetitive mental patterns as a permanent roommate unpacking his things.',\n        tags: ['personification', 'cycle'],\n      ),\n      \"he'll always remind you not to rest on the sabbath.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Reverses the Fourth Commandment (Exodus 20:8, \"Remember the Sabbath day, to keep it holy\")—an anxious mind that actively forbids guilt-free rest.',\n        tags: ['theology', 'mental-health'],\n      ),\n      \"let's hope you re-adjust so you'll stop laughing with a frown.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Circles all the way back to Track 1 (\"altering my frown into a big chagrin\"), hoping to trade defensive sarcasm for genuine joy.',\n        tags: ['callback', 'hope'],\n      ),\n      \"get out of bed and pick it up. i promise that you're better now.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'A tender, triumphant close to the entire album: after taking his mind apart across 13 tracks, Archer gently puts it back together with a promise of recovery.',\n        tags: ['hope', 'closer'],\n      ),\n    },\n  ),\n};\n",
  "lib/pages/music/annotations/santas_cookies_annotations.dart": "import 'package:archbtw_sh/pages/music/lyric_annotations.dart';\n\nfinal Map<String, TrackBreakdown> santasCookiesAnnotations = {\n  'who you calling a ho, ho?': const TrackBreakdown(\n    overview:\n        'The caustic opener to \"santa\\'s cookies\" weaponizes holiday tropes to skewer late-stage Christmas consumerism, billionaire hubris, and seasonal financial burnout. Between stoner domestic bliss and a literal hit-and-run on Santa\\'s sleigh by Elon Musk, Donald Trump, and Jeff Bezos, Archer contrasts the warmth of intimate holiday rituals with the hollow, commodified spectacle of December capitalism—closing on a deadpan \"Happy Birthday, Jesus.\"',\n    tags: ['satire', 'anti-consumerism', 'holiday', 'wordplay'],\n    lineAnnotations: {\n      'a lit christmas. a wishlist of wishes.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Triple-meaning opener on \"lit\": Christmas lights strung across the room, getting high for the holidays, and a hyped-up party. \"Wishlist of wishes\" doubles down on consumer longing—wanting to want things.',\n        tags: ['double-entendre', 'opener'],\n      ),\n      'toe of mistle, underneath which i kiss lips': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Inverts \"mistletoe\" into \"toe of mistle\" for crisp internal rhyme (\"mistle\" / \"kiss lips\"), setting an intimate, playful domestic holiday scene before the satire hits.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'rhyme-scheme'],\n      ),\n      'and grab hips, shotgun hits. the clause says missus.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Combines romantic intimacy with \"shotgun hits\" (blowing smoke directly into a partner\\'s mouth). \"The clause says missus\" puns on Santa Claus, Mrs. Claus, and a legal/marital contract clause.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'double-entendre'],\n      ),\n      'the tree is in the swisher with spit to stick it.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            '\"Tree\" doubles as a Christmas tree and weed rolled inside a Swisher Sweet blunt wrap, sealed with spit—subverting wholesome decorating imagery.',\n        tags: ['double-entendre', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      'cinnamon toothpicks but never chews pepper.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Playful mouthfeel contrast—liking sweet-spiced cinnamon toothpicks while avoiding harsh pepper—mirroring the song\\'s sweet-holiday-veneer vs. biting-reality tone.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'contrast'],\n      ),\n      'bloodshot green eyes and wreaths with scarlet letters.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Red-and-green Christmas colors reimagined as bloodshot green eyes; pairs festive wreaths with Nathaniel Hawthorne\\'s \"The Scarlet Letter,\" turning holiday decor into public moral branding.',\n        tags: ['literary-reference', 'color-motif'],\n      ),\n      'a couple vintage schmucks in brand new ugly sweaters.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Self-deprecating portrait of the couple leaning into tacky holiday tradition—oxymoronically pairing \"vintage\" personalities with \"brand new\" intentionally ugly Christmas sweaters.',\n        tags: ['self-deprecation', 'oxymoron'],\n      ),\n      \"beggars can't be choosers, but choosers can be beggars.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Flips the classic proverb via chiasmus: even people with options end up desperate and pleading under a culture built on endless consumer craving.',\n        tags: ['chiasmus', 'anti-consumerism'],\n      ),\n      'i saw the sleigh crash as elon fled the scene': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'The chorus erupts into grotesque satire: tech-billionaire culture (Elon Musk) literally runs Santa off the road and flees the wreckage without accountability.',\n        tags: ['satire', 'pop-culture'],\n      ),\n      \"with a passenger with fool's gold hair that recedes.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Thinly veiled caricature of Donald Trump riding shotgun—\"fool\\'s gold\" (pyrite) mocks both his signature blonde hair and the illusion of gilded wealth.',\n        tags: ['satire', 'metaphor'],\n      ),\n      'replayed 4:3 domestics on imported widescreens.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Contrasts old-school 4:3 aspect-ratio domestic drama (and \"domestic\" products/violence) stretched awkwardly onto cheap imported flat-screen TVs—peak Black Friday irony.',\n        tags: ['satire', 'tech-imagery'],\n      ),\n      'drove away in their tesla sipping juiced cocoa beans.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'The billionaires escape the crash in a Tesla while drinking luxury hot chocolate (\"juiced cocoa beans\"), insulated from the carnage they just caused.',\n        tags: ['satire', 'pop-culture'],\n      ),\n      \"bloody snow melted off santa's faux white collar.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Puns on \"white collar\": both the fake fur trim on Santa\\'s suit and white-collar corporate crime—now stained red in the snow.',\n        tags: ['double-entendre', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      \"now there's 8 or 9 deer on a beatup hauler.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'The iconic reindeer team (eight originals plus Rudolph) reduced to roadkill loaded onto a rusty tow truck—the magic of childhood folklore stripped down to scrap.',\n        tags: ['dark-humor', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      'but as the wreckage gets cleared, the problems get smaller.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Captures how quickly society sweeps disasters under the rug so the holiday shopping cycle can keep moving without interruption.',\n        tags: ['satire', 'social-commentary'],\n      ),\n      \"what'll he do next? he's no scholar.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'A biting aside questioning the competence of the wreck\\'s perpetrators—wealth and spectacle substituting for actual wisdom.',\n        tags: ['satire', 'sarcasm'],\n      ),\n      '12th month, filing the 13th chapter': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Clever numeric progression: December (12th month) leads directly into Chapter 13 bankruptcy (13th chapter) after people drown in holiday debt.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'anti-consumerism'],\n      ),\n      'while the stocks keep soaring on the deceased raptors.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            '\"Deceased raptors\" = fossil fuels (oil/gas from prehistoric creatures), pointing out that energy stocks boom even as working families go broke in December.',\n        tags: ['metaphor', 'social-commentary'],\n      ),\n      'in the rafters, stored for our afters.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Links attic storage (holiday boxes tucked in the rafters) with squirreling away scraps for \"afters\" (dessert/the afterlife) while hanging by a thread.',\n        tags: ['internal-rhyme', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      'i only self-destruct because i want to get there faster': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'A sudden flash of raw vulnerability beneath the comedy—impatiently speeding toward collapse or the afterlife (\"afters\") out of exhaustion.',\n        tags: ['mental-health', 'confessional'],\n      ),\n      \"can't leave the house if the gears don't shift.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Works literally (a broken car transmission trapping you at home in winter) and metaphorically (executive dysfunction or depression keeping you stuck in neutral).',\n        tags: ['metaphor', 'mental-health'],\n      ),\n      'santa claus is down and we need a pinch-hit.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Uses baseball terminology (\"pinch-hit\") to set up who steps in to replace the fallen gift-delivery mythos.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'narrative'],\n      ),\n      'jaws dropped when bezos whipped out his dick.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Crude, blunt punchline mocking Jeff Bezos\\'s infamous Blue Origin rocket shape and monopolistic flex as Amazon steps in to replace Santa Claus.',\n        tags: ['satire', 'pop-culture'],\n      ),\n      \"10 bucks a month, 2 days free, and it's shipped.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Amazon Prime officially usurps Christmas magic: Santa\\'s sleigh replaced by a monthly subscription fee and two-day doorstep delivery.',\n        tags: ['anti-consumerism', 'satire'],\n      ),\n      'how many dollars do you love me?': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Distills modern holiday anxiety into one brutal question: equating affection directly with gift price tags.',\n        tags: ['anti-consumerism', 'confessional'],\n      ),\n      'money is a drug and i know you want to drug me.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Treats retail therapy and financial gifts as a sedative used to numb real discontent or buy compliance.',\n        tags: ['metaphor', 'anti-consumerism'],\n      ),\n      'mickey in the eggnog and now he feels funny': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            '\"Slipping a Mickey\" (spiking a drink) mixed into festive eggnog extends the \"money is a drug\" metaphor into a woozy holiday stupor.',\n        tags: ['idiom', 'dark-humor'],\n      ),\n      'this time of year is just so lovely.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Dripping sarcasm—contrasting Hallmark holiday cheer with the spiked eggnog, bankruptcy, and sleigh carnage described throughout the song.',\n        tags: ['sarcasm', 'contrast'],\n      ),\n      'happy birthday, jesus.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'A deadpan reminder of what Christmas is nominally supposed to celebrate, arriving right after verses about Elon, Bezos, and debt.',\n        tags: ['theology', 'irony'],\n      ),\n      \"i'm so glad it's christmas\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Closes the track on an ambiguously deadpan note—equal parts weary irony and genuine gratitude for the small warmth found amidst the chaos.',\n        tags: ['irony', 'closer'],\n      ),\n    },\n  ),\n  'oh christmas tree': const TrackBreakdown(\n    overview:\n        'A warm, hazy, affectionate palate cleanser right after the bitter satire of track one. Set on a lazy winter morning in bed with his partner, Archer blends stoner humor (\"barter with fruit\", \"roll\"), Seinfeld\\'s Festivus pole, and quiet domestic romance into a cozy pocket universe where Santa can skip their house entirely because they already have everything they need.',\n    tags: ['romance', 'holiday', 'cozy', 'wordplay'],\n    lineAnnotations: {\n      'early morning, the sun peeks through the blinds.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Grounds the song in quiet, golden morning light—immediately shifting the EP\\'s mood from cynical chaos to bedroom stillness.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'opener'],\n      ),\n      'eyes red and green, colored outside the lines.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Revisits the bloodshot-green-eyes Christmas palette from track one, pairing it with \"coloring outside the lines\" to embrace an unconventional, rule-breaking holiday morning.',\n        tags: ['color-motif', 'wordplay'],\n      ),\n      'oh christmas tree, we laugh while we roll.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Subverts the traditional carol \"O Tannenbaum\" (\"O Christmas Tree\")—here \"tree\" is weed being rolled while the two of them crack up in bed.',\n        tags: ['double-entendre', 'holiday'],\n      ),\n      'in its place, we put up a pole.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Direct nod to Festivus from Seinfeld (\"a Festivus for the rest of us\"), where Frank Costanza replaces the Christmas tree with an unadorned aluminum pole—also cheekily flirting with strip-pole imagery.',\n        tags: ['pop-culture', 'double-entendre'],\n      ),\n      'the vapors rise and we follow suit.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Smoke/vapor drifts upward as they get high (\"follow suit\" = rising right along with it, floating above everyday stress).',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'idiom'],\n      ),\n      'when the paper runs out, we can barter with fruit.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Double joke: smoking out of a carved apple pipe when rolling papers run out, plus trading fruit like an old-fashioned barter economy when cash (\"paper\") is gone.',\n        tags: ['double-entendre', 'wordplay'],\n      ),\n      'icy cold hands but you radiate warmth.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Tender, classic couple detail—cold winter fingers contrasting with the physical and emotional warmth of the person beside him.',\n        tags: ['romance', 'contrast'],\n      ),\n      'under the covers and over this world.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Clean directional wordplay (\"under\" / \"over\"): hiding beneath the duvet while feeling completely done with—and floating above—the outside world.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'romance'],\n      ),\n      'prancing below us are reindeer that fly.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'They\\'re so high—literally and emotionally—that even Santa\\'s flying reindeer appear to be prancing beneath them.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'hyperbole'],\n      ),\n      \"it might be in our heads but it's such a gorgeous sight.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Embraces the daydream without cynicism: even if the magic is half-imagined or haze-induced, sharing it makes it beautiful.',\n        tags: ['romance', 'refrain'],\n      ),\n      \"he can skip our house. we'll eat the cookies instead.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Ties directly to the EP title \"santa\\'s cookies\"—turning away external holiday expectations to enjoy the treats meant for Santa themselves.',\n        tags: ['title-drop', 'cozy'],\n      ),\n      \"we've got everything we need right here in bed.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'The emotional thesis of the track: real contentment isn\\'t under a tree or in an Amazon box, it\\'s right next to you.',\n        tags: ['romance', 'refrain'],\n      ),\n      'twelve-gauged pecks from my favorite pigeon.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Playfully compares affectionate kisses (\"pecks\") to the punch of a 12-gauge shotgun—endearingly calling his partner his \"favorite pigeon.\"',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'romance'],\n      ),\n      \"they shouldn't have left us without supervision.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Captures the mischievous, giggling energy of two adults acting like kids left home alone.',\n        tags: ['humor', 'romance'],\n      ),\n      'we threw the first stone but we aimed at ourselves.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Flips Jesus\\'s famous line in John 8:7 (\"let him who is without sin cast the first stone\") into getting \"stoned\" together—self-inflicted and guilt-free.',\n        tags: ['theology', 'double-entendre'],\n      ),\n      'can you load up the next one? you do it so well.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Extends the \"stone\" / bowl-loading pun into affectionate domestic teamwork.',\n        tags: ['double-entendre', 'romance'],\n      ),\n      'stockings flanking our digital fire.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Relatable modern apartment detail: hanging real Christmas stockings on either side of a YouTube Yule log fireplace playing on a TV or monitor.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'modern-life'],\n      ),\n      \"i don't want to go to sleep yet, i'm not even tired.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Savoring a rare peaceful moment so much that you resist letting the day end.',\n        tags: ['romance', 'confessional'],\n      ),\n      \"the gifts are wrapped but we can't say the same.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Cheeky intimacy: unlike the presents under the tree, neither of them is wearing clothes.',\n        tags: ['double-entendre', 'romance'],\n      ),\n      'your presence is the present. presenting your frame.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Triple homophone/polyptoton chain (\"presence\" / \"present\" / \"presenting\") celebrating both her company as the real gift and admiring her body.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'romance'],\n      ),\n    },\n  ),\n  'he must be a south pole elf': const TrackBreakdown(\n    overview:\n        'Named after Peter Dinklage\\'s classic insult in the movie \"Elf\" (\"He\\'s an angry elf... he must be a South Pole elf\"), this track reimagines Santa\\'s workshop as an exploitative corporate sweatshop. Blending workplace alienation, under-the-table labor, hangover coping, and Orwellian \"naughty or nice\" classification, Archer turns holiday folklore into a sharp working-class anthem.',\n    tags: ['pop-culture', 'anti-capitalism', 'satire', 'workplace'],\n    lineAnnotations: {\n      'he marked their names in crimson red.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Santa\\'s Naughty-or-Nice list becomes a ruthless HR ledger written in blood-red ink—later echoed in the \"rudolph_spoke.sh\" game HUD (\"MARKED IN CRIMSON\").',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'easter-egg'],\n      ),\n      '\"a check for you and for you, an x.\"': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Reduces human worth to a binary pass/fail audit—echoing both \"checking it twice\" and cold bureaucratic sorting.',\n        tags: ['satire', 'anti-capitalism'],\n      ),\n      'classification is how he gets off.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Frames Santa\\'s obsession with sorting people into rigid moral/economic tiers as a perverse power trip.',\n        tags: ['satire', 'social-commentary'],\n      ),\n      'so turn off your thoughts and step into the box.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Critiques conformity and corporate compliance: stop thinking critically and fit neatly inside the cubicle or demographic label assigned to you.',\n        tags: ['anti-capitalism', 'metaphor'],\n      ),\n      'elves paid under tables chip away at christmas debt': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Turns the workshop elves into exploited, off-the-books gig workers laboring just to survive the very holiday machine they manufacture.',\n        tags: ['anti-capitalism', 'satire'],\n      ),\n      'swallow your feelings like hot chocolate and cigarettes': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Juxtaposes innocent winter comfort (hot chocolate) with stressed-out break-room coping (cigarettes)—bottling up burnout to get through the shift.',\n        tags: ['contrast', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      \"there's commotion of course, as the seconds tick down.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Captures crunch-time panic before the Christmas Eve deadline (or the end of a workday clock).',\n        tags: ['narrative', 'workplace'],\n      ),\n      'he waited too long and the marshmallows drowned.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'A tiny, poignant symbol of putting off joy for work: by the time you finally pause to enjoy something sweet, it\\'s already dissolved.',\n        tags: ['metaphor', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      'gingerbread house with a chimney that billows.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Opens the chorus with a storybook candy-house fantasy—a seductive facade concealing a factory smokestack.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'contrast'],\n      ),\n      'a bed made of frosting with gum drop pillows.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Sugar-coated comfort as a trap (evoking Hansel and Gretel\\'s witch house)—sweet promises meant to keep workers compliant.',\n        tags: ['literary-reference', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      \"minds being moulded, memory's malleable.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Alliterative M-sounds highlight how consumer propaganda and corporate conditioning reshape what people remember and desire.',\n        tags: ['alliteration', 'social-commentary'],\n      ),\n      'if you want to eat dessert, then give up your valuables.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'The transactional bargain of consumer culture: trade away your time, dignity, or savings for a brief taste of manufactured sweetness.',\n        tags: ['anti-capitalism', 'refrain'],\n      ),\n      'he worked 8-5 and then 5-12.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'A brutal 16-hour double-shift schedule—day job followed immediately by an evening grind or side hustle just to stay afloat.',\n        tags: ['workplace', 'realism'],\n      ),\n      'sleep in the middle, then repeat the hell.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Distills wage-slave monotony into a bare loop: brief exhaustion between shifts before clocking right back in.',\n        tags: ['workplace', 'mental-health'],\n      ),\n      'hair of the dog, feline whisker for garnish': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Plays off \"hair of the dog\" (drinking in the morning to cure a hangover) and escalates it absurdly with a \"feline whisker\" garnish.',\n        tags: ['idiom', 'wordplay'],\n      ),\n      'he reaked of the stuff, stinging nostrils like varnish.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Visceral sensory detail of stale alcohol seeping out of an overworked worker\\'s pores—sharp and toxic like wood finish.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'simile'],\n      ),\n      'the boss wore a vintage red polyester-blend jumpsuit.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Demystifies Santa\\'s iconic suit into cheap corporate-middle-management apparel—a tacky red polyester uniform.',\n        tags: ['satire', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      'you were supposed to punch the clock but you let it punch you.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Crisp antimetabole turning the workplace idiom \"punch the clock\" upside down—the schedule beats the worker into submission.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'workplace'],\n      ),\n      \"so drink your java down, you're a teeth-locked cog.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Chug the coffee and lock back into the machine: \"teeth-locked cog\" works both as mechanical gear teeth and jaw-clenching caffeine stress.',\n        tags: ['double-entendre', 'workplace'],\n      ),\n      'but before you go to sleep, you can write this song.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Breaks the fourth wall to reveal the narrator is Archer himself—carving out a few late-night minutes after grueling shifts to turn frustration into art.',\n        tags: ['meta', 'confessional'],\n      ),\n    },\n  ),\n  'rudolph spoke in class today': const TrackBreakdown(\n    overview:\n        'The pitch-black closer to \"santa\\'s cookies\" splices the beloved Rudolph fable with Pearl Jam\\'s 1991 classic \"Jeremy\" (\"Jeremy spoke in class today\"), turning the classic bullying-to-validation story into a chilling cautionary tale of alienation and retaliation. Packed with sinister holiday inversions—most famously unmasking \"Santa\" as an anagram for \"Satan\"—the song inspired the site\\'s playable Contra-style game rudolph_spoke.sh.',\n    tags: ['dark-satire', 'pop-culture', 'wordplay', 'narrative'],\n    lineAnnotations: {\n      'the moon grins down onto the snowcapped trees.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Sets an eerie, cinematic horror-movie atmosphere—even the moon looks complicit and sinister over the winter forest.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'opener'],\n      ),\n      'a truly silent night. a snapped branch would be deafening.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Subverts the peaceful carol \"Silent Night\" into suffocating, predatory tension right before violence erupts.',\n        tags: ['holiday', 'contrast'],\n      ),\n      'the wind stands still while his time runs out.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Freezes the frame on the ticking countdown before Rudolph finally snaps.',\n        tags: ['tension', 'narrative'],\n      ),\n      'always running his mouth. he better not pout.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Twists the cheerful warning from \"Santa Claus Is Comin\\' to Town\" (\"you better not pout\") into a cold threat aimed at a bully whose luck just ran out.',\n        tags: ['holiday', 'subversion'],\n      ),\n      'antlers covered in stains of their enemies.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Turns reindeer antlers from cute holiday silhouettes into bloodied weapons of vengeance.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'dark-satire'],\n      ),\n      'herbivores turned predatory. chewing on the melody.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Highlights the unnatural transformation of peaceful grazing animals into hunters—while \"chewing on the melody\" self-referentially nods to the song\\'s biting cadence.',\n        tags: ['contrast', 'meta'],\n      ),\n      \"deep grudges that won't heal slowly.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Points out how years of mockery and ostracization fester rather than fade on their own.',\n        tags: ['psychology', 'narrative'],\n      ),\n      \"please don't make light of a nose that's glowing.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Standout double entendre on \"make light of\": both mocking/dismissing his difference and literally joking about his luminous red nose.',\n        tags: ['double-entendre', 'wordplay'],\n      ),\n      \"now he leads the way of an anagram's carriage.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Brilliant concealed wordplay: rearrange the letters of SANTA and you get SATAN—turning the sleigh into the devil\\'s chariot with Rudolph at the helm.',\n        tags: ['wordplay', 'anagram'],\n      ),\n      \"distribution system's just a little too careless.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Deadpan understatement pointing to both Santa\\'s reckless gift logistics and a broken system that hands out power—or weapons—without care.',\n        tags: ['satire', 'social-commentary'],\n      ),\n      'picked last for games and he drew some bad cards.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'References the original carol (\"never let poor Rudolph join in any reindeer games\") alongside being dealt a cruel hand from birth.',\n        tags: ['holiday', 'idiom'],\n      ),\n      'rudolph snapped. clapped back a little too hard.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Uses casual modern slang (\"clapped back\") for catastrophic retaliation, sharpening the dark irony of the hook.',\n        tags: ['slang', 'dark-humor'],\n      ),\n      'hooves thrown up but they still lied down.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Surrender (\"hands/hooves up\") fails to save them—\"lied down\" puns on both falling dead/defeated and being caught in their past lies.',\n        tags: ['double-entendre', 'wordplay'],\n      ),\n      'is it a tko or is it another round?': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Boxing terminology (\"technical knockout\" / \"another round\") blurs with gunfire \"rounds,\" questioning whether the cycle of retaliation ever actually ends.',\n        tags: ['double-entendre', 'tension'],\n      ),\n      'the air smells like charcoal but more sadistic.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Replaces the cozy scent of fireplace charcoal (or lumps of coal in stockings) with the acrid smell of scorched destruction.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'dark-satire'],\n      ),\n      \"you shouldn't stare at the orb like a television.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Treats Rudolph\\'s hypnotic glowing red nose as a mesmerizing \"orb\"—critiquing how people passively gawk at catastrophe on TV screens.',\n        tags: ['metaphor', 'social-commentary'],\n      ),\n      'the next day, the crosses lined the horizon.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Stark aftermath imagery: makeshift roadside memorials or graves stretching across the snow the morning after.',\n        tags: ['imagery', 'somber'],\n      ),\n      'little figures mounted on the shoulders of giants.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Inverts Isaac Newton\\'s famous phrase (\"standing on the shoulders of giants\") into an unsettling tableau of small casualties perched atop colossal forces.',\n        tags: ['literary-reference', 'subversion'],\n      ),\n      'replaying voicemails of screamed last words.': LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'A gut-punch pivot into stark, haunting realism—evoking the real grief left behind after senseless tragedies.',\n        tags: ['somber', 'imagery'],\n      ),\n      \"they're the only ones saved so they're the only ones heard.\": LyricAnnotation(\n        summary:\n            'Devastating double meaning on \"saved\": digitally archived voicemail recordings vs. the people who weren\\'t saved—leaving grief looping on repeat.',\n        tags: ['double-entendre', 'closer'],\n      ),\n    },\n  ),\n};\n",
  "lib/pages/music/lyric_annotations.dart": "import 'package:archbtw_sh/pages/music/annotations/blubber_annotations.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/pages/music/annotations/lifes_lemons_annotations.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/pages/music/annotations/santas_cookies_annotations.dart';\n\n/// Normalizes a track title or lyric line so annotation lookups remain resilient\n/// against casing, extra spacing, or smart-quote differences.\nString normalizeAnnotationKey(String input) {\n  return input\n      .trim()\n      .replaceAll('\\u2019', \"'\")\n      .replaceAll('\\u2018', \"'\")\n      .replaceAll('\\u201c', '\"')\n      .replaceAll('\\u201d', '\"')\n      .replaceAll(RegExp(r'\\s+'), ' ')\n      .toLowerCase();\n}\n\n/// A single Rap Genius-style breakdown for a lyric line.\nclass LyricAnnotation {\n  final String summary;\n  final List<String> tags;\n\n  const LyricAnnotation({\n    required this.summary,\n    this.tags = const [],\n  });\n}\n\n/// Track-level overview plus per-line annotations keyed by normalized line text.\nclass TrackBreakdown {\n  final String overview;\n  final List<String> tags;\n  final Map<String, LyricAnnotation> lineAnnotations;\n\n  const TrackBreakdown({\n    required this.overview,\n    this.tags = const [],\n    this.lineAnnotations = const {},\n  });\n\n  LyricAnnotation? annotationForLine(String rawLine) {\n    final key = normalizeAnnotationKey(rawLine);\n    return lineAnnotations[key] ??\n        lineAnnotations[key.replaceAll(RegExp(r'\\.+\$'), '')] ??\n        lineAnnotations['\$key.'];\n  }\n}\n\n/// Identifies a clickable target inside the lyrics view (either a track title or a line).\nenum AnnotatableTargetKind {\n  track,\n  line,\n}\n\n/// Flat navigable item representing either a track header or an individual lyric line.\nclass AnnotatableItem {\n  final int index;\n  final int trackIndex;\n  final String trackTitle;\n  final AnnotatableTargetKind kind;\n  final String text;\n  final int? lineNumber;\n  final int totalLinesInTrack;\n\n  const AnnotatableItem({\n    required this.index,\n    required this.trackIndex,\n    required this.trackTitle,\n    required this.kind,\n    required this.text,\n    this.lineNumber,\n    required this.totalLinesInTrack,\n  });\n}\n\n/// A single rendered row inside a parsed track (either a stanza break or a lyric line).\nclass ParsedLyricRow {\n  final bool isStanzaBreak;\n  final AnnotatableItem? item;\n\n  const ParsedLyricRow.stanzaBreak()\n      : isStanzaBreak = true,\n        item = null;\n\n  const ParsedLyricRow.line(this.item) : isStanzaBreak = false;\n}\n\n/// A parsed track section from raw album lyrics.\nclass ParsedLyricTrack {\n  final int trackIndex;\n  final String title;\n  final AnnotatableItem headerItem;\n  final List<ParsedLyricRow> rows;\n\n  const ParsedLyricTrack({\n    required this.trackIndex,\n    required this.title,\n    required this.headerItem,\n    required this.rows,\n  });\n\n  int get lineCount => rows.where((r) => !r.isStanzaBreak).length;\n}\n\n/// Complete parsed lyrics document for an album.\nclass ParsedAlbumLyrics {\n  final List<ParsedLyricTrack> tracks;\n  final List<AnnotatableItem> allItems;\n\n  const ParsedAlbumLyrics({\n    required this.tracks,\n    required this.allItems,\n  });\n}\n\n/// Parses the `[track title]` delimited raw lyrics string into structured tracks\n/// and clickable items while preserving stanza breaks.\nParsedAlbumLyrics parseAlbumLyrics(String rawLyrics) {\n  final rawLines = rawLyrics.split('\\n');\n\n  final List<_RawTrackBuffer> rawTracks = [];\n  _RawTrackBuffer? current;\n  bool inDescriptionBlock = false;\n\n  for (final line in rawLines) {\n    final trimmed = line.trim();\n    if (trimmed == '**') {\n      inDescriptionBlock = !inDescriptionBlock;\n      continue;\n    }\n    if (inDescriptionBlock) {\n      continue;\n    }\n\n    if (trimmed.startsWith('[') && trimmed.endsWith(']')) {\n      final title = trimmed.substring(1, trimmed.length - 1).trim();\n      current = _RawTrackBuffer(title);\n      rawTracks.add(current);\n      continue;\n    }\n\n    if (current == null) {\n      continue;\n    }\n\n    if (trimmed.isEmpty) {\n      if (current.entries.isNotEmpty && current.entries.last != null) {\n        current.entries.add(null);\n      }\n    } else {\n      current.entries.add(trimmed);\n    }\n  }\n\n  final List<ParsedLyricTrack> parsedTracks = [];\n  final List<AnnotatableItem> allItems = [];\n\n  for (int t = 0; t < rawTracks.length; t++) {\n    final buffer = rawTracks[t];\n    // Trim trailing stanza breaks inside a track.\n    while (buffer.entries.isNotEmpty && buffer.entries.last == null) {\n      buffer.entries.removeLast();\n    }\n\n    final int totalLines = buffer.entries.where((e) => e != null).length;\n\n    final headerItem = AnnotatableItem(\n      index: allItems.length,\n      trackIndex: t,\n      trackTitle: buffer.title,\n      kind: AnnotatableTargetKind.track,\n      text: buffer.title,\n      totalLinesInTrack: totalLines,\n    );\n    allItems.add(headerItem);\n\n    final List<ParsedLyricRow> rows = [];\n    int lineNum = 0;\n    for (final entry in buffer.entries) {\n      if (entry == null) {\n        rows.add(const ParsedLyricRow.stanzaBreak());\n      } else {\n        lineNum++;\n        final item = AnnotatableItem(\n          index: allItems.length,\n          trackIndex: t,\n          trackTitle: buffer.title,\n          kind: AnnotatableTargetKind.line,\n          text: entry,\n          lineNumber: lineNum,\n          totalLinesInTrack: totalLines,\n        );\n        allItems.add(item);\n        rows.add(ParsedLyricRow.line(item));\n      }\n    }\n\n    parsedTracks.add(\n      ParsedLyricTrack(\n        trackIndex: t,\n        title: buffer.title,\n        headerItem: headerItem,\n        rows: rows,\n      ),\n    );\n  }\n\n  return ParsedAlbumLyrics(\n    tracks: parsedTracks,\n    allItems: allItems,\n  );\n}\n\nclass _RawTrackBuffer {\n  final String title;\n  final List<String?> entries = [];\n\n  _RawTrackBuffer(this.title);\n}\n\n/// Registry of all album annotations keyed by normalized album title.\nfinal Map<String, Map<String, TrackBreakdown>> _albumAnnotationsRegistry = {\n  normalizeAnnotationKey(\"santa's cookies\"): santasCookiesAnnotations,\n  normalizeAnnotationKey('blubber'): blubberAnnotations,\n  normalizeAnnotationKey(\"life's lemons\"): lifesLemonsAnnotations,\n};\n\n/// Returns the [TrackBreakdown] for a given album and track title, if available.\nTrackBreakdown? getTrackBreakdown(String albumTitle, String trackTitle) {\n  final albumMap = _albumAnnotationsRegistry[normalizeAnnotationKey(albumTitle)];\n  if (albumMap == null) return null;\n  return albumMap[normalizeAnnotationKey(trackTitle)];\n}\n\n/// Returns the [LyricAnnotation] for a specific line within an album and track.\nLyricAnnotation? getLineAnnotation(\n  String albumTitle,\n  String trackTitle,\n  String line,\n) {\n  final track = getTrackBreakdown(albumTitle, trackTitle);\n  return track?.annotationForLine(line);\n}\n",
  "lib/pages/overheat/overheat_page.dart": "import 'dart:async';\nimport 'dart:math';\n\nimport 'package:flutter/material.dart';\nimport 'package:flutter/services.dart';\n\nenum OverheatPhase {\n  overheating,\n  announcement,\n  fading,\n  fireplace,\n}\n\nclass OverheatPage extends StatefulWidget {\n  const OverheatPage({super.key});\n\n  @override\n  State<OverheatPage> createState() => _OverheatPageState();\n}\n\nclass _OverheatPageState extends State<OverheatPage>\n    with SingleTickerProviderStateMixin {\n  OverheatPhase _phase = OverheatPhase.overheating;\n\n  // Timers\n  Timer? _sequenceTimer;\n  Timer? _shakeTimer;\n  Timer? _logTimer;\n  Timer? _fireTimer;\n  Timer? _cursorTimer;\n\n  // Phase 1: Overheating log simulation & meters\n  final List<String> _overheatLogs = [\n    \"[    0.000000] ACPI: ACPI thermal trip points reached!\",\n    \"[    0.041029] thermal thermal_zone0: critical temperature reached (105 C)\",\n    \"[    0.108231] CPU0: Core temperature above threshold, cpu clock throttled!\",\n    \"[    0.189442] coretemp: TCC activation temperature exceeded on CPU 0..7\",\n    \"[    0.280194] cooling_device0: max cooling state 100% engaged (8500 RPM)\",\n    \"[    0.391002] WARNING: HEAT DISSIPATION SATURATION DETECTED\",\n    \"[    0.512998] ACPI: \\\\_TZ.THM0: CRITICAL THERMAL EVENT IN PROGRESS\",\n    \"[    0.640129] KERNEL PANIC IMMINENT: CPU SILICON EXCEEDING SAFE LIMITS\",\n    \"[    0.781290] TEMPERATURE RUNAWAY: +15°C/s [112°C -> 128°C -> 149°C]\",\n    \"[    0.920194] EMERGENCY: COOLING SUB-SYSTEM FAILURE\",\n    \"[    1.104291] SYSTEM OVERHEATING: HARDWARE THERMAL TRIP DETECTED!\",\n    \"[    1.290112] CRITICAL: FLASHPOINT REACHED IN SYSTEM CORE\",\n  ];\n  final List<String> _displayedLogs = [];\n  int _logIndex = 0;\n  int _temperature = 45;\n  double _shakeX = 0;\n  double _shakeY = 0;\n  bool _redFlash = false;\n  final ScrollController _logScrollController = ScrollController();\n\n  // Phase 2: Announcement\n  bool _showCursor = true;\n\n  // Phase 3 & 4: Fade controller & Full-Screen ASCII Fire simulation\n  late AnimationController _fadeController;\n  late Animation<double> _textOpacityAnimation;\n  late Animation<double> _fireplaceOpacityAnimation;\n\n  final Random _rand = Random();\n\n  // Full-screen dynamic fire grid\n  int _heatCols = 0;\n  int _heatRows = 0;\n  List<List<int>> _heat = [];\n\n  // Flame height fraction (default: ~33% of screen height)\n  double _flameFraction = 0.33;\n  bool _isDragging = false;\n\n  @visibleForTesting\n  double get flameFraction => _flameFraction;\n\n  static const List<String> _fireRamp = [\n    ' ',\n    '.',\n    ':',\n    '-',\n    '=',\n    '+',\n    '*',\n    '#',\n    '%',\n    '@',\n  ];\n\n  static const List<Color> _firePalette = [\n    Colors.transparent,\n    Color(0xFF3E1205), // dark smoky ember\n    Color(0xFF6B1B0C), // dark crimson\n    Color(0xFF9E2300), // deep red\n    Color(0xFFC73600), // red-orange\n    Color(0xFFE85400), // fiery orange\n    Color(0xFFFF7A00), // bright flame orange\n    Color(0xFFFFB300), // warm amber gold\n    Color(0xFFFFEE58), // bright yellow\n    Color(0xFFFFFFFF), // pure white-hot center\n  ];\n\n  @override\n  void initState() {\n    super.initState();\n\n    // Animation controller for fading out announcement and fading in fireplace\n    _fadeController = AnimationController(\n      vsync: this,\n      duration: const Duration(milliseconds: 1000),\n    );\n\n    _textOpacityAnimation = Tween<double>(begin: 1.0, end: 0.0).animate(\n      CurvedAnimation(parent: _fadeController, curve: Curves.easeInOut),\n    );\n\n    _fireplaceOpacityAnimation = Tween<double>(begin: 0.0, end: 1.0).animate(\n      CurvedAnimation(parent: _fadeController, curve: Curves.easeInOut),\n    );\n\n    _fadeController.addStatusListener((status) {\n      if (status == AnimationStatus.completed) {\n        if (mounted) {\n          setState(() {\n            _phase = OverheatPhase.fireplace;\n          });\n        }\n      }\n    });\n\n    _startOverheatingSequence();\n  }\n\n  void _startOverheatingSequence() {\n    // Shake timer\n    _shakeTimer = Timer.periodic(const Duration(milliseconds: 40), (_) {\n      if (!mounted) return;\n      if (_phase == OverheatPhase.overheating) {\n        setState(() {\n          _shakeX = (_rand.nextDouble() * 6) - 3;\n          _shakeY = (_rand.nextDouble() * 6) - 3;\n          _redFlash = !_redFlash;\n        });\n      }\n    });\n\n    // Feed logs and increase temperature rapidly\n    _logTimer = Timer.periodic(const Duration(milliseconds: 250), (timer) {\n      if (!mounted) return;\n      if (_logIndex < _overheatLogs.length) {\n        setState(() {\n          _displayedLogs.add(_overheatLogs[_logIndex]);\n          _logIndex++;\n          _temperature = (_temperature + 12).clamp(45, 185);\n        });\n        if (_logScrollController.hasClients) {\n          _logScrollController.animateTo(\n            _logScrollController.position.maxScrollExtent,\n            duration: const Duration(milliseconds: 100),\n            curve: Curves.easeOut,\n          );\n        }\n      } else {\n        timer.cancel();\n      }\n    });\n\n    // After 3.5 seconds of overheating, transition to announcement\n    _sequenceTimer = Timer(const Duration(milliseconds: 3500), () {\n      if (!mounted) return;\n      _shakeTimer?.cancel();\n      _logTimer?.cancel();\n      setState(() {\n        _phase = OverheatPhase.announcement;\n        _shakeX = 0;\n        _shakeY = 0;\n      });\n\n      // Cursor blinking for announcement (fixed position, no layout shift)\n      _cursorTimer = Timer.periodic(const Duration(milliseconds: 450), (_) {\n        if (!mounted) return;\n        setState(() {\n          _showCursor = !_showCursor;\n        });\n      });\n\n      // Display announcement for 2.8 seconds, then start crossfade to fireplace\n      _sequenceTimer = Timer(const Duration(milliseconds: 2800), () {\n        if (!mounted) return;\n        _cursorTimer?.cancel();\n        _startFireplaceSimulation();\n        setState(() {\n          _phase = OverheatPhase.fading;\n        });\n        _fadeController.forward();\n      });\n    });\n  }\n\n  void _startFireplaceSimulation() {\n    // Fire animation runs indefinitely at ~50ms (~20 FPS matching fireplace-cli)\n    _fireTimer = Timer.periodic(const Duration(milliseconds: 50), (_) {\n      if (!mounted) return;\n      _updateFire();\n      setState(() {});\n    });\n  }\n\n  void _ensureGridSize(int cols, int rows) {\n    if (_heatCols == cols && _heatRows == rows) return;\n    _heatCols = cols;\n    _heatRows = rows;\n    _heat = List.generate(rows, (_) => List.filled(cols, 0));\n  }\n\n  void _updateFire() {\n    if (_heatCols <= 0 || _heatRows <= 0 || _heat.isEmpty) return;\n\n    // 1. Ignite bottom 2 rows with randomized fuel across the entire screen width\n    for (int x = 0; x < _heatCols; x++) {\n      if (_rand.nextDouble() < 0.88) {\n        _heat[_heatRows - 1][x] = 9;\n        _heat[_heatRows - 2][x] = 7 + _rand.nextInt(3);\n      } else {\n        _heat[_heatRows - 1][x] = 5 + _rand.nextInt(4);\n        _heat[_heatRows - 2][x] = _rand.nextInt(5);\n      }\n    }\n\n    // 2. Propagate upward (cellular automaton scaled to _flameFraction of screen height)\n    final double targetRows = max(4.0, _heatRows * _flameFraction);\n    final double baseDecayProb = (7.0 / targetRows).clamp(0.12, 0.88);\n\n    for (int y = 0; y < _heatRows - 2; y++) {\n      final double relativeHeight = (_heatRows - 1 - y) / targetRows;\n      final double decayProb = (baseDecayProb +\n              (relativeHeight > 0.8 ? (relativeHeight - 0.8) * 0.8 : 0.0))\n          .clamp(0.05, 0.95);\n\n      for (int x = 0; x < _heatCols; x++) {\n        int decay = _rand.nextDouble() < decayProb ? 1 : 0;\n        if (relativeHeight > 1.2 && _rand.nextBool()) decay += 1;\n        if (relativeHeight > 1.5) decay += _rand.nextInt(2);\n\n        final int spread = _rand.nextInt(3) - 1; // -1, 0, or 1\n        final int srcX = (x + spread).clamp(0, _heatCols - 1);\n        final int srcY =\n            min(_heatRows - 1, y + 1 + (_rand.nextDouble() < 0.2 ? 1 : 0));\n        _heat[y][x] = max(0, _heat[srcY][srcX] - decay);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  void _exit() {\n    Navigator.of(context).pop();\n  }\n\n  void _adjustFlame(int delta) {\n    setState(() {\n      _flameFraction = (_flameFraction + (delta * 0.05)).clamp(0.10, 0.85);\n    });\n  }\n\n  void _adjustFlameFraction(double delta) {\n    setState(() {\n      _flameFraction = (_flameFraction + delta).clamp(0.10, 0.85);\n    });\n  }\n\n  @override\n  void dispose() {\n    _sequenceTimer?.cancel();\n    _shakeTimer?.cancel();\n    _logTimer?.cancel();\n    _fireTimer?.cancel();\n    _cursorTimer?.cancel();\n    _fadeController.dispose();\n    _logScrollController.dispose();\n    super.dispose();\n  }\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    return KeyboardListener(\n      focusNode: FocusNode()..requestFocus(),\n      onKeyEvent: (event) {\n        if (event is KeyDownEvent) {\n          if (event.logicalKey == LogicalKeyboardKey.escape ||\n              event.logicalKey == LogicalKeyboardKey.keyQ) {\n            _exit();\n          } else if (event.logicalKey == LogicalKeyboardKey.arrowUp ||\n              event.logicalKey == LogicalKeyboardKey.keyW) {\n            _adjustFlame(1);\n          } else if (event.logicalKey == LogicalKeyboardKey.arrowDown ||\n              event.logicalKey == LogicalKeyboardKey.keyS) {\n            _adjustFlame(-1);\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      child: GestureDetector(\n        behavior: HitTestBehavior.opaque,\n        onTap: () {\n          if (_isDragging) return;\n          // If in fireplace stage or fading stage, click anywhere exits\n          if (_phase == OverheatPhase.fireplace ||\n              _phase == OverheatPhase.fading) {\n            _exit();\n          } else {\n            // If user clicks during early overheating, skip directly to fireplace\n            _skipToFireplace();\n          }\n        },\n        onPanStart: (_) {\n          if (_phase == OverheatPhase.fireplace ||\n              _phase == OverheatPhase.fading) {\n            _isDragging = true;\n          }\n        },\n        onPanUpdate: (details) {\n          if (_phase == OverheatPhase.fireplace ||\n              _phase == OverheatPhase.fading) {\n            _isDragging = true;\n            final double screenHeight = MediaQuery.sizeOf(context).height;\n            final double deltaY = details.delta.dy;\n            final double heightFactor = screenHeight > 0 ? screenHeight : 600.0;\n            // Dragging up (negative deltaY) increases flame size;\n            // dragging down (positive deltaY) decreases flame size.\n            _adjustFlameFraction(-deltaY / heightFactor);\n          }\n        },\n        onPanEnd: (_) {\n          Future.microtask(() {\n            if (mounted) {\n              _isDragging = false;\n            }\n          });\n        },\n        onPanCancel: () {\n          Future.microtask(() {\n            if (mounted) {\n              _isDragging = false;\n            }\n          });\n        },\n        child: Scaffold(\n          backgroundColor: Colors.black,\n          body: Stack(\n            fit: StackFit.expand,\n            children: [\n              // Content: overheating alert, announcement, or full-screen fire\n              _buildCurrentPhaseContent(),\n\n              // Subtle CRT red flash vignette during overheating\n              if (_phase == OverheatPhase.overheating && _redFlash)\n                IgnorePointer(\n                  child: Container(\n                    decoration: BoxDecoration(\n                      gradient: RadialGradient(\n                        center: Alignment.center,\n                        radius: 1.2,\n                        colors: [\n                          Colors.transparent,\n                          Colors.red.withValues(alpha: 0.15),\n                        ],\n                      ),\n                    ),\n                  ),\n                ),\n\n              // Close button in top-right\n              Positioned(\n                top: 20,\n                right: 20,\n                child: IconButton(\n                  icon: const Icon(Icons.close, color: Colors.white54, size: 24),\n                  tooltip: \"exit\",\n                  onPressed: _exit,\n                ),\n              ),\n\n              // Instructions / status hint in fireplace mode\n              if (_phase == OverheatPhase.fireplace ||\n                  _phase == OverheatPhase.fading)\n                Positioned(\n                  top: 24,\n                  left: 24,\n                  child: IgnorePointer(\n                    child: Column(\n                      crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.start,\n                      children: [\n                        Text(\n                          \"[ click anywhere to exit ]\",\n                          style: TextStyle(\n                            color: Colors.white.withValues(alpha: 0.35),\n                            fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                            fontSize: 12,\n                            letterSpacing: 1.2,\n                          ),\n                        ),\n                        const SizedBox(height: 4),\n                        Text(\n                          \"[ drag up/down to adjust flames ]\",\n                          style: TextStyle(\n                            color: Colors.white.withValues(alpha: 0.25),\n                            fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                            fontSize: 11,\n                            letterSpacing: 1.1,\n                          ),\n                        ),\n                      ],\n                    ),\n                  ),\n                ),\n            ],\n          ),\n        ),\n      ),\n    );\n  }\n\n  void _skipToFireplace() {\n    _shakeTimer?.cancel();\n    _logTimer?.cancel();\n    _sequenceTimer?.cancel();\n    _cursorTimer?.cancel();\n    _shakeX = 0;\n    _shakeY = 0;\n    _startFireplaceSimulation();\n    setState(() {\n      _phase = OverheatPhase.fireplace;\n    });\n  }\n\n  Widget _buildCurrentPhaseContent() {\n    switch (_phase) {\n      case OverheatPhase.overheating:\n        return Transform.translate(\n          offset: Offset(_shakeX, _shakeY),\n          child: Center(child: _buildOverheatingView()),\n        );\n      case OverheatPhase.announcement:\n        return Center(child: _buildAnnouncementText());\n      case OverheatPhase.fading:\n        return Stack(\n          fit: StackFit.expand,\n          children: [\n            FadeTransition(\n              opacity: _fireplaceOpacityAnimation,\n              child: _buildFullScreenFire(),\n            ),\n            Center(\n              child: FadeTransition(\n                opacity: _textOpacityAnimation,\n                child: _buildAnnouncementText(),\n              ),\n            ),\n          ],\n        );\n      case OverheatPhase.fireplace:\n        return _buildFullScreenFire();\n    }\n  }\n\n  // --- Phase 1: Overheating Alert & Logs ---\n  Widget _buildOverheatingView() {\n    return LayoutBuilder(\n      builder: (context, constraints) {\n        final isMobile = constraints.maxWidth < 600;\n        final double logHeight =\n            (constraints.maxHeight * 0.40).clamp(160.0, 280.0);\n\n        return ConstrainedBox(\n          constraints: const BoxConstraints(maxWidth: 720),\n          child: Padding(\n            padding: EdgeInsets.symmetric(\n              horizontal: isMobile ? 16.0 : 24.0,\n              vertical: isMobile ? 16.0 : 32.0,\n            ),\n            child: Column(\n              mainAxisAlignment: MainAxisAlignment.center,\n              crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.stretch,\n              children: [\n                // Warning Box\n                Container(\n                  padding: EdgeInsets.all(isMobile ? 12.0 : 16.0),\n                  decoration: BoxDecoration(\n                    color: Colors.red.withValues(alpha: 0.12),\n                    border: Border.all(\n                      color: _redFlash ? Colors.redAccent : Colors.deepOrange,\n                      width: 2,\n                    ),\n                    borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(4),\n                  ),\n                  child: Column(\n                    children: [\n                      FittedBox(\n                        fit: BoxFit.scaleDown,\n                        child: Row(\n                          mainAxisAlignment: MainAxisAlignment.center,\n                          children: [\n                            Icon(\n                              Icons.warning_amber_rounded,\n                              color: _redFlash\n                                  ? Colors.redAccent\n                                  : Colors.orangeAccent,\n                              size: isMobile ? 22 : 28,\n                            ),\n                            const SizedBox(width: 8),\n                            Text(\n                              \"SYSTEM OVERHEATING\",\n                              style: TextStyle(\n                                color: _redFlash\n                                    ? Colors.redAccent\n                                    : Colors.orangeAccent,\n                                fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                                fontSize: isMobile ? 18 : 22,\n                                fontWeight: FontWeight.bold,\n                                letterSpacing: isMobile ? 1.2 : 2.0,\n                              ),\n                            ),\n                          ],\n                        ),\n                      ),\n                      const SizedBox(height: 10),\n                      FittedBox(\n                        fit: BoxFit.scaleDown,\n                        child: Text(\n                          \"THERMAL RUNAWAY // TEMP: \$_temperature°C // CRITICAL\",\n                          style: TextStyle(\n                            color: Colors.white,\n                            fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                            fontSize: isMobile ? 11 : 13,\n                            fontWeight: FontWeight.bold,\n                            letterSpacing: 1.1,\n                          ),\n                          textAlign: TextAlign.center,\n                        ),\n                      ),\n                    ],\n                  ),\n                ),\n                const SizedBox(height: 20),\n\n                // Live Kernel Thermal Log Output\n                Container(\n                  height: logHeight,\n                  padding: const EdgeInsets.all(16),\n                  decoration: BoxDecoration(\n                    color: Colors.white.withValues(alpha: 0.03),\n                    border: Border.all(color: Colors.white24),\n                    borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(4),\n                  ),\n                  child: ListView.builder(\n                    controller: _logScrollController,\n                    itemCount: _displayedLogs.length,\n                    itemBuilder: (context, index) {\n                      final log = _displayedLogs[index];\n                      final isCrit = log.contains(\"CRITICAL\") ||\n                          log.contains(\"OVERHEATING\") ||\n                          log.contains(\"PANIC\") ||\n                          log.contains(\"EMERGENCY\");\n                      return Padding(\n                        padding: const EdgeInsets.symmetric(vertical: 3.0),\n                        child: Text(\n                          log,\n                          style: TextStyle(\n                            color: isCrit ? Colors.redAccent : Colors.white70,\n                            fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                            fontSize: isMobile ? 11 : 12,\n                            height: 1.3,\n                          ),\n                        ),\n                      );\n                    },\n                  ),\n                ),\n              ],\n            ),\n          ),\n        );\n      },\n    );\n  }\n\n  // --- Phase 2: Announcement ---\n  // Symmetrical layout prevents any horizontal shifting when cursor blinks\n  Widget _buildAnnouncementText() {\n    return Padding(\n      padding: const EdgeInsets.symmetric(horizontal: 24.0),\n      child: LayoutBuilder(\n        builder: (context, constraints) {\n          final isDesktop = constraints.maxWidth >= 768;\n          final double fontSize = isDesktop ? 30 : 20;\n\n          final textStyle = TextStyle(\n            color: Colors.white,\n            fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n            fontSize: fontSize,\n            fontWeight: FontWeight.bold,\n            letterSpacing: 1.5,\n            shadows: const [\n              Shadow(color: Colors.white38, blurRadius: 20),\n            ],\n          );\n\n          final cursorStyle = TextStyle(\n            color: Colors.white,\n            fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n            fontSize: fontSize,\n            fontWeight: FontWeight.bold,\n          );\n\n          return FittedBox(\n            fit: BoxFit.scaleDown,\n            child: Row(\n              mainAxisSize: MainAxisSize.min,\n              mainAxisAlignment: MainAxisAlignment.center,\n              children: [\n                // Hidden dummy cursor on left to perfectly balance the right cursor\n                Opacity(\n                  opacity: 0.0,\n                  child: Text(\"_\", style: cursorStyle),\n                ),\n                Text(\n                  \"third-degree coming march 2027\",\n                  style: textStyle,\n                  textAlign: TextAlign.center,\n                ),\n                // Visible blinking cursor on right - Opacity changes paint only, zero layout change\n                Opacity(\n                  opacity: _showCursor ? 1.0 : 0.0,\n                  child: Text(\"_\", style: cursorStyle),\n                ),\n              ],\n            ),\n          );\n        },\n      ),\n    );\n  }\n\n  // --- Phase 4: Full-Screen ASCII Fire (fireplace-cli aesthetic) ---\n  Widget _buildFullScreenFire() {\n    return LayoutBuilder(\n      builder: (context, constraints) {\n        final double width = constraints.maxWidth;\n        final double height = constraints.maxHeight;\n\n        // Responsive font sizing to densely fill the screen\n        final double fontSize = width < 600 ? 10.0 : 13.0;\n        final double charWidth = fontSize * 0.60;\n        final double charHeight = fontSize * 1.15;\n\n        final int cols = max(30, (width / charWidth).ceil() + 1);\n        final int rows = max(15, (height / charHeight).ceil() + 1);\n\n        _ensureGridSize(cols, rows);\n\n        if (_heat.isEmpty || _heatRows != rows || _heatCols != cols) {\n          return const SizedBox.expand();\n        }\n\n        // Build spans using Run-Length Encoding (RLE) for high performance\n        final spans = <TextSpan>[];\n\n        for (int y = 0; y < rows; y++) {\n          int currentHeat = _heat[y][0].clamp(0, 9);\n          int runCount = 0;\n\n          for (int x = 0; x < cols; x++) {\n            final int h = _heat[y][x].clamp(0, 9);\n            if (h == currentHeat) {\n              runCount++;\n            } else {\n              if (runCount > 0) {\n                spans.add(\n                  TextSpan(\n                    text: _fireRamp[currentHeat] * runCount,\n                    style: TextStyle(\n                      color: _firePalette[currentHeat],\n                      fontWeight:\n                          currentHeat >= 7 ? FontWeight.bold : FontWeight.normal,\n                    ),\n                  ),\n                );\n              }\n              currentHeat = h;\n              runCount = 1;\n            }\n          }\n          if (runCount > 0) {\n            spans.add(\n              TextSpan(\n                text: _fireRamp[currentHeat] * runCount,\n                style: TextStyle(\n                  color: _firePalette[currentHeat],\n                  fontWeight:\n                      currentHeat >= 7 ? FontWeight.bold : FontWeight.normal,\n                ),\n              ),\n            );\n          }\n          if (y < rows - 1) {\n            spans.add(const TextSpan(text: '\\n'));\n          }\n        }\n\n        return ClipRect(\n          child: SizedBox(\n            width: width,\n            height: height,\n            child: Align(\n              alignment: Alignment.bottomCenter,\n              child: SizedBox(\n                width: cols * charWidth,\n                height: rows * charHeight,\n                child: Text.rich(\n                  TextSpan(children: spans),\n                  style: TextStyle(\n                    fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                    fontSize: fontSize,\n                    height: 1.15,\n                    letterSpacing: 0,\n                  ),\n                  softWrap: false,\n                  overflow: TextOverflow.clip,\n                ),\n              ),\n            ),\n          ),\n        );\n      },\n    );\n  }\n}\n",
  "lib/pages/source_code/file_tree.dart": "import 'package:flutter/material.dart';\n\nclass FileNode {\n  final String name;\n  final String? fullPath;\n  final List<FileNode> children;\n\n  FileNode({required this.name, this.fullPath, List<FileNode>? children})\n      : children = children ?? [];\n\n  bool get isFile => fullPath != null;\n}\n\nclass FileTreeWidget extends StatelessWidget {\n  final Map<String, String> files;\n  final String? selectedFile;\n  final ValueChanged<String> onFileSelected;\n\n  const FileTreeWidget({\n    super.key,\n    required this.files,\n    this.selectedFile,\n    required this.onFileSelected,\n  });\n\n  FileNode _buildTree() {\n    final root = FileNode(name: 'archbtw.sh');\n    final libNode = FileNode(name: 'lib');\n    root.children.add(libNode);\n\n    for (final path in files.keys) {\n      final cleanPath = path.startsWith('lib/') ? path.substring(4) : path;\n      final parts = cleanPath.split('/');\n      var current = libNode;\n      for (var i = 0; i < parts.length; i++) {\n        final part = parts[i];\n        final isFile = i == parts.length - 1;\n\n        var child = current.children.cast<FileNode?>().firstWhere(\n            (n) => n!.name == part,\n            orElse: () => null);\n        if (child == null) {\n          child = FileNode(\n            name: part,\n            fullPath: isFile ? path : null,\n          );\n          current.children.add(child);\n        }\n        current = child;\n      }\n    }\n    \n    _sortNode(libNode);\n    return root;\n  }\n\n  void _sortNode(FileNode node) {\n    node.children.sort((a, b) {\n      if (a.isFile && !b.isFile) return 1;\n      if (!a.isFile && b.isFile) return -1;\n      return a.name.compareTo(b.name);\n    });\n    for (final child in node.children) {\n      _sortNode(child);\n    }\n  }\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    final root = _buildTree();\n    return Container(\n      color: const Color(0xFF0D0D0D), // very dark background for sidebar\n      child: Column(\n        crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.start,\n        children: [\n          const Padding(\n            padding: EdgeInsets.fromLTRB(16, 12, 16, 8),\n            child: Text(\n              'EXPLORER',\n              style: TextStyle(\n                fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                fontSize: 11,\n                color: Colors.white54,\n                letterSpacing: 1.2,\n                fontWeight: FontWeight.bold,\n              ),\n            ),\n          ),\n          Expanded(\n            child: ListView(\n              padding: EdgeInsets.zero,\n              children: [\n                _TreeNodeWidget(\n                  node: root,\n                  level: 0,\n                  selectedFile: selectedFile,\n                  onFileSelected: onFileSelected,\n                  initiallyExpanded: true,\n                ),\n              ],\n            ),\n          ),\n        ],\n      ),\n    );\n  }\n}\n\nclass _TreeNodeWidget extends StatefulWidget {\n  final FileNode node;\n  final int level;\n  final String? selectedFile;\n  final ValueChanged<String> onFileSelected;\n  final bool initiallyExpanded;\n\n  const _TreeNodeWidget({\n    required this.node,\n    required this.level,\n    required this.selectedFile,\n    required this.onFileSelected,\n    this.initiallyExpanded = false,\n  });\n\n  @override\n  State<_TreeNodeWidget> createState() => _TreeNodeWidgetState();\n}\n\nclass _TreeNodeWidgetState extends State<_TreeNodeWidget> {\n  late bool _isExpanded;\n\n  @override\n  void initState() {\n    super.initState();\n    _isExpanded = widget.initiallyExpanded || widget.level <= 1;\n  }\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    if (widget.node.isFile) {\n      final isSelected = widget.node.fullPath == widget.selectedFile;\n      return InkWell(\n        onTap: () => widget.onFileSelected(widget.node.fullPath!),\n        child: Container(\n          color: isSelected ? Colors.white.withOpacity(0.1) : Colors.transparent,\n          padding: EdgeInsets.only(left: 16.0 + (widget.level * 12.0), top: 4, bottom: 4, right: 8),\n          child: Row(\n            children: [\n              const Icon(Icons.insert_drive_file, size: 14, color: Colors.white70),\n              const SizedBox(width: 6),\n              Expanded(\n                child: Text(\n                  widget.node.name,\n                  style: TextStyle(\n                    fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                    fontSize: 13,\n                    color: isSelected ? Colors.white : Colors.white70,\n                  ),\n                  overflow: TextOverflow.ellipsis,\n                ),\n              ),\n            ],\n          ),\n        ),\n      );\n    } else {\n      return Column(\n        crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.start,\n        children: [\n          InkWell(\n            onTap: () {\n              setState(() {\n                _isExpanded = !_isExpanded;\n              });\n            },\n            child: Container(\n              padding: EdgeInsets.only(left: 8.0 + (widget.level * 12.0), top: 4, bottom: 4, right: 8),\n              child: Row(\n                children: [\n                  Icon(\n                    _isExpanded ? Icons.keyboard_arrow_down : Icons.keyboard_arrow_right,\n                    size: 16,\n                    color: Colors.white54,\n                  ),\n                  const SizedBox(width: 2),\n                  const Icon(Icons.folder, size: 14, color: Color(0xFF9E75FF)), // purple folder\n                  const SizedBox(width: 6),\n                  Expanded(\n                    child: Text(\n                      widget.node.name,\n                      style: const TextStyle(\n                        fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                        fontSize: 13,\n                        color: Colors.white,\n                        fontWeight: FontWeight.w500,\n                      ),\n                      overflow: TextOverflow.ellipsis,\n                    ),\n                  ),\n                ],\n              ),\n            ),\n          ),\n          if (_isExpanded)\n            ...widget.node.children.map((child) => _TreeNodeWidget(\n                  node: child,\n                  level: widget.level + 1,\n                  selectedFile: widget.selectedFile,\n                  onFileSelected: widget.onFileSelected,\n                )),\n        ],\n      );\n    }\n  }\n}\n",
  "lib/pages/source_code/source_code_page.dart": "import 'package:archbtw_sh/generated/source_code.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/pages/source_code/file_tree.dart';\nimport 'package:flutter/material.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/widgets/selectable_highlight_view.dart';\nimport 'package:flutter_highlight/themes/atom-one-dark.dart';\n\nclass SourceCodePage extends StatefulWidget {\n  const SourceCodePage({super.key});\n\n  @override\n  State<SourceCodePage> createState() => _SourceCodePageState();\n}\n\nclass _SourceCodePageState extends State<SourceCodePage> {\n  String? _selectedFile = 'lib/main.dart';\n\n  final GlobalKey<ScaffoldState> _scaffoldKey = GlobalKey<ScaffoldState>();\n\n  Widget _buildTopBar(bool isDesktop) {\n    return Container(\n      height: 40,\n      color: const Color(0xFF0D0D0D),\n      padding: const EdgeInsets.symmetric(horizontal: 16),\n      child: Row(\n        children: [\n          IconButton(\n            icon: const Icon(Icons.arrow_back, color: Colors.white70, size: 20),\n            onPressed: () {\n              Navigator.pop(context); // Go back home\n            },\n            tooltip: 'Back to Home',\n            padding: EdgeInsets.zero,\n            constraints: const BoxConstraints(),\n          ),\n          const Spacer(),\n          const Text(\n            'archBTW.sh',\n            style: TextStyle(\n              fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n              fontSize: 14,\n              color: Colors.white70,\n              fontWeight: FontWeight.bold,\n            ),\n          ),\n          const Spacer(),\n          if (!isDesktop)\n            IconButton(\n              icon: const Icon(Icons.menu, color: Colors.white70, size: 20),\n              onPressed: () {\n                _scaffoldKey.currentState?.openDrawer();\n              },\n              tooltip: 'files',\n              padding: EdgeInsets.zero,\n              constraints: const BoxConstraints(),\n            )\n          else\n            const SizedBox(width: 20),\n        ],\n      ),\n    );\n  }\n\n  Widget _buildCodeViewer(String content, bool isDesktop) {\n    final lines = content.split('\\n');\n    final double fontSize = isDesktop ? 14 : 11;\n\n    return SelectionArea(\n      child: SingleChildScrollView(\n        padding: const EdgeInsets.all(16.0),\n        child: SingleChildScrollView(\n          scrollDirection: Axis.horizontal,\n          child: Row(\n            crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.start,\n            children: [\n              // Line numbers\n              SelectionContainer.disabled(\n                child: Column(\n                  crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.end,\n                  children: List.generate(lines.length, (index) {\n                    return Text(\n                      '\${index + 1}',\n                      style: TextStyle(\n                        fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                        fontSize: fontSize,\n                        color: Colors.white38,\n                        height: 1.5,\n                      ),\n                    );\n                  }),\n                ),\n              ),\n              const SizedBox(width: 16),\n              // Code\n              SelectableHighlightView(\n                content,\n                language: 'dart',\n                theme: {\n                  ...atomOneDarkTheme,\n                  'root': TextStyle(\n                    backgroundColor: const Color(0xFF0D0D0D),\n                    color:\n                        atomOneDarkTheme['root']?.color ??\n                        const Color(0xffabb2bf),\n                  ),\n                },\n                padding: EdgeInsets.zero,\n                textStyle: TextStyle(\n                  fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                  fontSize: fontSize,\n                  height: 1.5,\n                ),\n              ),\n            ],\n          ),\n        ),\n      ),\n    );\n  }\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    final screenWidth = MediaQuery.of(context).size.width;\n    final isDesktop = screenWidth >= 768.0;\n\n    final fileTreeWidget = FileTreeWidget(\n      files: sourceCodeFiles,\n      selectedFile: _selectedFile,\n      onFileSelected: (path) {\n        setState(() {\n          _selectedFile = path;\n        });\n        if (!isDesktop) {\n          Navigator.of(context).pop(); // Close drawer\n        }\n      },\n    );\n\n    final String? fileName = _selectedFile?.split('/').last;\n    final content = _selectedFile != null\n        ? sourceCodeFiles[_selectedFile!]\n        : null;\n\n    final codeViewerWidget = Container(\n      color: const Color(0xFF0D0D0D), // Match sidebar background\n      width: double.infinity,\n      height: double.infinity,\n      child: Column(\n        crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.start,\n        children: [\n          if (fileName != null)\n            Container(\n              color: const Color(0xFF0D0D0D),\n              child: Row(\n                children: [\n                  Container(\n                    padding: const EdgeInsets.symmetric(\n                      horizontal: 16,\n                      vertical: 8,\n                    ),\n                    decoration: const BoxDecoration(\n                      color: Color(0xFF0D0D0D), // Match the background\n                      border: Border(\n                        top: BorderSide(color: Colors.blueAccent, width: 2),\n                      ),\n                    ),\n                    child: Row(\n                      children: [\n                        Text(\n                          fileName,\n                          style: const TextStyle(\n                            fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                            color: Colors.white,\n                            fontSize: 13,\n                          ),\n                        ),\n                        const SizedBox(width: 8),\n                        const Icon(\n                          Icons.close,\n                          size: 14,\n                          color: Colors.white54,\n                        ),\n                      ],\n                    ),\n                  ),\n                ],\n              ),\n            ),\n          Expanded(\n            child: content == null\n                ? const Center(\n                    child: Text(\n                      'Select a file to view its source code.',\n                      style: TextStyle(\n                        fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                        color: Colors.white54,\n                      ),\n                    ),\n                  )\n                : _buildCodeViewer(content, isDesktop),\n          ),\n        ],\n      ),\n    );\n\n    return Scaffold(\n      key: _scaffoldKey,\n      backgroundColor: const Color(0xFF0D0D0D),\n      drawer: isDesktop ? null : Drawer(child: fileTreeWidget),\n      body: SafeArea(\n        child: Column(\n          children: [\n            _buildTopBar(isDesktop),\n            Expanded(\n              child: isDesktop\n                  ? Row(\n                      crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.start,\n                      children: [\n                        SizedBox(width: 250, child: fileTreeWidget),\n                        Expanded(child: codeViewerWidget),\n                      ],\n                    )\n                  : codeViewerWidget,\n            ),\n          ],\n        ),\n      ),\n    );\n  }\n}\n",
  "lib/widgets/floating_music_toast.dart": "import 'dart:ui';\n\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/global/colors.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/global/site_music_controller.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/widgets/in_game_music_hud.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/widgets/marquee_text.dart';\nimport 'package:flutter/material.dart';\n\nclass FloatingMusicToast extends StatelessWidget {\n  const FloatingMusicToast({super.key});\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    final controller = SiteMusicController.instance;\n\n    return ListenableBuilder(\n      listenable: controller,\n      builder: (context, _) {\n        if (!controller.shouldShowFloatingToast) {\n          return const SizedBox.shrink();\n        }\n\n        final String trackTitle = cleanTrackTitle(controller.currentTrackName);\n        final String albumTitle = controller.albumTitle ?? 'archbtw.sh';\n        final bool isPlaying = controller.isPlaying;\n\n        return SafeArea(\n          child: Align(\n            alignment: Alignment.bottomRight,\n            child: Padding(\n              padding: const EdgeInsets.only(\n                left: 16,\n                right: 16,\n                bottom: 16,\n              ),\n              child: ConstrainedBox(\n                constraints: const BoxConstraints(maxWidth: 380),\n                child: ClipRRect(\n                  borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(10),\n                  child: BackdropFilter(\n                    filter: ImageFilter.blur(sigmaX: 12, sigmaY: 12),\n                    child: Material(\n                      key: const Key('floating_music_toast'),\n                      color: const Color(0xEB0A0E17),\n                      shape: RoundedRectangleBorder(\n                        borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(10),\n                        side: BorderSide(\n                          color: kAccentColor.withValues(alpha: 0.75),\n                          width: 1.2,\n                        ),\n                      ),\n                      elevation: 10,\n                      child: Padding(\n                        padding: const EdgeInsets.symmetric(\n                          horizontal: 12,\n                          vertical: 10,\n                        ),\n                        child: Row(\n                          mainAxisSize: MainAxisSize.min,\n                          children: [\n                            Container(\n                              width: 30,\n                              height: 30,\n                              decoration: BoxDecoration(\n                                color: kAccentColor.withValues(alpha: 0.14),\n                                borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(6),\n                                border: Border.all(\n                                  color: kAccentColor.withValues(alpha: 0.5),\n                                ),\n                              ),\n                              child: Icon(\n                                isPlaying\n                                    ? Icons.graphic_eq\n                                    : Icons.music_note_outlined,\n                                color: kAccentColor,\n                                size: 16,\n                              ),\n                            ),\n                            const SizedBox(width: 10),\n                            Expanded(\n                              child: Column(\n                                mainAxisSize: MainAxisSize.min,\n                                crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.start,\n                                children: [\n                                  Text(\n                                    '// \$albumTitle',\n                                    maxLines: 1,\n                                    overflow: TextOverflow.ellipsis,\n                                    style: TextStyle(\n                                      color: kAccentColor.withValues(alpha: 0.8),\n                                      fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                                      fontSize: 10,\n                                      fontWeight: FontWeight.bold,\n                                      letterSpacing: 0.6,\n                                    ),\n                                  ),\n                                  const SizedBox(height: 2),\n                                  MarqueeText(\n                                    text: trackTitle,\n                                    style: const TextStyle(\n                                      color: Colors.white,\n                                      fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                                      fontSize: 12,\n                                      fontWeight: FontWeight.w600,\n                                    ),\n                                  ),\n                                ],\n                              ),\n                            ),\n                            const SizedBox(width: 6),\n                            _ToastButton(\n                              buttonKey: const Key('toast_prev_button'),\n                              tooltip: 'Previous Track',\n                              icon: Icons.skip_previous_rounded,\n                              onTap: controller.previous,\n                            ),\n                            const SizedBox(width: 2),\n                            _ToastButton(\n                              buttonKey: const Key('toast_play_pause_button'),\n                              tooltip: isPlaying ? 'Pause' : 'Play',\n                              icon: isPlaying\n                                  ? Icons.pause_rounded\n                                  : Icons.play_arrow_rounded,\n                              isPrimary: true,\n                              onTap: controller.togglePlayPause,\n                            ),\n                            const SizedBox(width: 2),\n                            _ToastButton(\n                              buttonKey: const Key('toast_next_button'),\n                              tooltip: 'Next Track',\n                              icon: Icons.skip_next_rounded,\n                              onTap: controller.next,\n                            ),\n                            const SizedBox(width: 4),\n                            _ToastButton(\n                              buttonKey: const Key('toast_close_button'),\n                              tooltip: 'Stop & Close',\n                              icon: Icons.close_rounded,\n                              iconSize: 15,\n                              onTap: controller.stopAndDismiss,\n                            ),\n                          ],\n                        ),\n                      ),\n                    ),\n                  ),\n                ),\n              ),\n            ),\n          ),\n        );\n      },\n    );\n  }\n}\n\nclass _ToastButton extends StatelessWidget {\n  final Key buttonKey;\n  final String tooltip;\n  final IconData icon;\n  final VoidCallback onTap;\n  final bool isPrimary;\n  final double iconSize;\n\n  const _ToastButton({\n    required this.buttonKey,\n    required this.tooltip,\n    required this.icon,\n    required this.onTap,\n    this.isPrimary = false,\n    this.iconSize = 18,\n  });\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    return InkWell(\n      key: buttonKey,\n      onTap: onTap,\n      borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(6),\n      child: Container(\n        padding: const EdgeInsets.all(5),\n        decoration: BoxDecoration(\n          color: isPrimary\n              ? kAccentColor.withValues(alpha: 0.2)\n              : Colors.white.withValues(alpha: 0.05),\n          borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(6),\n          border: Border.all(\n            color: isPrimary\n                ? kAccentColor.withValues(alpha: 0.85)\n                : Colors.white24,\n          ),\n        ),\n        child: Icon(\n          icon,\n          size: iconSize,\n          color: isPrimary ? kAccentColor : Colors.white,\n        ),\n      ),\n    );\n  }\n}\n",
  "lib/widgets/in_game_music_hud.dart": "import 'package:archbtw_sh/global/colors.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/widgets/marquee_text.dart';\nimport 'package:audioplayers/audioplayers.dart';\nimport 'package:flutter/material.dart';\n\nvoid configureBackgroundAudioContext() {\n  try {\n    AudioPlayer.global.setAudioContext(\n      AudioContext(\n        iOS: AudioContextIOS(\n          category: AVAudioSessionCategory.playback,\n        ),\n        android: const AudioContextAndroid(\n          isSpeakerphoneOn: false,\n          stayAwake: true,\n          contentType: AndroidContentType.music,\n          usageType: AndroidUsageType.media,\n          audioFocus: AndroidAudioFocus.gain,\n        ),\n      ),\n    );\n  } catch (_) {\n    // Ignore on platforms or test environments where AudioContext isn't supported\n  }\n}\n\nString cleanTrackTitle(String filename) {\n  return filename\n      .replaceAll('.wav', '')\n      .replaceAll('.m4a', '')\n      .replaceAll('_', ' ');\n}\n\nclass InGameMusicHud extends StatelessWidget {\n  final String currentTrack;\n  final bool isPlaying;\n  final VoidCallback onPrevious;\n  final VoidCallback onNext;\n  final VoidCallback onPlayPause;\n  final Color accentColor;\n\n  const InGameMusicHud({\n    super.key,\n    required this.currentTrack,\n    required this.isPlaying,\n    required this.onPrevious,\n    required this.onNext,\n    required this.onPlayPause,\n    this.accentColor = kAccentColor,\n  });\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    final String displayTitle = cleanTrackTitle(currentTrack);\n\n    return Container(\n      height: 36,\n      padding: const EdgeInsets.symmetric(horizontal: 10),\n      decoration: BoxDecoration(\n        color: Colors.black.withValues(alpha: 0.72),\n        border: Border(\n          bottom: BorderSide(\n            color: accentColor.withValues(alpha: 0.35),\n            width: 1,\n          ),\n        ),\n      ),\n      child: Row(\n        children: [\n          Icon(\n            Icons.music_note,\n            color: accentColor,\n            size: 15,\n          ),\n          const SizedBox(width: 6),\n          Expanded(\n            child: MarqueeText(\n              text: displayTitle.isEmpty ? 'loading track...' : displayTitle,\n              style: const TextStyle(\n                color: Colors.white,\n                fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                fontSize: 12,\n                fontWeight: FontWeight.w600,\n              ),\n            ),\n          ),\n          const SizedBox(width: 8),\n          _HudIconButton(\n            key: const Key('music_prev_button'),\n            tooltip: 'Previous Track',\n            icon: Icons.skip_previous,\n            color: Colors.white70,\n            onTap: onPrevious,\n          ),\n          const SizedBox(width: 2),\n          _HudIconButton(\n            key: const Key('music_play_pause_button'),\n            tooltip: isPlaying ? 'Pause' : 'Play',\n            icon: isPlaying ? Icons.pause : Icons.play_arrow,\n            color: accentColor,\n            onTap: onPlayPause,\n          ),\n          const SizedBox(width: 2),\n          _HudIconButton(\n            key: const Key('music_next_button'),\n            tooltip: 'Next Track',\n            icon: Icons.skip_next,\n            color: Colors.white70,\n            onTap: onNext,\n          ),\n        ],\n      ),\n    );\n  }\n}\n\nclass _HudIconButton extends StatelessWidget {\n  final String tooltip;\n  final IconData icon;\n  final Color color;\n  final VoidCallback onTap;\n\n  const _HudIconButton({\n    super.key,\n    required this.tooltip,\n    required this.icon,\n    required this.color,\n    required this.onTap,\n  });\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    return Tooltip(\n      message: tooltip,\n      child: InkWell(\n        onTap: onTap,\n        borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(6),\n        child: Padding(\n          padding: const EdgeInsets.symmetric(horizontal: 6, vertical: 4),\n          child: Icon(icon, color: color, size: 18),\n        ),\n      ),\n    );\n  }\n}\n\n",
  "lib/widgets/loading_waveform.dart": "import 'dart:math' as math;\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/global/colors.dart';\nimport 'package:flutter/material.dart';\n\nclass WaveformLoader extends StatefulWidget {\n  final double height;\n  final double barWidth;\n  final Color? color;\n\n  const WaveformLoader({\n    super.key,\n    this.height = 50.0,\n    this.barWidth = 4.0,\n    this.color,\n  });\n\n  @override\n  State<WaveformLoader> createState() => _WaveformLoaderState();\n}\n\nclass _WaveformLoaderState extends State<WaveformLoader>\n    with SingleTickerProviderStateMixin {\n  late AnimationController _controller;\n\n  @override\n  void initState() {\n    super.initState();\n    _controller = AnimationController(\n      vsync: this,\n      duration: const Duration(milliseconds: 1200),\n    )..repeat();\n  }\n\n  @override\n  void dispose() {\n    _controller.dispose();\n    super.dispose();\n  }\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    final color = Colors.white;\n\n    return SizedBox(\n      height: widget.height,\n      child: Row(\n        mainAxisSize: MainAxisSize.min,\n        mainAxisAlignment: MainAxisAlignment.center,\n        crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.center,\n        children: List.generate(5, (index) {\n          final double delayFactor = index * (1 / 12);\n\n          return AnimatedBuilder(\n            animation: _controller,\n            builder: (context, child) {\n              double t = (_controller.value - delayFactor) % 1.0;\n\n              double sinVal = math.sin(t * 2 * math.pi);\n\n              double normalized = (sinVal + 1) / 2;\n              double scale = 0.1 + (normalized * 0.9);\n\n              return Container(\n                width: widget.barWidth,\n                height: widget.height * scale,\n                margin: const EdgeInsets.symmetric(horizontal: 3.0),\n                decoration: BoxDecoration(\n                  color: color,\n                  borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(99),\n                ),\n              );\n            },\n          );\n        }),\n      ),\n    );\n  }\n}\n",
  "lib/widgets/marquee_text.dart": "import 'package:flutter/material.dart';\n\nclass MarqueeText extends StatefulWidget {\n  final String text;\n  final TextStyle style;\n  final double gap;\n  final double pixelsPerSecond;\n\n  const MarqueeText({\n    super.key,\n    required this.text,\n    required this.style,\n    this.gap = 36.0,\n    this.pixelsPerSecond = 35.0,\n  });\n\n  @override\n  State<MarqueeText> createState() => _MarqueeTextState();\n}\n\nclass _MarqueeTextState extends State<MarqueeText>\n    with SingleTickerProviderStateMixin {\n  late AnimationController _controller;\n\n  @override\n  void initState() {\n    super.initState();\n    _controller = AnimationController(\n      vsync: this,\n      duration: const Duration(seconds: 8),\n    )..repeat();\n  }\n\n  @override\n  void didUpdateWidget(covariant MarqueeText oldWidget) {\n    super.didUpdateWidget(oldWidget);\n    if (oldWidget.text != widget.text) {\n      _controller.forward(from: 0.0);\n      _controller.repeat();\n    }\n  }\n\n  @override\n  void dispose() {\n    _controller.dispose();\n    super.dispose();\n  }\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    return LayoutBuilder(\n      builder: (context, constraints) {\n        final TextPainter tp = TextPainter(\n          text: TextSpan(text: widget.text, style: widget.style),\n          maxLines: 1,\n          textDirection: TextDirection.ltr,\n        )..layout();\n\n        final double textWidth = tp.width;\n        final double maxWidth = constraints.maxWidth;\n\n        // If the text fits comfortably, render static text without scrolling\n        if (!maxWidth.isFinite || textWidth <= maxWidth) {\n          return Text(\n            widget.text,\n            style: widget.style,\n            maxLines: 1,\n            overflow: TextOverflow.clip,\n          );\n        }\n\n        final double loopDistance = textWidth + widget.gap;\n        final int durationMs =\n            ((loopDistance / widget.pixelsPerSecond) * 1000).round().clamp(\n                  2500,\n                  30000,\n                );\n        if (_controller.duration?.inMilliseconds != durationMs) {\n          _controller.duration = Duration(milliseconds: durationMs);\n          if (!_controller.isAnimating) {\n            _controller.repeat();\n          }\n        }\n\n        return ClipRect(\n          child: SizedBox(\n            width: maxWidth,\n            height: tp.height * 1.15,\n            child: AnimatedBuilder(\n              animation: _controller,\n              builder: (context, _) {\n                final double offset = -(_controller.value * loopDistance);\n                return OverflowBox(\n                  alignment: Alignment.centerLeft,\n                  minWidth: 0,\n                  maxWidth: double.infinity,\n                  child: Transform.translate(\n                    offset: Offset(offset, 0),\n                    child: Row(\n                      mainAxisSize: MainAxisSize.min,\n                      children: [\n                        Text(widget.text, style: widget.style, maxLines: 1),\n                        SizedBox(width: widget.gap),\n                        Text(widget.text, style: widget.style, maxLines: 1),\n                      ],\n                    ),\n                  ),\n                );\n              },\n            ),\n          ),\n        );\n      },\n    );\n  }\n}\n\n",
  "lib/widgets/selectable_highlight_view.dart": "import 'package:flutter/material.dart';\nimport 'package:highlight/highlight.dart' show highlight, Node;\n\nclass SelectableHighlightView extends StatelessWidget {\n  final String source;\n  final String? language;\n  final Map<String, TextStyle> theme;\n  final EdgeInsetsGeometry? padding;\n  final TextStyle? textStyle;\n\n  SelectableHighlightView(\n    String input, {\n    super.key,\n    this.language,\n    this.theme = const {},\n    this.padding,\n    this.textStyle,\n    int tabSize = 8,\n  }) : source = input.replaceAll('\\t', ' ' * tabSize);\n\n  List<TextSpan> _convert(List<Node> nodes) {\n    List<TextSpan> spans = [];\n    var currentSpans = spans;\n    List<List<TextSpan>> stack = [];\n\n    void _traverse(Node node) {\n      if (node.value != null) {\n        currentSpans.add(\n          node.className == null\n              ? TextSpan(text: node.value)\n              : TextSpan(text: node.value, style: theme[node.className!]),\n        );\n      } else if (node.children != null) {\n        List<TextSpan> tmp = [];\n        currentSpans.add(\n          TextSpan(children: tmp, style: theme[node.className!]),\n        );\n        stack.add(currentSpans);\n        currentSpans = tmp;\n\n        for (var n in node.children!) {\n          _traverse(n);\n          if (n == node.children!.last) {\n            currentSpans = stack.isEmpty ? spans : stack.removeLast();\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n\n    for (var node in nodes) {\n      _traverse(node);\n    }\n\n    return spans;\n  }\n\n  static const _rootKey = 'root';\n  static const _defaultFontColor = Color(0xff000000);\n  static const _defaultBackgroundColor = Color(0xffffffff);\n  static const _defaultFontFamily = 'monospace';\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    var style = TextStyle(\n      fontFamily: _defaultFontFamily,\n      color: theme[_rootKey]?.color ?? _defaultFontColor,\n    );\n    if (textStyle != null) {\n      style = style.merge(textStyle);\n    }\n\n    return Container(\n      color: theme[_rootKey]?.backgroundColor ?? _defaultBackgroundColor,\n      padding: padding,\n      child: Text.rich(\n        TextSpan(\n          style: style,\n          children: _convert(\n            highlight.parse(source, language: language).nodes!,\n          ),\n        ),\n        softWrap: false,\n      ),\n    );\n  }\n}\n",
  "lib/widgets/christmas_countdown.dart": "import 'dart:async';\nimport 'dart:math' as math;\n\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/global/colors.dart';\nimport 'package:flutter/material.dart';\n\nclass ChristmasCountdown extends StatefulWidget {\n  final DateTime Function()? currentTimeProvider;\n\n  const ChristmasCountdown({\n    super.key,\n    this.currentTimeProvider,\n  });\n\n  @override\n  State<ChristmasCountdown> createState() => _ChristmasCountdownState();\n}\n\nclass _ChristmasCountdownState extends State<ChristmasCountdown> {\n  Timer? _timer;\n\n  @override\n  void initState() {\n    super.initState();\n    _timer = Timer.periodic(const Duration(seconds: 1), (_) {\n      if (mounted) {\n        setState(() {});\n      }\n    });\n  }\n\n  @override\n  void dispose() {\n    _timer?.cancel();\n    super.dispose();\n  }\n\n  DateTime _getTargetChristmas(DateTime now) {\n    if (now.month == 12 && now.day > 25) {\n      return DateTime(now.year + 1, 12, 25);\n    }\n    return DateTime(now.year, 12, 25);\n  }\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    final bool isDesktop = MediaQuery.sizeOf(context).width >= 768.0;\n    final now = widget.currentTimeProvider?.call() ?? DateTime.now();\n\n    final bool isChristmasDay = now.month == 12 && now.day == 25;\n    final targetChristmas = _getTargetChristmas(now);\n    final difference = targetChristmas.difference(now);\n\n    final int days = math.max(0, difference.inDays);\n    final int hours = math.max(0, difference.inHours % 24);\n    final int minutes = math.max(0, difference.inMinutes % 60);\n    final int seconds = math.max(0, difference.inSeconds % 60);\n\n    final double fontSize = isDesktop ? 11.0 : 9.5;\n\n    return FittedBox(\n      fit: BoxFit.scaleDown,\n      child: Padding(\n        padding: const EdgeInsets.symmetric(horizontal: 8.0, vertical: 2.0),\n        child: isChristmasDay\n            ? Text.rich(\n                TextSpan(\n                  style: TextStyle(\n                    fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                    fontSize: fontSize,\n                    letterSpacing: 1.0,\n                  ),\n                  children: [\n                    TextSpan(\n                      text: '* ',\n                      style: TextStyle(\n                        color: kHolidayGold.withValues(alpha: 0.85),\n                      ),\n                    ),\n                    const TextSpan(\n                      text: 'merry christmas!',\n                      style: TextStyle(\n                        color: Colors.white,\n                        fontWeight: FontWeight.bold,\n                      ),\n                    ),\n                    TextSpan(\n                      text: ' *',\n                      style: TextStyle(\n                        color: kHolidayGreen.withValues(alpha: 0.85),\n                      ),\n                    ),\n                  ],\n                ),\n              )\n            : Text.rich(\n                TextSpan(\n                  style: TextStyle(\n                    fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                    fontSize: fontSize,\n                    letterSpacing: 1.0,\n                  ),\n                  children: [\n                    TextSpan(\n                      text: '// ',\n                      style: TextStyle(\n                        color: kHolidayGreen.withValues(alpha: 0.85),\n                      ),\n                    ),\n                    TextSpan(\n                      text: 'christmas countdown: ',\n                      style: TextStyle(\n                        color: Colors.white.withValues(alpha: 0.45),\n                      ),\n                    ),\n                    TextSpan(\n                      text: '\${days}d ',\n                      style: const TextStyle(\n                        color: kHolidayRed,\n                        fontWeight: FontWeight.bold,\n                      ),\n                    ),\n                    TextSpan(\n                      text: '\${hours.toString().padLeft(2, '0')}h ',\n                      style: const TextStyle(\n                        color: kHolidayGreen,\n                        fontWeight: FontWeight.bold,\n                      ),\n                    ),\n                    TextSpan(\n                      text: '\${minutes.toString().padLeft(2, '0')}m ',\n                      style: const TextStyle(\n                        color: kHolidayGold,\n                        fontWeight: FontWeight.bold,\n                      ),\n                    ),\n                    TextSpan(\n                      text: '\${seconds.toString().padLeft(2, '0')}s',\n                      style: const TextStyle(\n                        color: kHolidayIce,\n                        fontWeight: FontWeight.bold,\n                      ),\n                    ),\n                  ],\n                ),\n              ),\n      ),\n    );\n  }\n}\n\n",
  "lib/widgets/header.dart": "import 'dart:async';\nimport 'dart:math' as math;\n\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/global/colors.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/widgets/nav_link.dart';\nimport 'package:flutter/material.dart';\n\nclass Header extends StatelessWidget {\n  final int currentIndex;\n  final Function(int) onItemTapped;\n\n  const Header({\n    super.key,\n    required this.currentIndex,\n    required this.onItemTapped,\n  });\n\n  static const double kTabletBreakpoint = 768.0;\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    return LayoutBuilder(\n      builder: (context, constraints) {\n        final bool isDesktop = constraints.maxWidth >= kTabletBreakpoint;\n\n        final double titleFontSize = isDesktop ? 22 : 18;\n        final double navLinkFontSize = isDesktop ? 16 : 14;\n\n        final EdgeInsets padding = isDesktop\n            ? const EdgeInsets.only(\n                left: 48.0,\n                right: 64.0,\n                top: 16.0,\n                bottom: 16.0,\n              )\n            : const EdgeInsets.only(\n                left: 16.0,\n                right: 28.0,\n                top: 16.0,\n                bottom: 16.0,\n              );\n\n        final headerContent = Row(\n          mainAxisAlignment: MainAxisAlignment.spaceBetween,\n          crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.center,\n          children: [\n            TextButton(\n              onPressed: () => onItemTapped(0),\n              style: TextButton.styleFrom(\n                splashFactory: NoSplash.splashFactory,\n                overlayColor: Colors.transparent,\n                padding: EdgeInsets.zero,\n                minimumSize: Size.zero,\n                tapTargetSize: MaterialTapTargetSize.shrinkWrap,\n                alignment: Alignment.centerLeft,\n              ),\n              child: Text.rich(\n                TextSpan(\n                  style: TextStyle(\n                    color: kTextColor,\n                    fontSize: titleFontSize,\n                    fontWeight: FontWeight.bold,\n                    letterSpacing: 1.5,\n                    fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n                  ),\n                  children: const [\n                    TextSpan(\n                      text: '// ',\n                      style: TextStyle(color: kHolidayGreen),\n                    ),\n                    TextSpan(text: 'archBTW'),\n                    TextSpan(\n                      text: '.',\n                      style: TextStyle(color: kHolidayRed),\n                    ),\n                  ],\n                ),\n              ),\n            ),\n            Padding(\n              padding: EdgeInsets.only(right: isDesktop ? 12.0 : 8.0),\n              child: Row(\n                mainAxisSize: MainAxisSize.min,\n                mainAxisAlignment: MainAxisAlignment.end,\n                children: [\n                  NavLink(\n                    title: 'whoami',\n                    index: 1,\n                    currentIndex: currentIndex,\n                    onTap: () => onItemTapped(1),\n                    fontSize: navLinkFontSize,\n                  ),\n                  NavLink(\n                    title: 'music',\n                    index: 2,\n                    currentIndex: currentIndex,\n                    onTap: () => onItemTapped(2),\n                    fontSize: navLinkFontSize,\n                  ),\n                  NavLink(\n                    title: 'merch',\n                    index: 3,\n                    currentIndex: currentIndex,\n                    onTap: () => onItemTapped(3),\n                    fontSize: navLinkFontSize,\n                  ),\n                ],\n              ),\n            ),\n          ],\n        );\n        return RepaintBoundary(\n          child: Container(\n            color: kBackgroundColor,\n            child: Column(\n              mainAxisSize: MainAxisSize.min,\n              children: [\n                Padding(padding: padding, child: headerContent),\n                const HolidayStringLights(),\n              ],\n            ),\n          ),\n        );\n      },\n    );\n  }\n}\n\nenum HolidayLightsMode {\n  solid('solid'),\n  twinkle('twinkle'),\n  chase('chase'),\n  pulse('pulse'),\n  off('off');\n\n  final String label;\n  const HolidayLightsMode(this.label);\n\n  HolidayLightsMode get next {\n    final nextIndex = (index + 1) % HolidayLightsMode.values.length;\n    return HolidayLightsMode.values[nextIndex];\n  }\n}\n\nclass HolidayStringLights extends StatefulWidget {\n  final HolidayLightsMode initialMode;\n\n  const HolidayStringLights({\n    super.key,\n    this.initialMode = HolidayLightsMode.solid,\n  });\n\n  @override\n  State<HolidayStringLights> createState() => HolidayStringLightsState();\n}\n\nclass HolidayStringLightsState extends State<HolidayStringLights> {\n  late HolidayLightsMode _mode;\n  final ValueNotifier<double> _phaseNotifier = ValueNotifier<double>(0.0);\n  Timer? _animationTimer;\n\n  HolidayLightsMode get currentMode => _mode;\n\n  @override\n  void initState() {\n    super.initState();\n    _mode = widget.initialMode;\n    _updateTimer();\n  }\n\n  void _updateTimer() {\n    _animationTimer?.cancel();\n    _animationTimer = null;\n    if (_mode == HolidayLightsMode.solid || _mode == HolidayLightsMode.off) {\n      _phaseNotifier.value = 0.0;\n      return;\n    }\n    // Update animation at ~12.5 FPS (80ms) for low overhead\n    _animationTimer = Timer.periodic(const Duration(milliseconds: 80), (_) {\n      _phaseNotifier.value = (_phaseNotifier.value + 0.16) % (math.pi * 2);\n    });\n  }\n\n  void cycleMode() {\n    setState(() {\n      _mode = _mode.next;\n      _updateTimer();\n    });\n  }\n\n  @override\n  void dispose() {\n    _animationTimer?.cancel();\n    _phaseNotifier.dispose();\n    super.dispose();\n  }\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    return RepaintBoundary(\n      child: MouseRegion(\n        cursor: SystemMouseCursors.click,\n        child: GestureDetector(\n          key: const Key('holiday_string_lights'),\n          behavior: HitTestBehavior.opaque,\n          onTap: cycleMode,\n          child: Tooltip(\n            message: 'Holiday lights: \${_mode.label} (tap to change)',\n            child: Padding(\n              padding: const EdgeInsets.symmetric(vertical: 4.0),\n              child: SizedBox(\n                height: 22,\n                width: double.infinity,\n                child: CustomPaint(\n                  painter: _StringLightsPainter(\n                    phaseListenable: _phaseNotifier,\n                    mode: _mode,\n                  ),\n                ),\n              ),\n            ),\n          ),\n        ),\n      ),\n    );\n  }\n}\n\nclass _StringLightsPainter extends CustomPainter {\n  final ValueNotifier<double> phaseListenable;\n  final HolidayLightsMode mode;\n\n  _StringLightsPainter({required this.phaseListenable, required this.mode})\n    : super(repaint: phaseListenable);\n\n  static const List<Color> _bulbColors = [\n    kHolidayRed,\n    kHolidayGreen,\n    kHolidayGold,\n    kAccentColor,\n    kHolidayIce,\n  ];\n\n  // Precomputed C7 teardrop bulb contour so zero Paths are allocated per bulb.\n  static final Path _bulbPath = _createBulbPath(5.6, 9.2);\n\n  static Path _createBulbPath(double width, double height) {\n    final double hw = width / 2;\n    return Path()\n      ..moveTo(-hw * 0.55, 0)\n      ..cubicTo(-hw * 1.25, height * 0.28, -hw * 0.95, height * 0.72, 0, height)\n      ..cubicTo(\n        hw * 0.95,\n        height * 0.72,\n        hw * 1.25,\n        height * 0.28,\n        hw * 0.55,\n        0,\n      )\n      ..close();\n  }\n\n  final Paint _wirePaint = Paint()\n    ..color = const Color(0xFF284232)\n    ..strokeWidth = 1.4\n    ..style = PaintingStyle.stroke;\n\n  final Paint _wireHighlightPaint = Paint()\n    ..color = Colors.white.withValues(alpha: 0.10)\n    ..strokeWidth = 0.6\n    ..style = PaintingStyle.stroke;\n\n  final Paint _socketPaint = Paint()\n    ..color = const Color(0xFF1F3828)\n    ..style = PaintingStyle.fill;\n\n  final Paint _socketCapPaint = Paint()\n    ..color = const Color(0xFF8A795D)\n    ..style = PaintingStyle.fill;\n\n  final Paint _fillPaint = Paint()..style = PaintingStyle.fill;\n\n  Path? _cachedWirePath;\n  double _cachedWidth = -1;\n\n  @override\n  void paint(Canvas canvas, Size size) {\n    if (size.width <= 0) return;\n\n    const double swagSpan = 88.0;\n    const double topY = 2.0;\n    const double sagControlY = 10.5;\n    final int swagCount = (size.width / swagSpan).ceil();\n\n    if (_cachedWirePath == null || _cachedWidth != size.width) {\n      _cachedWidth = size.width;\n      final Path wirePath = Path()..moveTo(0, topY);\n      for (int s = 0; s < swagCount; s++) {\n        final double x0 = s * swagSpan;\n        final double x1 = (s + 1) * swagSpan;\n        final double midX = (x0 + x1) / 2;\n        wirePath.quadraticBezierTo(midX, sagControlY, x1, topY);\n      }\n      _cachedWirePath = wirePath;\n    }\n\n    canvas.drawPath(_cachedWirePath!, _wirePaint);\n    canvas.drawPath(_cachedWirePath!, _wireHighlightPaint);\n\n    final double phase = phaseListenable.value;\n    int bulbIndex = 0;\n\n    for (int s = 0; s < swagCount; s++) {\n      final double x0 = s * swagSpan;\n      for (final double t in const [0.28, 0.72]) {\n        final double bx = x0 + swagSpan * t;\n        if (bx < 8 || bx > size.width - 8) {\n          bulbIndex++;\n          continue;\n        }\n\n        final double oneMinusT = 1.0 - t;\n        final double by =\n            oneMinusT * oneMinusT * topY +\n            2 * oneMinusT * t * sagControlY +\n            t * t * topY;\n\n        final double tiltAngle = bulbIndex.isEven ? -0.16 : 0.16;\n        final Color baseColor = _bulbColors[bulbIndex % _bulbColors.length];\n\n        final double twinkle;\n        switch (mode) {\n          case HolidayLightsMode.solid:\n            twinkle = 1.0;\n            break;\n          case HolidayLightsMode.twinkle:\n            twinkle =\n                0.50 + 0.50 * (0.5 + 0.5 * math.sin(phase + bulbIndex * 1.45));\n            break;\n          case HolidayLightsMode.chase:\n            final double wave =\n                0.5 + 0.5 * math.sin(phase * 2.2 - bulbIndex * 0.70);\n            twinkle = math.pow(wave, 2.2).toDouble();\n            break;\n          case HolidayLightsMode.pulse:\n            final double wave = 0.5 + 0.5 * math.sin(phase * 1.5);\n            twinkle = 0.20 + 0.80 * (wave * wave);\n            break;\n          case HolidayLightsMode.off:\n            twinkle = 0.0;\n            break;\n        }\n\n        canvas.save();\n        canvas.translate(bx, by);\n        canvas.rotate(tiltAngle);\n\n        // 1. Fast layered halo glow (no expensive GPU MaskFilter.blur needed)\n        if (twinkle > 0.05) {\n          _fillPaint.color = baseColor.withValues(alpha: 0.11 * twinkle);\n          canvas.drawOval(\n            const Rect.fromLTWH(-6.2, 0.2, 12.4, 14.5),\n            _fillPaint,\n          );\n          _fillPaint.color = baseColor.withValues(alpha: 0.18 * twinkle);\n          canvas.drawOval(\n            const Rect.fromLTWH(-4.2, 1.5, 8.4, 11.2),\n            _fillPaint,\n          );\n        }\n\n        // 2. Socket base (dark green plastic clip + brass collar)\n        canvas.drawRRect(\n          RRect.fromRectAndRadius(\n            const Rect.fromLTWH(-1.8, -0.6, 3.6, 2.4),\n            const Radius.circular(0.8),\n          ),\n          _socketPaint,\n        );\n        canvas.drawRect(\n          const Rect.fromLTWH(-1.5, 1.4, 3.0, 1.0),\n          _socketCapPaint,\n        );\n\n        // 3. C7 teardrop glass bulb body\n        canvas.translate(0, 2.2);\n        final double bulbAlpha = mode == HolidayLightsMode.off\n            ? 0.22\n            : (0.74 + 0.24 * twinkle);\n        _fillPaint.color = baseColor.withValues(alpha: bulbAlpha);\n        canvas.drawPath(_bulbPath, _fillPaint);\n\n        // 4. Warm inner filament core + specular glass highlight\n        if (twinkle > 0.05) {\n          _fillPaint.color = Colors.white.withValues(\n            alpha: 0.48 + 0.42 * twinkle,\n          );\n          canvas.drawOval(const Rect.fromLTWH(-1.1, 1.6, 2.2, 4.2), _fillPaint);\n        }\n\n        final double specAlpha = mode == HolidayLightsMode.off\n            ? 0.20\n            : (0.55 * twinkle);\n        _fillPaint.color = Colors.white.withValues(alpha: specAlpha);\n        canvas.drawOval(const Rect.fromLTWH(-1.4, 1.5, 1.0, 2.6), _fillPaint);\n\n        canvas.restore();\n        bulbIndex++;\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  @override\n  bool shouldRepaint(covariant _StringLightsPainter oldDelegate) =>\n      oldDelegate.mode != mode;\n}\n",
  "lib/widgets/holiday_snow_overlay.dart": "import 'dart:math' as math;\n\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/global/colors.dart';\nimport 'package:flutter/material.dart';\nimport 'package:flutter/scheduler.dart';\n\nclass HolidaySnowOverlay extends StatefulWidget {\n  final int flakeCount;\n\n  const HolidaySnowOverlay({\n    super.key,\n    this.flakeCount = 95,\n  });\n\n  @override\n  State<HolidaySnowOverlay> createState() => _HolidaySnowOverlayState();\n}\n\nclass _HolidaySnowOverlayState extends State<HolidaySnowOverlay>\n    with SingleTickerProviderStateMixin {\n  late final Ticker _ticker;\n  final ValueNotifier<int> _frameNotifier = ValueNotifier<int>(0);\n  late final List<_Snowflake> _flakes;\n  Duration _lastElapsed = Duration.zero;\n\n  @override\n  void initState() {\n    super.initState();\n    final rng = math.Random(42);\n    _flakes = List.generate(\n      widget.flakeCount,\n      (i) => _Snowflake.random(rng, index: i),\n    );\n    _ticker = createTicker(_onTick)..start();\n  }\n\n  void _onTick(Duration elapsed) {\n    final double dt = _lastElapsed == Duration.zero\n        ? 0.016\n        : ((elapsed - _lastElapsed).inMicroseconds / 1000000.0).clamp(\n            0.0,\n            0.05,\n          );\n    _lastElapsed = elapsed;\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < _flakes.length; i++) {\n      _flakes[i].update(dt);\n    }\n    _frameNotifier.value++;\n  }\n\n  @override\n  void dispose() {\n    _ticker.dispose();\n    _frameNotifier.dispose();\n    super.dispose();\n  }\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    return IgnorePointer(\n      child: RepaintBoundary(\n        child: CustomPaint(\n          painter: _SnowPainter(\n            flakes: _flakes,\n            repaint: _frameNotifier,\n          ),\n          size: Size.infinite,\n        ),\n      ),\n    );\n  }\n}\n\nenum _FlakeShape { circle, star, plus }\n\nclass _Snowflake {\n  double x; // Normalized 0..1\n  double y; // Normalized 0..1\n  final double radius;\n  final double speedY;\n  final double driftAmplitude;\n  final double driftFrequency;\n  double phase;\n  final _FlakeShape shape;\n  final Color precomputedColor;\n\n  _Snowflake({\n    required this.x,\n    required this.y,\n    required this.radius,\n    required this.speedY,\n    required this.driftAmplitude,\n    required this.driftFrequency,\n    required this.phase,\n    required this.shape,\n    required this.precomputedColor,\n  });\n\n  factory _Snowflake.random(math.Random rng, {required int index}) {\n    final _FlakeShape shape;\n    if (index % 8 == 0) {\n      shape = _FlakeShape.star;\n    } else if (index % 12 == 0) {\n      shape = _FlakeShape.plus;\n    } else {\n      shape = _FlakeShape.circle;\n    }\n\n    final Color tint;\n    if (index % 9 == 0) {\n      tint = kHolidayIce;\n    } else if (index % 17 == 0) {\n      tint = kHolidayGold;\n    } else if (index % 23 == 0) {\n      tint = kAccentColor;\n    } else {\n      tint = Colors.white;\n    }\n\n    final double opacity = 0.14 + rng.nextDouble() * 0.26;\n\n    return _Snowflake(\n      x: rng.nextDouble(),\n      y: rng.nextDouble(),\n      radius: 1.2 + rng.nextDouble() * 2.0,\n      speedY: 0.025 + rng.nextDouble() * 0.045,\n      driftAmplitude: 0.0003 + rng.nextDouble() * 0.0007,\n      driftFrequency: 0.7 + rng.nextDouble() * 1.6,\n      phase: rng.nextDouble() * math.pi * 2,\n      shape: shape,\n      precomputedColor: tint.withValues(alpha: opacity),\n    );\n  }\n\n  void update(double dt) {\n    phase += driftFrequency * dt;\n    y += speedY * dt;\n    x += math.sin(phase) * driftAmplitude;\n\n    if (y > 1.04) {\n      y = -0.04;\n      x = (x + 0.13) % 1.0;\n    }\n    if (x < -0.02) x += 1.04;\n    if (x > 1.02) x -= 1.04;\n  }\n}\n\nclass _SnowPainter extends CustomPainter {\n  final List<_Snowflake> flakes;\n  final Paint _fillPaint = Paint()..style = PaintingStyle.fill;\n  final Paint _strokePaint = Paint()\n    ..style = PaintingStyle.stroke\n    ..strokeWidth = 1.1\n    ..strokeCap = StrokeCap.round;\n\n  _SnowPainter({\n    required this.flakes,\n    required Listenable repaint,\n  }) : super(repaint: repaint);\n\n  @override\n  void paint(Canvas canvas, Size size) {\n    if (size.isEmpty) return;\n\n    // Scale active flake count on smaller mobile viewports so density stays even\n    // and low-end mobile GPUs do less work per frame.\n    final int activeCount = size.width < 600\n        ? (flakes.length * 0.62).round()\n        : flakes.length;\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < activeCount; i++) {\n      final flake = flakes[i];\n      final double dx = flake.x * size.width;\n      final double dy = flake.y * size.height;\n\n      switch (flake.shape) {\n        case _FlakeShape.circle:\n          _fillPaint.color = flake.precomputedColor;\n          canvas.drawCircle(Offset(dx, dy), flake.radius, _fillPaint);\n        case _FlakeShape.plus:\n          _strokePaint.color = flake.precomputedColor;\n          final double r = flake.radius * 1.7;\n          canvas.drawLine(Offset(dx - r, dy), Offset(dx + r, dy), _strokePaint);\n          canvas.drawLine(Offset(dx, dy - r), Offset(dx, dy + r), _strokePaint);\n        case _FlakeShape.star:\n          _strokePaint.color = flake.precomputedColor;\n          final double r = flake.radius * 1.85;\n          final double d = r * 0.7;\n          canvas.drawLine(Offset(dx - r, dy), Offset(dx + r, dy), _strokePaint);\n          canvas.drawLine(Offset(dx, dy - r), Offset(dx, dy + r), _strokePaint);\n          canvas.drawLine(\n            Offset(dx - d, dy - d),\n            Offset(dx + d, dy + d),\n            _strokePaint,\n          );\n          canvas.drawLine(\n            Offset(dx - d, dy + d),\n            Offset(dx + d, dy - d),\n            _strokePaint,\n          );\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  @override\n  bool shouldRepaint(covariant _SnowPainter oldDelegate) => false;\n}\n",
  "lib/widgets/nav_link.dart": "import 'package:archbtw_sh/global/colors.dart';\nimport 'package:flutter/material.dart';\n\nclass NavLink extends StatelessWidget {\n  final String title;\n  final int index;\n  final int currentIndex;\n  final VoidCallback onTap;\n  final double fontSize;\n\n  const NavLink({\n    super.key,\n    required this.title,\n    required this.index,\n    required this.currentIndex,\n    required this.onTap,\n    this.fontSize = 14.0,\n  });\n\n  Color get _holidayIndicatorColor {\n    switch (index) {\n      case 1:\n        return kHolidayGreen;\n      case 2:\n        return kHolidayRed;\n      case 3:\n        return kHolidayGold;\n      default:\n        return kAccentColor;\n    }\n  }\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    final bool isActive = index == currentIndex;\n\n    return TextButton(\n      onPressed: onTap,\n      style: TextButton.styleFrom(\n        splashFactory: NoSplash.splashFactory,\n        overlayColor: Colors.transparent,\n        foregroundColor: isActive ? kTextColor : Colors.grey,\n        textStyle: TextStyle(\n          fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n          fontSize: fontSize,\n          fontWeight: isActive ? FontWeight.bold : FontWeight.normal,\n        ),\n      ),\n      child: Column(\n        mainAxisSize: MainAxisSize.min,\n        children: [\n          Text(title),\n          const SizedBox(height: 2),\n          Container(\n            width: 14,\n            height: 2,\n            decoration: BoxDecoration(\n              color: isActive ? _holidayIndicatorColor : Colors.transparent,\n              borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(2),\n            ),\n          ),\n        ],\n      ),\n    );\n  }\n}\n",
  "lib/widgets/social_icons.dart": "import 'package:archbtw_sh/global/colors.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/global/helpers.dart';\nimport 'package:flutter/material.dart';\nimport 'package:font_awesome_flutter/font_awesome_flutter.dart';\n\nclass SocialIcon extends StatelessWidget {\n  final dynamic icon;\n  final String? url;\n  final double iconSize;\n  final VoidCallback? onPressed;\n  final String? tooltip;\n  final Color? color;\n  final Color? hoverColor;\n\n  const SocialIcon({\n    super.key,\n    required this.icon,\n    this.url,\n    this.iconSize = 18.0,\n    this.onPressed,\n    this.tooltip,\n    this.color,\n    this.hoverColor,\n  });\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    final effectiveHover = hoverColor ?? kAccentColor;\n    final Widget iconWidget = icon is FaIconData\n        ? FaIcon(\n            icon as FaIconData,\n            color: color ?? Colors.grey,\n            size: iconSize,\n          )\n        : Icon(icon as IconData, color: color ?? Colors.grey, size: iconSize);\n\n    return IconButton(\n      tooltip: tooltip,\n      icon: iconWidget,\n      onPressed:\n          onPressed ??\n          () {\n            if (url != null) openUrl(url!);\n          },\n      style: IconButton.styleFrom(\n        minimumSize: Size.zero,\n        padding: const EdgeInsets.all(6.0),\n        tapTargetSize: MaterialTapTargetSize.shrinkWrap,\n      ),\n      splashColor: effectiveHover.withValues(alpha: 0.3),\n      hoverColor: effectiveHover.withValues(alpha: 0.1),\n    );\n  }\n}\n",
  "lib/main.dart": "import 'dart:async';\n\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/games/super_archbtw.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/global/colors.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/pages/about/about.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/pages/error/kernel_panic_page.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/pages/home/home_page.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/pages/merch/merch__page.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/pages/music/album_item_list.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/pages/music/music_page.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/pages/overheat/overheat_page.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/widgets/floating_music_toast.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/widgets/header.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/widgets/holiday_snow_overlay.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/widgets/loading_waveform.dart';\nimport 'package:archbtw_sh/pages/source_code/source_code_page.dart';\nimport 'package:flutter/material.dart';\nimport 'package:flutter_web_plugins/url_strategy.dart'\n    if (dart.library.io) 'package:archbtw_sh/global/noop_url_strategy.dart';\n\nvoid main() {\n  usePathUrlStrategy();\n  runApp(const ArchWebsite());\n}\n\nclass ArchWebsite extends StatelessWidget {\n  const ArchWebsite({super.key});\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    return MaterialApp(\n      title: 'archBTW.',\n      debugShowCheckedModeBanner: false,\n      theme: ThemeData(\n        fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n        scaffoldBackgroundColor: kBackgroundColor,\n        textTheme: TextTheme(\n          bodyMedium: TextStyle(\n            color: kTextColor,\n            fontSize: 16,\n            fontFamily: 'JetBrainsMono',\n          ),\n        ),\n        useMaterial3: true,\n      ),\n      builder: (context, child) {\n        return Stack(\n          children: [if (child != null) child, const FloatingMusicToast()],\n        );\n      },\n      initialRoute: '/',\n      onGenerateRoute: (settings) {\n        if (settings.name == '/') {\n          return PageRouteBuilder(\n            pageBuilder: (context, animation, secondaryAnimation) =>\n                const MainScreen(),\n            transitionDuration: Duration.zero,\n            reverseTransitionDuration: Duration.zero,\n          );\n        } else if (settings.name == '/source') {\n          return PageRouteBuilder(\n            pageBuilder: (context, animation, secondaryAnimation) =>\n                const SourceCodePage(),\n            transitionDuration: Duration.zero,\n            reverseTransitionDuration: Duration.zero,\n          );\n        } else if (settings.name == '/overheat' ||\n            settings.name == '/third-degree') {\n          return PageRouteBuilder(\n            pageBuilder: (context, animation, secondaryAnimation) =>\n                const OverheatPage(),\n            transitionDuration: Duration.zero,\n            reverseTransitionDuration: Duration.zero,\n          );\n        } else if (settings.name == '/game' ||\n            settings.name == '/okc' ||\n            settings.name == '/super_archbtw') {\n          return PageRouteBuilder(\n            pageBuilder: (context, animation, secondaryAnimation) =>\n                const SuperArchBtw(),\n            transitionDuration: Duration.zero,\n            reverseTransitionDuration: Duration.zero,\n          );\n        }\n        return MaterialPageRoute(builder: (context) => const KernelPanicPage());\n      },\n    );\n  }\n}\n\nclass MainScreen extends StatefulWidget {\n  const MainScreen({super.key});\n\n  @override\n  State<MainScreen> createState() => _MainScreenState();\n}\n\nclass _MainScreenState extends State<MainScreen> {\n  int _currentIndex = 0;\n  bool _loadAbout = false;\n  bool _loadMusic = false;\n  bool _loadMerch = false;\n  bool _didPrecache = false;\n\n  Timer? _staggerTimer1;\n  Timer? _staggerTimer2;\n  Timer? _staggerTimer3;\n\n  final Widget _homePage = const RepaintBoundary(child: HomePage());\n  final Widget _aboutPage = const RepaintBoundary(child: AboutPage());\n  final Widget _musicPage = const RepaintBoundary(child: MusicPage());\n  final Widget _merchPage = const RepaintBoundary(child: MerchPage());\n  final Widget _snowOverlay = const Positioned.fill(\n    child: HolidaySnowOverlay(),\n  );\n\n  @override\n  void initState() {\n    super.initState();\n    _startStaggeredLoading();\n  }\n\n  @override\n  void didChangeDependencies() {\n    super.didChangeDependencies();\n    if (!_didPrecache) {\n      _didPrecache = true;\n      for (final item in albumItems) {\n        precacheImage(AssetImage(item.coverUrl), context);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  void _startStaggeredLoading() {\n    _staggerTimer1 = Timer(const Duration(milliseconds: 300), () {\n      if (mounted) setState(() => _loadAbout = true);\n    });\n    _staggerTimer2 = Timer(const Duration(milliseconds: 400), () {\n      if (mounted) setState(() => _loadMusic = true);\n    });\n    _staggerTimer3 = Timer(const Duration(milliseconds: 500), () {\n      if (mounted) setState(() => _loadMerch = true);\n    });\n  }\n\n  @override\n  void dispose() {\n    _staggerTimer1?.cancel();\n    _staggerTimer2?.cancel();\n    _staggerTimer3?.cancel();\n    super.dispose();\n  }\n\n  void _onItemTapped(int index) {\n    setState(() {\n      _currentIndex = index;\n      if (index == 1) {\n        _loadAbout = true;\n        _staggerTimer1?.cancel();\n      }\n      if (index == 2) {\n        _loadMusic = true;\n        _staggerTimer2?.cancel();\n      }\n      if (index == 3) {\n        _loadMerch = true;\n        _staggerTimer3?.cancel();\n      }\n    });\n  }\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    return Scaffold(\n      body: Stack(\n        children: [\n          Column(\n            children: [\n              Header(currentIndex: _currentIndex, onItemTapped: _onItemTapped),\n              Expanded(\n                child: RepaintBoundary(\n                  child: IndexedStack(\n                    index: _currentIndex,\n                    children: [\n                      _homePage,\n                      _loadAbout\n                          ? _aboutPage\n                          : const Center(child: WaveformLoader()),\n                      _loadMusic\n                          ? _musicPage\n                          : const Center(child: WaveformLoader()),\n                      _loadMerch\n                          ? _merchPage\n                          : const Center(child: WaveformLoader()),\n                    ],\n                  ),\n                ),\n              ),\n            ],\n          ),\n          _snowOverlay,\n        ],\n      ),\n    );\n  }\n}\n",
};
